time**: asyncio\\n- **WebSocket**: Starlette WebSocket support\\n- **State Management**: Redis for distributed caching\\n- **Metrics**: Prometheus + Grafana\\n\\n### State & Messaging\\n- **Event Bus**: RabbitMQ (reliable, scalable messaging)\\n- **State Persistence**: Redis + Local Filesystem Checkpoints\\n- **Metrics Database**: InfluxDB (time-series performance tracking)\\n\\n### Frontend (Optional Monitoring Dashboard)\\n- **Framework**: Vue.js 3\\n- **State Management**: Vuex\\n- **Real-Time Updates**: Socket.IO\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### A. Progress Streaming Service\\n```\\n{\\n    \\"responsibility\\": \\"Real-time agent execution tracking\\",\\n    \\"features\\": [\\n        \\"Granular event emission\\",\\n        \\"WebSocket broadcast\\",\\n        \\"Low-latency updates (<500ms)\\"\\n    ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### B. Error Recovery Manager\\n```\\n{\\n    \\"responsibility\\": \\"Automatic failure detection and resume\\",\\n    \\"features\\": [\\n        \\"Exponential backoff retry\\",\\n        \\"Context preservation\\",\\n        \\"Error classification\\",\\n        \\"Checkpoint validation\\"\\n    ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### C. Agent Analytics Engine\\n```\\n{\\n    \\"responsibility\\": \\"Performance tracking and optimization\\",\\n    \\"features\\": [\\n        \\"Metrics collection\\",\\n        \\"Model performance comparison\\",\\n        \\"Adaptive model selection\\",\\n        \\"Cost optimization tracking\\"\\n    ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 4. Data Flow Diagram\\n\\n```\\nAgent Execution Flow:\\n[User Request] \\u2192 [Progress Streaming Service]\\n             \\u2193\\n    [Error Recovery Manager] \\u2190 [Checkpoint Store]\\n             \\u2193\\n    [Agent Analytics Engine] \\u2192 [Metrics Database]\\n             \\u2193\\n    [Final Result Delivery]\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Containerization\\n- **Docker Compose** for local development\\n- **Kubernetes** for production scaling\\n- **Helm Charts** for consistent deployment\\n\\n### CI/CD\\n- **GitHub Actions** for testing\\n- **Automated Deployment** to staging/production\\n- **Blue-Green Deployment** for zero-downtime updates\\n\\n## 6. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Testing\\n- **pytest** for backend\\n- **Coverage Target**: 95%\\n- **Mocking**: Extensive use of `unittest.mock`\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n- **Docker Compose** test environments\\n- **Chaos Testing**: Simulate failure scenarios\\n- **Performance Benchmarks**\\n\\n## 7. Security Considerations\\n- JWT Authentication\\n- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)\\n- Encrypted WebSocket connections\\n- Rate limiting on all endpoints\\n\\n## 8. Performance Optimization\\n\\n### Caching Strategies\\n- **L1 Cache**: In-memory (per-service)\\n- **L2 Cache**: Distributed Redis\\n- **Intelligent Eviction Policies**\\n\\n### Performance Targets\\n- **Latency**: <100ms for most operations\\n- **Throughput**: 100 concurrent agent executions\\n- **Resource Efficiency**: < 10% overhead from new features\\n\\n## 9. Scalability Plan\\n- Stateless service design\\n- Horizontal scaling via Kubernetes\\n- Dynamic resource allocation\\n- Circuit breaker patterns\\n\\n## 10. Open Questions & User Input Needed\\n1. Preferred monitoring dashboard design\\n2. Acceptable performance overhead threshold\\n3. Specific error recovery granularity\\n\\n## 11. Risks & Mitigations\\n\\n### Primary Risks\\n- **Increased Complexity**: Mitigated by clear component boundaries\\n- **Performance Overhead**: Extensive benchmarking\\n- **Token Cost Increase**: Adaptive model selection\\n\\n## 12. Migration Path\\n- **Phase 1**: Progress Streaming (Low Risk)\\n- **Phase 2**: Error Recovery (Medium Risk)\\n- **Phase 3**: Analytics Engine (Highest Risk)\\n\\n## Implementation Complexity\\n- **Estimated Development Time**: 8-12 days\\n- **Team Size Recommendation**: 2 senior engineers"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01K41TW1cGPfh8b2qpeZBqb9', 'name': 'read_file', 'inp