{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:59:40", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-8427735f-b9d9-4a55-a66b-d3cc3a768223', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Milestone 1: CLI Provider Integration - Implement CLI provider adapter system that detects and uses locally installed Claude CLI and ChatGPT CLI tools as preferred API alternatives.",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ai_provider_enhancement_milestones.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01ETR6fHJ8tAAfzNKnk8X44j', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01ETR6fHJ8tAAfzNKnk8X44j', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Interval Selector Update Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\nThe interval selector will be updated to provide more production-appropriate refresh intervals while maintaining the existing UI component structure and reactivity.\\n\\n## 2. Tech Stack Impact\\n- **Frontend**: React component modification\\n- **No backend changes required**\\n- Existing WebSocket mechanism remains unchanged\\n\\n## 3. Component Changes\\n### 3.1 Interval Selector Component\\n```typescript\\ninterface IntervalOption {\\n  value: number;  // milliseconds\\n  label: string;  // User-friendly label\\n}\\n\\nconst INTERVAL_OPTIONS: IntervalOption[] = [\\n  { value: 1000, label: \'1 second\' },\\n  { value: 60000, label: \'1 minute\' },\\n  { value: 300000, label: \'5 minutes\' }\\n];\\n```\\n\\n### 3.2 State Management Update\\n- Replace current high-frequency options with production intervals\\n- Maintain same selection mechanism\\n- Default to most sensible interval (1 minute)\\n\\n## 4. UI/UX Considerations\\n- Clear, readable interval labels\\n- Sensible default selection\\n- Consistent with professional monitoring interfaces\\n\\n## 5. Implementation Strategy\\n1. Update React component\'s option list\\n2. Adjust default selection\\n3. Minimal testing required due to simple change\\n4. No backend modifications needed\\n\\n## 6. Risks and Mitigations\\n- **Risk**: User confusion with new intervals\\n- **Mitigation**: Clear labeling, tooltips explaining interval purpose\\n\\n## 7. Testing Approach\\n- Unit tests for interval selection\\n- Verify WebSocket update mechanism remains consistent\\n- UI regression testing\\n\\n## 8. Performance Implications\\n- Reduced update frequency will decrease unnecessary network load\\n- Lower computational overhead for real-time tracking\\n\\n## 9. Open Questions\\n- Confirm desired default interval\\n- Validate user preference for these specific intervals"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VEW2xAqfvxaxNxBfb8DFzS', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ai_provider_enhancement_milestones.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VEW2xAqfvxaxNxBfb8DFzS', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# AI Provider Enhancement System - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Project ID**: 3cd35d78\\n**Created**: 2026-01-13\\n**Status**: Planning\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 1: CLI Provider Integration\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: Highest\\n\\n### Objective\\nImplement CLI provider adapter system that detects and uses locally installed Claude CLI and ChatGPT CLI tools as preferred API alternatives.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `provider_manager.py` - AI provider abstraction and detection system\\n2. `cli_provider.py` - CLI provider implementations for Claude and ChatGPT\\n3. Updated `runtime.py` - Integration with provider manager\\n4. Unit tests for provider detection and execution\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Claude CLI at `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude` is detected automatically\\n- [ ] CLI provider executes prompts using `claude --print` flag\\n- [ ] Graceful fallback to Anthropic API when CLI unavailable\\n- [ ] Provider success/failure metrics tracked in database\\n- [ ] No increase in execution latency >10%\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Existing runtime.py infrastructure\\n- Claude CLI installed at `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 2: Cost Estimation Module\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n### Objective\\nImplement comprehensive pre-execution cost estimation and post-execution cost tracking with dashboard integration.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `cost_estimator.py` - Pre-execution cost estimation based on task complexity\\n2. Enhanced `cost_calculator.py` - Extended with estimation capabilities\\n3. Updated `metrics.py` - Cost tracking fields and aggregation queries\\n4. Cost API endpoints for dashboard\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Pre-execution cost estimates available before spawning agents\\n- [ ] Estimates within 50% of actual costs\\n- [ ] Cost aggregation by project, agent type, and time period\\n- [ ] Cost fields added to agent_executions table\\n- [ ] API endpoints expose cost data to dashboard\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 1 (provider tracking needed for CLI vs API cost differentiation)\\n- Existing cost_calculator.py\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 3: Smart Agent Router\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: Medium-High\\n\\n### Objective\\nImplement intelligent agent-task routing based on historical performance metrics.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `agent_router.py` - Performance analysis and routing recommendations\\n2. Updated agent execution flow to use router recommendations\\n3. Routing analytics API endpoints\\n4. Dashboard widget for routing explanations\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Agent recommendations based on historical performance from metrics.db\\n- [ ] Routing considers success rate (50%), cost efficiency (30%), speed (20%)\\n- [ ] Agent specialization bonuses applied (e.g., code_writer +10% for code tasks)\\n- [ ] Override capability for manual agent selection\\n- [ ] 10% improvement in overall success rate (measurable after deployment)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 2 (cost data needed for cost efficiency calculations)\\n- Populated metrics.db with historical data\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 4: Project Recovery & Dashboard Integration\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: Medium\\n\\n### Objective\\nRestart 10 stalled projects and integrate all new features into the dashboard.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `recovery_orchestrator.py` - Project recovery logic\\n2. Recovery execution report\\n3. Dashboard integration for provider, cost, and routing features\\n4. Updated frontend components\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] All 10 stalled projects attempted for restart\\n- [ ] Recovery report generated with outcomes per project\\n- [ ] Independent error boundaries (one failure doesn\'t stop others)\\n- [ ] Dashboard shows provider usage, cost trends, routing info\\n- [ ] Provider success rates visible in dashboard\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestones 1-3 completed\\n- Access to project tracking system\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone Summary\\n\\n| Milestone | Objective | Duration | Dependencies |\\n|-----------|-----------|----------|--------------|\\n| 1 | CLI Provider Integration | 2-3 days | None |\\n| 2 | Cost Estimation Module | 2-3 days | Milestone 1 |\\n| 3 | Smart Agent Router | 2-3 days | Milestone 2 |\\n| 4 | Project Recovery & Dashboard | 2-3 days | Milestones 1-3 |\\n\\n**Total Estimated Duration**: 8-12 days\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Technical Decisions Made\\n\\n### TD1: Provider Selection Strategy\\n- **Decision**: CLI preferred over API when available\\n- **Rationale**: CLI tools use user\'s existing subscription, avoiding API costs\\n\\n### TD2: Cost Estimation Approach\\n- **Decision**: Use task complexity heuristics for output token estimation\\n- **Rationale**: More accurate than fixed estimates, calibrated to task types\\n\\n### TD3: Routing Algorithm Weights\\n- **Decision**: 50% success rate, 30% cost efficiency, 20% speed\\n- **Rationale**: Reliability most important, then cost, then speed\\n\\n### TD4: Recovery Sequence\\n- **Decision**: Sequential processing, not parallel\\n- **Rationale**: Easier debugging, independent error boundaries, API rate limits\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Files to Create\\n- `src/runtime/agents/provider_manager.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/cli_provider.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/cost_estimator.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/agent_router.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/recovery_orchestrator.py`\\n\\n## Files to Modify\\n- `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/metrics.py`\\n- `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`\\n- `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/App.jsx`\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Document Status**: Complete\\n**Next Step**: System Architecture\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016uJ443YzsaRThjgVW7WfSZ', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Backend Tasks - Milestone 1: CLI Provider Integration\n\n## Overview\nImplement CLI provider adapter system that detects and uses locally installed Claude CLI and ChatGPT CLI tools as preferred API alternatives with graceful fallback to API providers.\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Phase 1: Foundation and Provider Abstraction\n\n#### Task 1.1: Create Provider Interface and Detection System\n**File**: `src/runtime/agents/provider_manager.py`\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Dependencies**: None\n\n**Description**: \nCreate abstract provider interface and detection system that can identify available CLI tools and manage provider fallback chains.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Abstract `AIProvider` base class with standard interface (`execute_prompt`, `get_capabilities`, `is_available`)\n- [ ] `ProviderManager` class that detects available providers on initialization\n- [ ] Detection logic for Claude CLI at `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude`\n- [ ] Detection logic for ChatGPT CLI (common installation paths)\n- [ ] Provider priority system (CLI preferred over API)\n- [ ] Health check mechanism for provider availability\n- [ ] Unit tests with 90%+ coverage\n\n#### Task 1.2: Implement Claude CLI Provider\n**File**: `src/runtime/agents/cli_provider.py`\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1\n\n**Description**:\nImplement Claude CLI provider that executes prompts using the `claude --print` flag with proper error handling and response parsing.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] `ClaudeCLIProvider` class implementing `AIProvider` interface\n- [ ] Command execution using `claude --print` with subprocess handling\n- [ ] Response parsing and formatting to match API response structure\n- [ ] Timeout handling (30 second default)\n- [ ] Error parsing and classification (CLI errors vs model errors)\n- [ ] Stdin prompt handling for long prompts\n- [ ] Unit tests with mocked subprocess calls\n- [ ] Integration test with actual CLI (when available)\n\n#### Task 1.3: Implement ChatGPT CLI Provider\n**File**: `src/runtime/agents/cli_provider.py` (extended)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.2\n\n**Description**:\nImplement ChatGPT CLI provider with similar capabilities to Claude CLI provider.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] `ChatGPTCLIProvider` class implementing `AIProvider` interface\n- [ ] Command execution with appropriate CLI flags\n- [ ] Response parsing and error handling\n- [ ] Timeout and subprocess management\n- [ ] Unit tests with mocked subprocess calls\n- [ ] Integration test with actual CLI (when available)\n\n### Phase 2: Provider Metrics and Tracking\n\n#### Task 2.1: Extend Metrics System for Provider Tracking\n**File**: `src/runtime/agents/metrics.py` (modified)\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1\n\n**Description**:\nExtend existing metrics system to track provider usage, success rates, and performance metrics.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Add `provider_type` field to agent execution tracking\n- [ ] Add `provider_success` boolean field\n- [ ] Add `provider_response_time` timing field\n- [ ] Provider usage aggregation queries\n- [ ] Provider success rate calculation methods\n- [ ] Database migration script for new fields\n- [ ] Unit tests for new metrics functions\n\n#### Task 2.2: Implement Provider Performance Tracking\n**File**: `src/runtime/agents/provider_manager.py` (extended)\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.1\n\n**Description**:\nAdd performance tracking and metrics collection to provider manager for monitoring provider health and usage patterns.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Response time tracking for each provider call\n- [ ] Success/failure rate tracking per provider\n- [ ] Provider fallback event logging\n- [ ] Periodic health checks for CLI availability\n- [ ] Metrics persistence to database\n- [ ] Unit tests for tracking functionality\n\n### Phase 3: Runtime Integration\n\n#### Task 3.1: Integrate Provider Manager with Runtime\n**File**: `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py` (modified)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Dependencies**: Tasks 1.1, 1.2, 1.3, 2.1\n\n**Description**:\nIntegrate the provider manager into the existing runtime system, replacing direct API calls with provider-managed calls.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Replace direct Anthropic API calls with provider manager\n- [ ] Maintain backward compatibility with existing agent interfaces\n- [ ] Provider fallback logic when CLI fails\n- [ ] Error propagation from providers to agents\n- [ ] No increase in execution latency >10%\n- [ ] Integration tests covering CLI + API fallback scenarios\n- [ ] Regression tests for existing functionality\n\n#### Task 3.2: Add Provider Configuration System\n**File**: `src/runtime/agents/config.py` (new) or environment variables\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Dependencies**: Task 3.1\n\n**Description**:\nAdd configuration system for provider preferences, CLI paths, and fallback behavior.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Environment variables for CLI tool paths\n- [ ] Provider preference configuration\n- [ ] Timeout configuration per provider type\n- [ ] Enable/disable flags for each provider\n- [ ] Configuration validation on startup\n- [ ] Documentation for configuration options\n\n### Phase 4: Testing and Validation\n\n#### Task 4.1: Comprehensive Provider Integration Tests\n**File**: `tests/integration/test_provider_integration.py` (new)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n**Dependencies**: Task 3.1, 3.2\n\n**Description**:\nCreate comprehensive integration tests that validate the entire provider system including fallback scenarios.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] End-to-end test with Claude CLI present\n- [ ] End-to-end test with CLI absent (API fallback)\n- [ ] Provider failure simulation tests\n- [ ] Performance benchmark tests\n- [ ] Concurrent execution tests\n- [ ] Error handling validation tests\n- [ ] Test coverage report >85%\n\n#### Task 4.2: Provider System Documentation\n**File**: `docs/provider_system.md` (new)\n**Complexity**: Simple\n**Dependencies**: All previous tasks\n\n**Description**:\nCreate comprehensive documentation for the provider system including setup, configuration, and troubleshooting.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Provider system architecture documentation\n- [ ] CLI installation and setup instructions\n- [ ] Configuration guide with examples\n- [ ] Troubleshooting guide for common issues\n- [ ] Provider performance tuning guide\n- [ ] API reference for provider interfaces\n\n## Task Dependencies\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[Task 1.1: Provider Interface] --> B[Task 1.2: Claude CLI]\n    A --> D[Task 2.1: Metrics Extension]\n    B --> C[Task 1.3: ChatGPT CLI]\n    D --> E[Task 2.2: Performance Tracking]\n    C --> F[Task 3.1: Runtime Integration]\n    E --> F\n    F --> G[Task 3.2: Configuration]\n    G --> H[Task 4.1: Integration Tests]\n    H --> I[Task 4.2: Documentation]\n```\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n**High Risk**:\n- CLI tool detection may fail on different system configurations\n- Subprocess handling could introduce security vulnerabilities\n\n**Medium Risk**:\n- Performance regression due to subprocess overhead\n- CLI tool version compatibility issues\n\n**Mitigation Strategies**:\n- Comprehensive error handling and fallback mechanisms\n- Sandboxed subprocess execution with proper timeout handling\n- Performance benchmarking during development\n- Version detection and compatibility checks\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n- [ ] Claude CLI detection success rate: 100% when CLI is installed\n- [ ] Provider fallback works in <1 second when CLI unavailable\n- [ ] No regression in existing agent execution success rates\n- [ ] Provider system adds <10% latency overhead\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met with >85% test coverage\n\n## Estimated Complexity: Medium\n**Total Tasks**: 8\n**Estimated Duration**: 2-3 days\n**Critical Path**: Tasks 1.1 → 1.2 → 1.3 → 3.1 → 4.1'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016uJ443YzsaRThjgVW7WfSZ', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260116_025940.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260116_025940.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Backend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks backend milestones into specific API, database, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify backend components, endpoints, data models, and business logic. Coordinates backend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break backend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Backend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**API Style**: REST with JSON, OpenAPI docs\n**Framework**: FastAPI (Python) or Express (Node.js)\n**Database**: PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy/Prisma ORM\n**Auth**: JWT tokens, bcrypt password hashing\n**Validation**: Pydantic (Python) or Joi (Node.js)\n**Testing**: pytest or Jest with coverage\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all backend components:\n  * API endpoints (REST, GraphQL)\n  * Database models/schemas\n  * Business logic services\n  * Authentication/authorization\n  * Background jobs/workers\n  * External API integrations\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (how to know it\'s done)\nDependencies (what must be done first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by Priority**\nGroup related tasks together\nOrder by dependencies (foundational → features)\nIdentify critical path tasks\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Backend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Business logic is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "calculate shipping" without formula)\n- **Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., sync vs async processing)\n- **Data relationships are contradictory** (e.g., conflicting schema requirements)\n- **Security/compliance requirements are ambiguous** (e.g., PII handling rules)\n- **NOT for**: standard tech choices, common patterns, typical implementations\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All backend tasks identified and documented\n- Task dependencies mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 98.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.8\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
