{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:59:41", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-18a13597-e16d-4d2a-a673-18586d442041', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/project-view/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Project View Dashboard",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01NrXrGDAATEsVVUboFtziGT', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/project-view/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01NrXrGDAATEsVVUboFtziGT', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Project View Dashboard Requirements\\n\\n## Overview\\nAdd a dedicated Project View to the Ensemble UI that provides comprehensive visibility into a project\'s status, SDLC position, milestone progress, and next steps with actionable controls.\\n\\n## User Vision\\n\\"Let\'s add a project view, so we can see a project view, its status, its position in the SDLC, the number of milestones determined, the number completed, and next steps along with a \'continue to next step\' button to force the agent system to move to implementation.\\"\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n### Primary Goals\\n1. **Project Status Visibility**: Display comprehensive project status at a glance\\n2. **SDLC Position Tracking**: Show where the project is in the Software Development Lifecycle\\n3. **Milestone Progress**: Display milestone counts (total, completed, remaining)\\n4. **Next Steps Visibility**: Show actionable next steps for the project\\n5. **Manual Control**: Provide \\"Continue to Next Step\\" button to force advancement\\n\\n### Success Criteria\\n- Users can view project status without navigating multiple screens\\n- SDLC phase is clearly visible (requirements \\u2192 architecture \\u2192 planning \\u2192 implementation \\u2192 testing \\u2192 complete)\\n- Milestone progress shows as numerical count and visual progress indicator\\n- Next steps are clearly listed with descriptions\\n- \\"Continue to Next Step\\" button triggers agent system to advance implementation\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### FR-1: Project Selection\\n- Display list of active projects (from `/api/projects/summary` or project tracker)\\n- Allow selection of a specific project to view details\\n- Show project name, created date, and current status in list\\n\\n### FR-2: Project Status Display\\n- Show overall project status: active, paused, completed, failed\\n- Display project name and description\\n- Show creation timestamp and last update timestamp\\n- Display associated request_id for tracing\\n\\n### FR-3: SDLC Position Indicator\\n- Visual indicator showing current phase:\\n  - Requirements\\n  - Architecture\\n  - Planning (task breakdown)\\n  - Implementation\\n  - Testing\\n  - Complete\\n- Phase should be determined from project tracking data or Executive Director output\\n\\n### FR-4: Milestone Tracking\\n- Display total number of milestones determined\\n- Show number of milestones completed\\n- Show number of milestones remaining/in-progress\\n- Visual progress bar (completed/total)\\n- List individual milestones with their status\\n\\n### FR-5: Task Summary\\n- Show task counts by status (todo, in_progress, completed, blocked)\\n- Completion percentage\\n- Link to detailed task view if available\\n\\n### FR-6: Next Steps Display\\n- List next actionable steps for the project\\n- Show which tasks can be started (no blocking dependencies)\\n- Display agent assignments for pending tasks\\n\\n### FR-7: Continue to Next Step Button\\n- Button to trigger continuation of project execution\\n- When clicked:\\n  - Spawn a new Executive Director with context to continue\\n  - Pass project_id and current state\\n  - Include instruction to proceed to next phase/milestone\\n- Visual feedback during execution (loading state)\\n- Error handling for failed continuations\\n\\n### FR-8: Agent Activity for Project\\n- Show currently running agents for this project\\n- Display recent agent activity\\n- Link to agent hierarchy for the project\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Backend Integration\\n\\n#### Existing Endpoints to Leverage\\n- `GET /api/projects/summary` - List projects with summary stats\\n- `GET /api/activity/hierarchy` - Agent hierarchy for project\\n- `GET /api/requests/{request_id}/timeline` - Timeline data\\n- `POST /api/generate-solution` - For continuation functionality\\n\\n#### New/Enhanced Endpoints Needed\\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/details` - Detailed project view with milestones\\n- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/continue` - Trigger project continuation\\n\\n### Data Sources\\n- Project Tracker (`~/.ensemble/projects/`) - SDLC state, milestones, notes\\n- Swarm State (SQLite) - Active agents, session data\\n- Activity Tracker - Recent activities\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n- New view tab \\"Projects\\" in App.jsx navigation\\n- ProjectView.jsx - Main component\\n- ProjectStatusCard.jsx - Project header with status\\n- SDLCIndicator.jsx - Visual SDLC phase indicator\\n- MilestoneProgress.jsx - Milestone tracking display\\n- NextStepsPanel.jsx - Actionable next steps\\n\\n## UI/UX Specifications\\n\\n### Visual Design\\n- Follow existing dark theme (backgroundColor: \'#1a1d29\')\\n- Card-based layout consistent with other views\\n- Use existing Badge component for status indicators\\n- Progress bars for milestone completion\\n\\n### Layout (Desktop)\\n```\\n+--------------------------------------------------+\\n| [Navigation: Activity | Timeline | ... | Projects] |\\n+--------------------------------------------------+\\n| Project List (Left)  |  Project Details (Right)   |\\n|                      |                            |\\n| [Project 1]         | Project Name                |\\n| [Project 2] <--     | Status: Active | Phase: X   |\\n| [Project 3]         |                            |\\n|                     | SDLC Progress              |\\n|                     | [=====>------] Architecture |\\n|                     |                            |\\n|                     | Milestones                 |\\n|                     | 3/7 Complete [=====>--]    |\\n|                     |                            |\\n|                     | Next Steps                 |\\n|                     | \\u2022 Task A (assigned: Dev)   |\\n|                     | \\u2022 Task B (unassigned)      |\\n|                     |                            |\\n|                     | [Continue to Next Step]    |\\n+--------------------------------------------------+\\n```\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Performance\\n- Project list should load in < 500ms\\n- Project details should load in < 1s\\n- Continue action should show immediate feedback\\n\\n### Reliability\\n- Handle missing/incomplete project data gracefully\\n- Show meaningful error states\\n- Recover from backend failures\\n\\n### Accessibility\\n- Keyboard navigation for project selection\\n- Screen reader compatible status indicators\\n- Clear visual contrast for all states\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Project deletion/archival (future feature)\\n- Milestone editing (manual intervention)\\n- Budget/cost per project (exists in Cost Tracking view)\\n- Multi-project comparison view\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Existing project_tracker.py module\\n- Backend main.py endpoints\\n- React Bootstrap UI framework\\n- Existing API service layer\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n1. Project data is available in ~/.ensemble/projects/ directory\\n2. Executive Director agents create and maintain project state\\n3. SDLC phase is tracked in project notes or result status\\n4. Backend has access to project tracker module\\n\\n## Risks\\n- SDLC phase may not be consistently tracked in current implementation\\n- Milestone data may be sparse for older projects\\n- \\"Continue\\" action may require careful context preservation\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Qb2XGXK5fG6gHaZMMY7MjJ', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Project View Dashboard - Architecture Proposal\n\n## A. Architecture Overview\n\n### Architectural Pattern: Modular Single Page Application (SPA)\n- Frontend: React-based component-driven architecture\n- Backend: Python Flask microservices\n- State Management: Redux for complex UI state\n- Communication: RESTful API with WebSocket support for real-time updates\n\n### Core Design Principles\n- Modularity: Each component has a single, well-defined responsibility\n- Scalability: Loosely coupled components that can be independently developed\n- Performance: Minimal payload, efficient data fetching\n- Extensibility: Easy to add new project tracking features\n\n## B. Tech Stack\n\n### Frontend\n- **Framework**: React 18\n- **State Management**: Redux Toolkit\n- **UI Components**: React Bootstrap\n- **Routing**: React Router\n- **HTTP Client**: Axios\n- **Testing**: Jest, React Testing Library\n\n### Backend\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\n- **Web Framework**: Flask\n- **API Design**: Flask-RESTful\n- **Authentication**: JWT (Flask-JWT-Extended)\n- **Database Access**: SQLAlchemy\n- **WebSocket**: Flask-SocketIO\n\n### Infrastructure\n- **Containerization**: Docker\n- **Orchestration**: Docker Compose\n- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions\n- **Deployment**: Kubernetes (optional scaling)\n\n## C. System Components\n\n### Frontend Components\n1. **ProjectViewContainer**\n   - Manages overall project view layout\n   - Handles project selection and data loading\n   - Renders child components\n\n2. **ProjectListPanel**\n   - Displays list of projects\n   - Handles project selection\n   - Filters and searches projects\n\n3. **ProjectStatusCard**\n   - Shows project metadata\n   - Displays status badges\n   - Shows timestamps\n\n4. **SDLCIndicator**\n   - Visualizes current SDLC phase\n   - Provides phase progression tracking\n\n5. **MilestoneTracker**\n   - Displays milestone progress\n   - Shows completion percentages\n   - Renders milestone details\n\n6. **NextStepsPanel**\n   - Lists actionable next steps\n   - Shows task assignments\n   - Provides "Continue" functionality\n\n### Backend Services\n1. **ProjectService**\n   - Retrieves project details\n   - Manages project lifecycle\n   - Handles project continuation requests\n\n2. **MilestoneService**\n   - Tracks milestone progress\n   - Calculates milestone statistics\n   - Updates milestone status\n\n3. **AgentActivityService**\n   - Retrieves agent activities\n   - Tracks running agents\n   - Provides agent hierarchy information\n\n## D. File/Directory Structure\n\n```\nensemble_ui/\n├── frontend/\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── components/\n│   │   │   ├── ProjectView/\n│   │   │   │   ├── ProjectListPanel.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── ProjectStatusCard.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── SDLCIndicator.jsx\n│   │   │   │   ├── MilestoneTracker.jsx\n│   │   │   │   └── NextStepsPanel.jsx\n│   │   │   └── common/\n│   │   ├── redux/\n│   │   │   ├── projectSlice.js\n│   │   │   └── milestoneSlice.js\n│   │   ├── services/\n│   │   │   └── apiService.js\n│   │   └── App.jsx\n│   └── package.json\n├── backend/\n│   ├── services/\n│   │   ├── project_service.py\n│   │   ├── milestone_service.py\n│   │   └── agent_activity_service.py\n│   ├── models/\n│   │   ├── project.py\n│   │   └── milestone.py\n│   ├── routes/\n│   │   └── project_routes.py\n│   └── app.py\n└── docker-compose.yml\n```\n\n## E. Data Model\n\n### Project Model\n```python\nclass Project:\n    id: str\n    name: str\n    description: str\n    status: ProjectStatus\n    sdlc_phase: SDLCPhase\n    created_at: datetime\n    updated_at: datetime\n    milestones: List[Milestone]\n    tasks: List[Task]\n```\n\n### Milestone Model\n```python\nclass Milestone:\n    id: str\n    name: str\n    status: MilestoneStatus\n    started_at: datetime\n    completed_at: datetime\n    tasks: List[Task]\n```\n\n## F. API Design\n\n### Project Endpoints\n- `GET /api/projects` - List projects\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}` - Get project details\n- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/continue` - Continue project\n\n### Response Examples\n```json\n{\n  "project_id": "proj_123",\n  "name": "AI Research Platform",\n  "status": "active",\n  "sdlc_phase": "architecture",\n  "milestones": [\n    {"name": "Design", "status": "completed"},\n    {"name": "Implementation", "status": "in_progress"}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## G. Deployment Strategy\n- Docker containers for frontend and backend\n- Nginx as reverse proxy\n- Optional Kubernetes for horizontal scaling\n- Environment-specific configuration management\n\n## H. Testing Strategy\n- Unit Tests: \n  - Frontend: Jest for React components\n  - Backend: pytest for Python services\n- Integration Tests: \n  - API endpoint testing\n  - Database interaction validation\n- E2E Tests: Cypress for critical user flows\n\n## I. Alternatives Considered\n1. **GraphQL vs REST**\n   - Chose REST for simplicity and existing infrastructure\n   - GraphQL would provide more flexible querying\n2. **Redux vs Context API**\n   - Redux chosen for complex state management\n   - Provides better debugging and middleware support\n\n## J. Risks and Mitigations\n- **Risk**: Inconsistent project tracking\n  - **Mitigation**: Robust data validation, default states\n- **Risk**: Performance with large projects\n  - **Mitigation**: Pagination, lazy loading, caching\n\n## K. Open Questions\n- Precise mechanism for "Continue to Next Step"\n- Handling edge cases in project progression\n- Long-term data retention strategy\n\n## Conclusion\nA modular, scalable architecture that meets the Project View Dashboard requirements while providing flexibility for future enhancements.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Qb2XGXK5fG6gHaZMMY7MjJ', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_025941.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_025941.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.5\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the requirements by providing a lightweight, flexible approach to adding new achievements. By focusing on modularity and compatibility, the design mini...\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the visibility requirements by proposing targeted, minimally invasive changes to the frontend and backend. The design maintains the existing system\'s c...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent