time**: asyncio\\n- **WebSocket**: Starlette WebSocket support\\n- **State Management**: Redis for distributed caching\\n- **Metrics**: Prometheus + Grafana\\n\\n### State & Messaging\\n- **Event Bus**: RabbitMQ (reliable, scalable messaging)\\n- **State Persistence**: Redis + Local Filesystem Checkpoints\\n- **Metrics Database**: InfluxDB (time-series performance tracking)\\n\\n### Frontend (Optional Monitoring Dashboard)\\n- **Framework**: Vue.js 3\\n- **State Management**: Vuex\\n- **Real-Time Updates**: Socket.IO\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### A. Progress Streaming Service\\n```\\n{\\n    \\"responsibility\\": \\"Real-time agent execution tracking\\",\\n    \\"features\\": [\\n        \\"Granular event emission\\",\\n        \\"WebSocket broadcast\\",\\n        \\"Low-latency updates (<500ms)\\"\\n    ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### B. Error Recovery Manager\\n```\\n{\\n    \\"responsibility\\": \\"Automatic failure detection and resume\\",\\n    \\"features\\": [\\n        \\"Exponential backoff retry\\",\\n        \\"Context preservation\\",\\n        \\"Error classification\\",\\n        \\"Checkpoint validation\\"\\n    ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### C. Agent Analytics Engine\\n```\\n{\\n    \\"responsibility\\": \\"Performance tracking and optimization\\",\\n    \\"features\\": [\\n        \\"Metrics collection\\",\\n        \\"Model performance comparison\\",\\n        \\"Adaptive model selection\\",\\n        \\"Cost optimization tracking\\"\\n    ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 4. Data Flow Diagram\\n\\n```\\nAgent Execution Flow:\\n[User Request] \\u2192 [Progress Streaming Service]\\n             \\u2193\\n    [Error Recovery Manager] \\u2190 [Checkpoint Store]\\n             \\u2193\\n    [Agent Analytics Engine] \\u2192 [Metrics Database]\\n             \\u2193\\n    [Final Result Delivery]\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Containerization\\n- **Docker Compose** for local development\\n- **Kubernetes** for production scaling\\n- **Helm Charts** for consistent deployment\\n\\n### CI/CD\\n- **GitHub Actions** for testing\\n- **Automated Deployment** to staging/production\\n- **Blue-Green Deployment** for zero-downtime updates\\n\\n## 6. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Testing\\n- **pytest** for backend\\n- **Coverage Target**: 95%\\n- **Mocking**: Extensive use of `unittest.mock`\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n- **Docker Compose** test environments\\n- **Chaos Testing**: Simulate failure scenarios\\n- **Performance Benchmarks**\\n\\n## 7. Security Considerations\\n- JWT Authentication\\n- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)\\n- Encrypted WebSocket connections\\n- Rate limiting on all endpoints\\n\\n## 8. Performance Optimization\\n\\n### Caching Strategies\\n- **L1 Cache**: In-memory (per-service)\\n- **L2 Cache**: Distributed Redis\\n- **Intelligent Eviction Policies**\\n\\n### Performance Targets\\n- **Latency**: <100ms for most operations\\n- **Throughput**: 100 concurrent agent executions\\n- **Resource Efficiency**: < 10% overhead from new features\\n\\n## 9. Scalability Plan\\n- Stateless service design\\n- Horizontal scaling via Kubernetes\\n- Dynamic resource allocation\\n- Circuit breaker patterns\\n\\n## 10. Open Questions & User Input Needed\\n1. Preferred monitoring dashboard design\\n2. Acceptable performance overhead threshold\\n3. Specific error recovery granularity\\n\\n## 11. Risks & Mitigations\\n\\n### Primary Risks\\n- **Increased Complexity**: Mitigated by clear component boundaries\\n- **Performance Overhead**: Extensive benchmarking\\n- **Token Cost Increase**: Adaptive model selection\\n\\n## 12. Migration Path\\n- **Phase 1**: Progress Streaming (Low Risk)\\n- **Phase 2**: Error Recovery (Medium Risk)\\n- **Phase 3**: Analytics Engine (Highest Risk)\\n\\n## Implementation Complexity\\n- **Estimated Development Time**: 8-12 days\\n- **Team Size Recommendation**: 2 senior engineers"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01K41TW1cGPfh8b2qpeZBqb9', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/smart_task_decomposition_milestones.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01K41TW1cGPfh8b2qpeZBqb9', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Smart Task Decomposition Engine - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nImplement a comprehensive Task Decomposition Engine for Ensemble AI that analyzes complex user requests, generates dependency graphs, estimates resources, and presents execution plans for user approval.\\n\\n## Milestones\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Core Infrastructure & Decomposition Engine\\n**Objective**: Build the core decomposition engine with task analysis and dependency graph generation.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `src/runtime/agents/decomposition_engine.py` - Core engine with:\\n   - Pydantic data models (TaskAnalysis, SubTask, DecompositionPlan, ResourceEstimate, AllocationPlan, Schedule)\\n   - `TaskDecompositionEngine` class with all core methods\\n   - NetworkX-based DAG generation and validation\\n   - Resource estimation and allocation optimization\\n   - Execution schedule generation\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Can analyze task complexity and domain\\n- Generates valid DAGs (no cycles)\\n- Produces resource estimates with cost calculations\\n- Creates parallel execution waves\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Learning Module\\n**Objective**: Build the learning module for continuous improvement of estimates.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `src/runtime/agents/decomposition_learner.py` - Learning module with:\\n   - `DecompositionLearner` class\\n   - Execution recording and history storage\\n   - Estimate improvement based on historical data\\n   - Accuracy metrics tracking\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Records execution outcomes\\n- Improves estimates over time\\n- Provides accuracy metrics\\n- Suggests improvements based on patterns\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (uses DecompositionPlan models)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Executive Director Integration\\n**Objective**: Integrate decomposition engine into Executive Director workflow.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Updated `leadership/executive_director.md` with:\\n   - New decomposition workflow\\n   - Extended output format with `decomposition_plan` field\\n   - User approval flow for plans\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Executive Director uses decomposition before spawning agents\\n- Output includes decomposition plan\\n- Supports plan approval workflow\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1, 2\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 4: API Endpoints\\n**Objective**: Add backend API endpoints for decomposition functionality.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Updated `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py` with:\\n   - `POST /api/decompose` - Decompose user request\\n   - `POST /api/approve-plan` - Accept/reject/modify plans\\n   - `GET /api/decomposition-history` - Historical accuracy\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All endpoints functional\\n- Proper error handling\\n- Integration with decomposition engine\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1, 2\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 5: Frontend Visualization\\n**Objective**: Build React component for task decomposition visualization.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/TaskDecompositionViewer.jsx` with:\\n   - Mermaid diagram rendering\\n   - Resource estimates display\\n   - Execution wave visualization\\n   - Agent assignment table\\n   - Approve/Reject/Modify buttons\\n   - Plan modification interface\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Renders dependency graph with Mermaid\\n- Displays resource estimates\\n- Action buttons work correctly\\n- Responsive UI\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 4 (needs API endpoints)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 6: Test Suite\\n**Objective**: Comprehensive testing for all decomposition functionality.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `tests/test_decomposition.py` with:\\n   - Unit tests for each method\\n   - Integration tests for full flow\\n   - Graph validity tests\\n   - Benchmark tests (simple, medium, complex)\\n   - Learning accuracy tests\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All unit tests pass\\n- Integration tests cover full workflow\\n- DAG validity verified\\n- Performance benchmarks documented\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1, 2, 4\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 7: Documentation\\n**Objective**: Complete documentation for the decomposition engine.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `TASK_DECOMPOSITION.md` with:\\n   - Architecture overview\\n   - Usage examples\\n   - API reference\\n   - Configuration options\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Clear architecture explanation\\n- Working code examples\\n- Complete API documentation\\n- Configuration fully documented\\n\\n**Dependencies**: All previous milestones\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Execution Order\\n1. Milestone 1 (Core Engine) - Foundation\\n2. Milestone 2 (Learning Module) - Builds on engine\\n3. Milestones 3, 4 (Integration + API) - Can run in parallel\\n4. Milestone 5 (Frontend) - Needs API\\n5. Milestone 6 (Tests) - Needs all code\\n6. Milestone 7 (Documentation) - Final\\n\\n## Estimated Timeline\\n- Milestones 1-2: Core implementation\\n- Milestones 3-5: Integration and UI\\n- Milestones 6-7: Quality and documentation\\n\\n## Risk Assessment\\n- **Medium Risk**: NetworkX/PuLP integration complexity\\n- **Low Risk**: Standard patterns for API/UI\\n- **Mitigation**: Use existing project patterns, fallback to simpler algorithms if needed\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015fnZ8YHjENQ5c2qYUzn8kQ', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Backend Tasks - Milestone 1: Core Infrastructure & Decomposition Engine\n\n## Task 1: Data Models Setup\n- **Name**: Implement Pydantic Data Models\n- **Description**: Create Pydantic models for task analysis and decomposition\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  * All models defined: TaskAnalysis, SubTask, DecompositionPlan, ResourceEstimate\n  * Proper type hints and validation\n  * JSON schema generation works\n- **Complexity**: Simple\n- **Dependencies**: None\n\n## Task 2: Decomposition Engine Core Logic \n- **Name**: Implement TaskDecompositionEngine Base Class\n- **Description**: Create core engine class with key decomposition methods\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  * `analyze_task` method functional\n  * Basic complexity scoring\n  * Domain categorization logic\n- **Complexity**: Medium\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1 (Data Models)\n\n## Task 3: DAG Generation with NetworkX\n- **Name**: Implement Dependency Graph Generation\n- **Description**: Use NetworkX to create directed acyclic graphs for task dependencies\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  * Create valid DAGs\n  * Cycle detection and prevention\n  * Topological sorting of tasks\n- **Complexity**: Complex\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 2\n\n## Task 4: Resource Estimation Module\n- **Name**: Build Resource Estimation Logic\n- **Description**: Implement resource cost and allocation estimation\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  * Calculate computational complexity\n  * Estimate token usage\n  * Basic cost projection\n  * Optimize for parallel execution\n- **Complexity**: Complex\n- **Dependencies**: Task 2, Task 3\n\n## Task 5: Execution Schedule Generator\n- **Name**: Create Execution Wave Planner\n- **Description**: Generate parallel execution schedules\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  * Create execution waves\n  * Respect task dependencies\n  * Optimize for concurrent processing\n- **Complexity**: Complex\n- **Dependencies**: Task 3, Task 4\n\n## Task 6: Logging and Observability\n- **Name**: Add Comprehensive Logging\n- **Description**: Implement logging for decomposition engine\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  * Log key events and decision points\n  * Structured logging format\n  * Configurable log levels\n- **Complexity**: Simple\n- **Dependencies**: Task 2\n\n## Task 7: Initial Configuration Management\n- **Name**: Configure Decomposition Parameters\n- **Description**: Set up configurable parameters for the engine\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\n  * Default configuration values\n  * Ability to override via environment/config\n  * Validate configuration options\n- **Complexity**: Simple\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 2\n\n## Implementation Strategy\n1. Implement tasks in numerical order\n2. Use TDD approach for each component\n3. Ensure high test coverage\n4. Validate against architecture guidelines\n\n## Performance Targets\n- Latency: < 100ms for small tasks\n- Memory usage: < 50MB per decomposition\n- Scalability: Support tasks up to 100 subtasks\n\n## Potential Challenges\n- Handling extremely complex task graphs\n- Accurate resource estimation\n- Avoiding over-decomposition\n\n## Recommended Approach\n- Start with simple decomposition logic\n- Incrementally add complexity\n- Use extensive unit and integration testing\n\n## Estimated Development Time\n- Total: 3-5 days\n- Per task: 0.5-1 day'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_015fnZ8YHjENQ5c2qYUzn8kQ', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260116_025940.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260116_025940.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Backend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks backend milestones into specific API, database, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify backend components, endpoints, data models, and business logic. Coordinates backend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break backend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Backend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**API Style**: REST with JSON, OpenAPI docs\n**Framework**: FastAPI (Python) or Express (Node.js)\n**Database**: PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy/Prisma ORM\n**Auth**: JWT tokens, bcrypt password hashing\n**Validation**: Pydantic (Python) or Joi (Node.js)\n**Testing**: pytest or Jest with coverage\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all backend components:\n  * API endpoints (REST, GraphQL)\n  * Database models/schemas\n  * Business logic services\n  * Authentication/authorization\n  * Background jobs/workers\n  * External API integrations\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (how to know it\'s done)\nDependencies (what must be done first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by Priority**\nGroup related tasks together\nOrder by dependencies (foundational → features)\nIdentify critical path tasks\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Backend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Business logic is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "calculate shipping" without formula)\n- **Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., sync vs async processing)\n- **Data relationships are contradictory** (e.g., conflicting schema requirements)\n- **Security/compliance requirements are ambiguous** (e.g., PII handling rules)\n- **NOT for**: standard tech choices, common patterns, typical implementations\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All backend tasks identified and documented\n- Task dependencies mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 98.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.8\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type'