{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:59:44", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-cd461a81-73de-4842-968e-e865130f7cd2', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/project-view/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Project View Dashboard",\n  "project_id": "a2d7d1ab",\n  "context": "Implement comprehensive Project View Dashboard with SDLC tracking"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FFiGGWnfBKwEDo8PzYsgfH', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/project-view/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FFiGGWnfBKwEDo8PzYsgfH', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Project View Dashboard Requirements\\n\\n## Overview\\nAdd a dedicated Project View to the Ensemble UI that provides comprehensive visibility into a project\'s status, SDLC position, milestone progress, and next steps with actionable controls.\\n\\n## User Vision\\n\\"Let\'s add a project view, so we can see a project view, its status, its position in the SDLC, the number of milestones determined, the number completed, and next steps along with a \'continue to next step\' button to force the agent system to move to implementation.\\"\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n### Primary Goals\\n1. **Project Status Visibility**: Display comprehensive project status at a glance\\n2. **SDLC Position Tracking**: Show where the project is in the Software Development Lifecycle\\n3. **Milestone Progress**: Display milestone counts (total, completed, remaining)\\n4. **Next Steps Visibility**: Show actionable next steps for the project\\n5. **Manual Control**: Provide \\"Continue to Next Step\\" button to force advancement\\n\\n### Success Criteria\\n- Users can view project status without navigating multiple screens\\n- SDLC phase is clearly visible (requirements \\u2192 architecture \\u2192 planning \\u2192 implementation \\u2192 testing \\u2192 complete)\\n- Milestone progress shows as numerical count and visual progress indicator\\n- Next steps are clearly listed with descriptions\\n- \\"Continue to Next Step\\" button triggers agent system to advance implementation\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### FR-1: Project Selection\\n- Display list of active projects (from `/api/projects/summary` or project tracker)\\n- Allow selection of a specific project to view details\\n- Show project name, created date, and current status in list\\n\\n### FR-2: Project Status Display\\n- Show overall project status: active, paused, completed, failed\\n- Display project name and description\\n- Show creation timestamp and last update timestamp\\n- Display associated request_id for tracing\\n\\n### FR-3: SDLC Position Indicator\\n- Visual indicator showing current phase:\\n  - Requirements\\n  - Architecture\\n  - Planning (task breakdown)\\n  - Implementation\\n  - Testing\\n  - Complete\\n- Phase should be determined from project tracking data or Executive Director output\\n\\n### FR-4: Milestone Tracking\\n- Display total number of milestones determined\\n- Show number of milestones completed\\n- Show number of milestones remaining/in-progress\\n- Visual progress bar (completed/total)\\n- List individual milestones with their status\\n\\n### FR-5: Task Summary\\n- Show task counts by status (todo, in_progress, completed, blocked)\\n- Completion percentage\\n- Link to detailed task view if available\\n\\n### FR-6: Next Steps Display\\n- List next actionable steps for the project\\n- Show which tasks can be started (no blocking dependencies)\\n- Display agent assignments for pending tasks\\n\\n### FR-7: Continue to Next Step Button\\n- Button to trigger continuation of project execution\\n- When clicked:\\n  - Spawn a new Executive Director with context to continue\\n  - Pass project_id and current state\\n  - Include instruction to proceed to next phase/milestone\\n- Visual feedback during execution (loading state)\\n- Error handling for failed continuations\\n\\n### FR-8: Agent Activity for Project\\n- Show currently running agents for this project\\n- Display recent agent activity\\n- Link to agent hierarchy for the project\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Backend Integration\\n\\n#### Existing Endpoints to Leverage\\n- `GET /api/projects/summary` - List projects with summary stats\\n- `GET /api/activity/hierarchy` - Agent hierarchy for project\\n- `GET /api/requests/{request_id}/timeline` - Timeline data\\n- `POST /api/generate-solution` - For continuation functionality\\n\\n#### New/Enhanced Endpoints Needed\\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/details` - Detailed project view with milestones\\n- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/continue` - Trigger project continuation\\n\\n### Data Sources\\n- Project Tracker (`~/.ensemble/projects/`) - SDLC state, milestones, notes\\n- Swarm State (SQLite) - Active agents, session data\\n- Activity Tracker - Recent activities\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n- New view tab \\"Projects\\" in App.jsx navigation\\n- ProjectView.jsx - Main component\\n- ProjectStatusCard.jsx - Project header with status\\n- SDLCIndicator.jsx - Visual SDLC phase indicator\\n- MilestoneProgress.jsx - Milestone tracking display\\n- NextStepsPanel.jsx - Actionable next steps\\n\\n## UI/UX Specifications\\n\\n### Visual Design\\n- Follow existing dark theme (backgroundColor: \'#1a1d29\')\\n- Card-based layout consistent with other views\\n- Use existing Badge component for status indicators\\n- Progress bars for milestone completion\\n\\n### Layout (Desktop)\\n```\\n+--------------------------------------------------+\\n| [Navigation: Activity | Timeline | ... | Projects] |\\n+--------------------------------------------------+\\n| Project List (Left)  |  Project Details (Right)   |\\n|                      |                            |\\n| [Project 1]         | Project Name                |\\n| [Project 2] <--     | Status: Active | Phase: X   |\\n| [Project 3]         |                            |\\n|                     | SDLC Progress              |\\n|                     | [=====>------] Architecture |\\n|                     |                            |\\n|                     | Milestones                 |\\n|                     | 3/7 Complete [=====>--]    |\\n|                     |                            |\\n|                     | Next Steps                 |\\n|                     | \\u2022 Task A (assigned: Dev)   |\\n|                     | \\u2022 Task B (unassigned)      |\\n|                     |                            |\\n|                     | [Continue to Next Step]    |\\n+--------------------------------------------------+\\n```\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Performance\\n- Project list should load in < 500ms\\n- Project details should load in < 1s\\n- Continue action should show immediate feedback\\n\\n### Reliability\\n- Handle missing/incomplete project data gracefully\\n- Show meaningful error states\\n- Recover from backend failures\\n\\n### Accessibility\\n- Keyboard navigation for project selection\\n- Screen reader compatible status indicators\\n- Clear visual contrast for all states\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Project deletion/archival (future feature)\\n- Milestone editing (manual intervention)\\n- Budget/cost per project (exists in Cost Tracking view)\\n- Multi-project comparison view\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Existing project_tracker.py module\\n- Backend main.py endpoints\\n- React Bootstrap UI framework\\n- Existing API service layer\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n1. Project data is available in ~/.ensemble/projects/ directory\\n2. Executive Director agents create and maintain project state\\n3. SDLC phase is tracked in project notes or result status\\n4. Backend has access to project tracker module\\n\\n## Risks\\n- SDLC phase may not be consistently tracked in current implementation\\n- Milestone data may be sparse for older projects\\n- \\"Continue\\" action may require careful context preservation\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RbPwnrZtnxy1YsFT8uobyD', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Project View Dashboard', 'description': 'Implement comprehensive Project View Dashboard with SDLC tracking, milestone progress, and continuation controls'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RbPwnrZtnxy1YsFT8uobyD', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "0cbb353b", "message": "Created project: Project View Dashboard", "summary": {"project_id": "0cbb353b", "project_name": "Project View Dashboard", "description": "Implement comprehensive Project View Dashboard with SDLC tracking, milestone progress, and continuation controls", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T02:58:39.567418", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T02:58:39.567418", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T02:58:39.567418", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Project View Dashboard\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01EKMzzLqida9SmYUSjoc93A', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Project View Dashboard - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\n**Project**: Project View Dashboard  \n**Goal**: Implement comprehensive Project View Dashboard with SDLC tracking, milestone progress, and continuation controls  \n**Total Estimated Duration**: 4-5 weeks\n\n## Milestone 1: Backend Foundation & API Development\n**Duration**: 1-2 weeks  \n**Objective**: Establish backend infrastructure and API endpoints for project data retrieval and management\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. Enhanced project tracker integration\n2. New API endpoints for project details and continuation\n3. SDLC phase tracking implementation\n4. Project data aggregation services\n\n### Key Features:\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/details` - Detailed project view with milestones\n- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/continue` - Trigger project continuation  \n- Enhanced project tracker to include SDLC phase tracking\n- Milestone and task aggregation from project tracker data\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- API endpoints return consistent project data structure\n- SDLC phase accurately determined from project state\n- Milestone counts and progress calculated correctly\n- Continue endpoint successfully spawns Executive Director with context\n- All endpoints have proper error handling\n\n### Dependencies:\n- Existing project_tracker.py module\n- Backend main.py structure\n- SQLite swarm state database\n\n## Milestone 2: Frontend Components Development\n**Duration**: 1-2 weeks  \n**Objective**: Create React components for the Project View Dashboard\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. Project selection and navigation components\n2. Project status and overview display\n3. SDLC phase indicator component\n4. Milestone progress visualization\n5. Next steps and task summary panels\n\n### Key Components:\n- `ProjectView.jsx` - Main container component\n- `ProjectStatusCard.jsx` - Project header with status\n- `SDLCIndicator.jsx` - Visual SDLC phase indicator\n- `MilestoneProgress.jsx` - Milestone tracking display\n- `NextStepsPanel.jsx` - Actionable next steps display\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- All components follow existing dark theme design\n- Responsive layout works on different screen sizes\n- Components handle loading and error states gracefully\n- Data refreshes automatically when project status changes\n- Visual indicators clearly show project progression\n\n### Dependencies:\n- Milestone 1 completion (backend APIs)\n- Existing React Bootstrap UI framework\n- API service layer integration\n\n## Milestone 3: Integration & User Interactions\n**Duration**: 1 week  \n**Objective**: Integrate frontend with backend and implement interactive features\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. Complete frontend-backend integration\n2. "Continue to Next Step" functionality\n3. Real-time status updates\n4. Error handling and user feedback\n\n### Key Features:\n- Project selection triggers API calls to load project details\n- Continue button spawns agents and shows progress feedback\n- Real-time updates of project status and agent activity\n- Comprehensive error handling with user-friendly messages\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- Users can select projects and view comprehensive details\n- Continue functionality successfully advances project execution\n- Loading states and progress indicators work correctly\n- Error messages are clear and actionable\n- Data updates in real-time without manual refresh\n\n### Dependencies:\n- Milestones 1 & 2 completion\n- Backend agent spawning infrastructure\n- WebSocket/polling for real-time updates\n\n## Milestone 4: Testing, Polish & Documentation\n**Duration**: 1 week  \n**Objective**: Comprehensive testing, performance optimization, and documentation\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. Unit tests for all React components\n2. Integration tests for API endpoints\n3. End-to-end user workflow testing\n4. Performance optimization\n5. User documentation and technical documentation\n\n### Key Activities:\n- React component testing with Jest/React Testing Library\n- Backend API testing with pytest\n- User acceptance testing for complete workflows\n- Performance testing and optimization\n- Documentation for users and developers\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- All tests pass with >90% code coverage\n- Performance targets met (load times, responsiveness)\n- User documentation complete and clear\n- Technical documentation updated\n- No critical bugs or usability issues\n\n### Dependencies:\n- All previous milestones completed\n- Testing framework setup\n- Documentation standards\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n\n### Technical Risks:\n1. **SDLC Phase Tracking Complexity**: May require analysis of existing project data structures\n   - Mitigation: Start with simple phase detection, enhance iteratively\n\n2. **Real-time Updates Performance**: Frequent polling may impact performance\n   - Mitigation: Implement efficient caching and selective updates\n\n3. **Agent Spawning Integration**: Complex integration with existing agent infrastructure\n   - Mitigation: Thorough testing in development environment first\n\n### Project Risks:\n1. **Scope Creep**: Additional features may be requested during development\n   - Mitigation: Clear acceptance criteria and change control process\n\n2. **Data Consistency**: Project data may be inconsistent across different sources\n   - Mitigation: Robust error handling and data validation\n\n## Success Metrics\n- Users can view complete project status in under 2 seconds\n- Continue functionality successfully advances 95% of eligible projects\n- Zero data loss during project transitions\n- User satisfaction score >4.5/5 for dashboard usability'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01EKMzzLqida9SmYUSjoc93A', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_025904.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_025904.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01QDS2jffCki9xpuFdWHWZt6', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/project-view/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'project_name': 'Project View Dashboard'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01QDS2jffCki9xpuFdWHWZt6', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01JN56Zgnpinnrq5S8oA8oXh', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/project-view/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'project_name': 'Project View Dashboard', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01JN56Zgnpinnrq5S8oA8oXh', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": null}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 81.5%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.3\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively executed the complete planning and implementation workflow for Milestone 1. Successfully coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all three Coordinators for com...\n- Successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Effectively managed the sequential process: milestone planning, architec...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'des