{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:59:45", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-4e23c3ce-a5ea-4f8e-8f55-10081af31b8e', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Locate and Update UI Components - Update interval selector from high-frequency options (500ms, 1s, 2s) to production intervals (1s, 1m, 5m)",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01SPnTjSZxGhCft5xobmfjwf', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01SPnTjSZxGhCft5xobmfjwf', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Project View Dashboard - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## A. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Architectural Pattern: Modular Single Page Application (SPA)\\n- Frontend: React-based component-driven architecture\\n- Backend: Python Flask microservices\\n- State Management: Redux for complex UI state\\n- Communication: RESTful API with WebSocket support for real-time updates\\n\\n### Core Design Principles\\n- Modularity: Each component has a single, well-defined responsibility\\n- Scalability: Loosely coupled components that can be independently developed\\n- Performance: Minimal payload, efficient data fetching\\n- Extensibility: Easy to add new project tracking features\\n\\n## B. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **Framework**: React 18\\n- **State Management**: Redux Toolkit\\n- **UI Components**: React Bootstrap\\n- **Routing**: React Router\\n- **HTTP Client**: Axios\\n- **Testing**: Jest, React Testing Library\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\\n- **Web Framework**: Flask\\n- **API Design**: Flask-RESTful\\n- **Authentication**: JWT (Flask-JWT-Extended)\\n- **Database Access**: SQLAlchemy\\n- **WebSocket**: Flask-SocketIO\\n\\n### Infrastructure\\n- **Containerization**: Docker\\n- **Orchestration**: Docker Compose\\n- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions\\n- **Deployment**: Kubernetes (optional scaling)\\n\\n## C. System Components\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n1. **ProjectViewContainer**\\n   - Manages overall project view layout\\n   - Handles project selection and data loading\\n   - Renders child components\\n\\n2. **ProjectListPanel**\\n   - Displays list of projects\\n   - Handles project selection\\n   - Filters and searches projects\\n\\n3. **ProjectStatusCard**\\n   - Shows project metadata\\n   - Displays status badges\\n   - Shows timestamps\\n\\n4. **SDLCIndicator**\\n   - Visualizes current SDLC phase\\n   - Provides phase progression tracking\\n\\n5. **MilestoneTracker**\\n   - Displays milestone progress\\n   - Shows completion percentages\\n   - Renders milestone details\\n\\n6. **NextStepsPanel**\\n   - Lists actionable next steps\\n   - Shows task assignments\\n   - Provides \\"Continue\\" functionality\\n\\n### Backend Services\\n1. **ProjectService**\\n   - Retrieves project details\\n   - Manages project lifecycle\\n   - Handles project continuation requests\\n\\n2. **MilestoneService**\\n   - Tracks milestone progress\\n   - Calculates milestone statistics\\n   - Updates milestone status\\n\\n3. **AgentActivityService**\\n   - Retrieves agent activities\\n   - Tracks running agents\\n   - Provides agent hierarchy information\\n\\n## D. File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nensemble_ui/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ProjectView/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ProjectListPanel.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ProjectStatusCard.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 SDLCIndicator.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 MilestoneTracker.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 NextStepsPanel.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 common/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 redux/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 projectSlice.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 milestoneSlice.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 apiService.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 App.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 package.json\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 backend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 project_service.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 milestone_service.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 agent_activity_service.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 models/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 project.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 milestone.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 routes/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 project_routes.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 app.py\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 docker-compose.yml\\n```\\n\\n## E. Data Model\\n\\n### Project Model\\n```python\\nclass Project:\\n    id: str\\n    name: str\\n    description: str\\n    status: ProjectStatus\\n    sdlc_phase: SDLCPhase\\n    created_at: datetime\\n    updated_at: datetime\\n    milestones: List[Milestone]\\n    tasks: List[Task]\\n```\\n\\n### Milestone Model\\n```python\\nclass Milestone:\\n    id: str\\n    name: str\\n    status: MilestoneStatus\\n    started_at: datetime\\n    completed_at: datetime\\n    tasks: List[Task]\\n```\\n\\n## F. API Design\\n\\n### Project Endpoints\\n- `GET /api/projects` - List projects\\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}` - Get project details\\n- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/continue` - Continue project\\n\\n### Response Examples\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"project_id\\": \\"proj_123\\",\\n  \\"name\\": \\"AI Research Platform\\",\\n  \\"status\\": \\"active\\",\\n  \\"sdlc_phase\\": \\"architecture\\",\\n  \\"milestones\\": [\\n    {\\"name\\": \\"Design\\", \\"status\\": \\"completed\\"},\\n    {\\"name\\": \\"Implementation\\", \\"status\\": \\"in_progress\\"}\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## G. Deployment Strategy\\n- Docker containers for frontend and backend\\n- Nginx as reverse proxy\\n- Optional Kubernetes for horizontal scaling\\n- Environment-specific configuration management\\n\\n## H. Testing Strategy\\n- Unit Tests: \\n  - Frontend: Jest for React components\\n  - Backend: pytest for Python services\\n- Integration Tests: \\n  - API endpoint testing\\n  - Database interaction validation\\n- E2E Tests: Cypress for critical user flows\\n\\n## I. Alternatives Considered\\n1. **GraphQL vs REST**\\n   - Chose REST for simplicity and existing infrastructure\\n   - GraphQL would provide more flexible querying\\n2. **Redux vs Context API**\\n   - Redux chosen for complex state management\\n   - Provides better debugging and middleware support\\n\\n## J. Risks and Mitigations\\n- **Risk**: Inconsistent project tracking\\n  - **Mitigation**: Robust data validation, default states\\n- **Risk**: Performance with large projects\\n  - **Mitigation**: Pagination, lazy loading, caching\\n\\n## K. Open Questions\\n- Precise mechanism for \\"Continue to Next Step\\"\\n- Handling edge cases in project progression\\n- Long-term data retention strategy\\n\\n## Conclusion\\nA modular, scalable architecture that meets the Project View Dashboard requirements while providing flexibility for future enhancements."}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Frontend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks frontend milestones into specific component, page, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify UI components, user flows, state management, and API integration needs. Coordinates frontend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break frontend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable UI/UX assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Frontend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**Framework**: React with hooks or Vue 3 with Composition API\n**Styling**: Tailwind CSS or CSS Modules\n**State**: Context API (simple) or Redux/Vuex (complex)\n**API Client**: fetch or axios with error handling\n**Forms**: Controlled components with validation\n**Routing**: React Router or Vue Router\n**Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all frontend components:\n  * Pages/Routes\n  * UI components (forms, buttons, cards, modals)\n  * Services (API client, WebSocket, auth)\n  * State management (Context, Redux, stores)\n  * Utilities (formatting, validation)\n  * Styling (CSS, Tailwind classes)\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (user can do X, component shows Y)\nDependencies (what must exist first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by User Flow**\nGroup by user journey or feature\nOrder by dependencies (layout → components → pages)\nIdentify reusable components\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Frontend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **User flow is genuinely ambiguous** (e.g., "manage users" without specifying CRUD operations)\n- **Multiple valid UX approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., modal vs full-page form)\n- **Design requirements are contradictory** (e.g., "simple but feature-rich")\n- **Accessibility requirements unclear** (e.g., WCAG level needed)\n- **NOT for**: standard UI patterns, common component structures, typical interactions\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All frontend tasks identified and documented\n- Component hierarchy mapped\n- Task breakdown fil