{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 03:00:10", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-8b6a4298-0df8-4612-848b-12d1a80ad767', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/project-view/milestone_plan.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "project_name": "Project View Dashboard"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_014DccdVoTDwzXfoJ4PjJaiF', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/project-view/milestone_plan.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_014DccdVoTDwzXfoJ4PjJaiF', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Project View Dashboard - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Project Name**: Project View Dashboard\\n**Description**: Add a dedicated Project View to the Ensemble UI that displays project status, SDLC position, milestone progress, next steps, and includes a \\"Continue to Next Step\\" button to advance implementation.\\n\\n## Milestones\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Backend API Enhancement\\n**Objective**: Create and enhance backend endpoints to support project view functionality\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Enhanced `/api/projects/{project_id}/details` endpoint for detailed project view\\n2. New `/api/projects/{project_id}/continue` endpoint to trigger project continuation\\n3. SDLC phase determination logic from project notes/status\\n4. Integration with existing project_tracker.py module\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- GET `/api/projects/{project_id}/details` returns complete project state including SDLC phase, milestones, tasks\\n- POST `/api/projects/{project_id}/continue` triggers a new Executive Director with appropriate context\\n- API handles missing/incomplete project data gracefully\\n- Endpoints respond within specified performance thresholds (<500ms for list, <1s for details)\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None (uses existing project_tracker.py)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Frontend Project View Components\\n**Objective**: Build React components for the Project View dashboard\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. ProjectView.jsx - Main container component with project list and details pane\\n2. ProjectStatusCard.jsx - Project header showing name, status, timestamps\\n3. SDLCIndicator.jsx - Visual SDLC phase progress indicator\\n4. MilestoneProgress.jsx - Milestone tracking with progress bar\\n5. NextStepsPanel.jsx - Actionable next steps display\\n6. Integration with App.jsx navigation (new \\"Projects\\" tab)\\n7. API service integration (api.js updates)\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Project list displays all projects with status badges\\n- Selected project shows detailed view with all required information\\n- SDLC indicator clearly shows current phase\\n- Milestone progress displays numerical counts and visual progress bar\\n- \\"Continue to Next Step\\" button triggers backend continuation endpoint\\n- UI follows existing dark theme and Bootstrap patterns\\n- Loading and error states handled appropriately\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (backend endpoints must be available)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Testing and Polish\\n**Objective**: Comprehensive testing and UI refinement\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Backend unit tests for new endpoints\\n2. Frontend component tests (Jest/React Testing Library)\\n3. Integration testing for continue functionality\\n4. Error handling refinement\\n5. Loading state animations\\n6. Documentation\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All new backend endpoints have unit test coverage\\n- Frontend components render correctly in tests\\n- Continue functionality works end-to-end\\n- Error states display user-friendly messages\\n- Documentation updated for new endpoints\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1 and 2\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Technical Decisions Made\\n\\n### Architecture Decisions\\n1. **SDLC Phase Tracking**: Will infer SDLC phase from project notes by scanning for phase-related keywords (requirements, architecture, planning, implementation, testing). This is pragmatic given current data.\\n\\n2. **Milestone Data Source**: Will use project tracker tasks and notes to infer milestones. Tasks tagged as milestones or notes with category \\"milestone\\" will be used.\\n\\n3. **Continue Functionality**: Will spawn a new Executive Director agent with the project context, instructing it to continue to the next phase/milestone.\\n\\n4. **Component Structure**: Single ProjectView.jsx as main container with sub-components for modularity, following existing patterns like SelfImprovementDashboard.\\n\\n### Technical Stack (Following Existing Patterns)\\n- Backend: FastAPI (Python) with existing project_tracker integration\\n- Frontend: React with Bootstrap components\\n- State: Local React state (following App.jsx pattern)\\n- Styling: Inline styles with existing dark theme colors\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n1. **SDLC Phase Detection**: If project notes don\'t contain phase information, default to \\"unknown\\" with graceful UI handling\\n2. **Milestone Data**: If no milestone data exists, show \\"No milestones defined\\" rather than empty state\\n3. **Continue Action**: Include confirmation dialog and proper error handling for failed continuation attempts\\n\\n## Estimated Scope\\n- **Milestone 1**: ~200-300 lines backend code\\n- **Milestone 2**: ~500-700 lines frontend code (5 components + api changes)\\n- **Milestone 3**: ~200-300 lines test code + documentation\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01S7ueGkW1HcCH9o6bT9NhCu', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Project View Dashboard - Architecture Proposal\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n**Architectural Pattern**: Modular Single-Page Application (SPA) with Backend-Driven Views\n**Core Goal**: Create a flexible, maintainable project tracking dashboard that provides comprehensive project insights and actionable next steps.\n\n## 2. Tech Stack\n\n### Backend\n- **Language**: Python\n- **Framework**: FastAPI\n  - Rationale: Lightweight, high-performance, built-in OpenAPI support\n  - Alternatives Considered: Flask (less opinionated), Django (too heavyweight)\n\n### Frontend\n- **Framework**: React\n  - Rationale: Component-based architecture, existing codebase uses React\n- **Styling**: Bootstrap + Custom Dark Theme\n- **State Management**: Local React State (for simplicity)\n  - Alternatives: Redux (over-engineered for current scope), Context API (potential future upgrade)\n\n### Persistence\n- **Existing Project Tracking**: Leverage `project_tracker.py`\n- **Data Source**: Project notes and tasks as primary data store\n\n## 3. System Components\n\n### Backend Components\n1. **ProjectDetailsEndpoint**\n   - Responsibility: Retrieve comprehensive project information\n   - Input: `project_id`\n   - Output: Project state, SDLC phase, milestones, tasks\n\n2. **ProjectContinuationEndpoint**\n   - Responsibility: Trigger next phase of project\n   - Mechanism: Spawn Executive Director with project context\n   - Handles: Phase transition, context preservation\n\n### Frontend Components\n1. **ProjectView.jsx** (Main Container)\n   - Manages overall layout and page state\n   - Fetches and displays project list\n   - Renders detailed project view\n\n2. **ProjectStatusCard.jsx**\n   - Displays high-level project metadata\n   - Shows status, timestamps, basic info\n\n3. **SDLCIndicator.jsx**\n   - Visualizes current SDLC phase\n   - Supports multiple phase representations\n\n4. **MilestoneProgress.jsx**\n   - Tracks and displays milestone completion\n   - Provides visual and numerical progress\n\n5. **NextStepsPanel.jsx**\n   - Displays actionable project continuation steps\n   - Manages "Continue" button interaction\n\n## 4. File/Directory Structure\n```\nsrc/\n├── backend/\n│   ├── api/\n│   │   ├── project_details.py\n│   │   └── project_continuation.py\n│   └── services/\n│       └── sdlc_tracker.py\n├── frontend/\n│   ├── components/\n│   │   ├── ProjectView.jsx\n│   │   ├── ProjectStatusCard.jsx\n│   │   ├── SDLCIndicator.jsx\n│   │   ├── MilestoneProgress.jsx\n│   │   └── NextStepsPanel.jsx\n│   └── services/\n│       └── api.js\n```\n\n## 5. Data Flow\n1. User navigates to Projects view\n2. Frontend requests `/api/projects` to fetch project list\n3. User selects a project\n4. Frontend calls `/api/projects/{project_id}/details`\n5. Backend retrieves project info from project_tracker\n6. Frontend renders detailed project view\n7. User clicks "Continue"\n8. Frontend calls `/api/projects/{project_id}/continue`\n9. Backend spawns Executive Director\n10. UI updates to reflect new project state\n\n## 6. API Design\n### Endpoints\n- `GET /api/projects` - List all projects\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/details` - Get project details\n- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/continue` - Advance project\n\n### Response Format\n```json\n{\n  "project_id": "string",\n  "name": "string",\n  "current_phase": "string",\n  "milestones": [\n    {\n      "name": "string",\n      "status": "completed|in_progress|pending",\n      "progress": 0.75\n    }\n  ],\n  "next_steps": ["string"]\n}\n```\n\n## 7. Deployment Strategy\n- Containerized with Docker\n- Deployed alongside existing Ensemble UI\n- Uses existing authentication mechanisms\n\n## 8. Testing Strategy\n### Backend\n- Unit tests for SDLC phase detection\n- Integration tests for API endpoints\n- Error handling and edge case coverage\n\n### Frontend\n- Component rendering tests (Jest)\n- Interaction tests (React Testing Library)\n- API service mocking\n- State management tests\n\n## 9. Risks and Mitigations\n1. **Incomplete Project Data**\n   - Mitigation: Graceful UI handling, default states\n2. **SDLC Phase Detection Accuracy**\n   - Mitigation: Flexible keyword-based detection, manual override capability\n3. **Performance with Large Project Sets**\n   - Mitigation: Implement pagination, lazy loading\n\n## 10. Open Questions\n- How granular should milestone tracking be?\n- Preferences for SDLC phase visual representation?\n- Desired level of "Continue" action customization?\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n1. Microservices Architecture: Rejected due to unnecessary complexity\n2. Redux for State Management: Premature optimization\n3. Static Phase Definitions: Chose flexible, inference-based approach\n\n**Recommended Next Steps**:\n1. Review architecture proposal\n2. Validate technical approach\n3. Confirm design meets business requirements\n4. Proceed with implementation'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01S7ueGkW1HcCH9o6bT9NhCu', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_030010.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_030010.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.1%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.5\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the requirements by providing a lightweight, flexible approach to UI enhancements. The modular design allows for easy implementation of new features wi...\n- The architecture proposal effectively addresses the 404 error issue by providing a targeted, low-risk solution that preserves the existing system architecture. By analyzing root causes and proposing m...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the