{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 03:00:15", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-62ca39d9-4cd5-475a-8bdf-c135451ba10d', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Core Infrastructure & Decomposition Engine",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/smart_task_decomposition_milestones.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01M5evXtMd2vyf5WxZ7CyCP3', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01M5evXtMd2vyf5WxZ7CyCP3', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Project View Dashboard - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n**Architectural Pattern**: Modular Single-Page Application (SPA) with Backend-Driven Views\\n**Core Goal**: Create a flexible, maintainable project tracking dashboard that provides comprehensive project insights and actionable next steps.\\n\\n## 2. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Language**: Python\\n- **Framework**: FastAPI\\n  - Rationale: Lightweight, high-performance, built-in OpenAPI support\\n  - Alternatives Considered: Flask (less opinionated), Django (too heavyweight)\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **Framework**: React\\n  - Rationale: Component-based architecture, existing codebase uses React\\n- **Styling**: Bootstrap + Custom Dark Theme\\n- **State Management**: Local React State (for simplicity)\\n  - Alternatives: Redux (over-engineered for current scope), Context API (potential future upgrade)\\n\\n### Persistence\\n- **Existing Project Tracking**: Leverage `project_tracker.py`\\n- **Data Source**: Project notes and tasks as primary data store\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### Backend Components\\n1. **ProjectDetailsEndpoint**\\n   - Responsibility: Retrieve comprehensive project information\\n   - Input: `project_id`\\n   - Output: Project state, SDLC phase, milestones, tasks\\n\\n2. **ProjectContinuationEndpoint**\\n   - Responsibility: Trigger next phase of project\\n   - Mechanism: Spawn Executive Director with project context\\n   - Handles: Phase transition, context preservation\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n1. **ProjectView.jsx** (Main Container)\\n   - Manages overall layout and page state\\n   - Fetches and displays project list\\n   - Renders detailed project view\\n\\n2. **ProjectStatusCard.jsx**\\n   - Displays high-level project metadata\\n   - Shows status, timestamps, basic info\\n\\n3. **SDLCIndicator.jsx**\\n   - Visualizes current SDLC phase\\n   - Supports multiple phase representations\\n\\n4. **MilestoneProgress.jsx**\\n   - Tracks and displays milestone completion\\n   - Provides visual and numerical progress\\n\\n5. **NextStepsPanel.jsx**\\n   - Displays actionable project continuation steps\\n   - Manages \\"Continue\\" button interaction\\n\\n## 4. File/Directory Structure\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 backend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 api/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 project_details.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 project_continuation.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 sdlc_tracker.py\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ProjectView.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ProjectStatusCard.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 SDLCIndicator.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 MilestoneProgress.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 NextStepsPanel.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 api.js\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Data Flow\\n1. User navigates to Projects view\\n2. Frontend requests `/api/projects` to fetch project list\\n3. User selects a project\\n4. Frontend calls `/api/projects/{project_id}/details`\\n5. Backend retrieves project info from project_tracker\\n6. Frontend renders detailed project view\\n7. User clicks \\"Continue\\"\\n8. Frontend calls `/api/projects/{project_id}/continue`\\n9. Backend spawns Executive Director\\n10. UI updates to reflect new project state\\n\\n## 6. API Design\\n### Endpoints\\n- `GET /api/projects` - List all projects\\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/details` - Get project details\\n- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/continue` - Advance project\\n\\n### Response Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"project_id\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"name\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"current_phase\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"milestones\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"name\\": \\"string\\",\\n      \\"status\\": \\"completed|in_progress|pending\\",\\n      \\"progress\\": 0.75\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\"next_steps\\": [\\"string\\"]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 7. Deployment Strategy\\n- Containerized with Docker\\n- Deployed alongside existing Ensemble UI\\n- Uses existing authentication mechanisms\\n\\n## 8. Testing Strategy\\n### Backend\\n- Unit tests for SDLC phase detection\\n- Integration tests for API endpoints\\n- Error handling and edge case coverage\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- Component rendering tests (Jest)\\n- Interaction tests (React Testing Library)\\n- API service mocking\\n- State management tests\\n\\n## 9. Risks and Mitigations\\n1. **Incomplete Project Data**\\n   - Mitigation: Graceful UI handling, default states\\n2. **SDLC Phase Detection Accuracy**\\n   - Mitigation: Flexible keyword-based detection, manual override capability\\n3. **Performance with Large Project Sets**\\n   - Mitigation: Implement pagination, lazy loading\\n\\n## 10. Open Questions\\n- How granular should milestone tracking be?\\n- Preferences for SDLC phase visual representation?\\n- Desired level of \\"Continue\\" action customization?\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n1. Microservices Architecture: Rejected due to unnecessary complexity\\n2. Redux for State Management: Premature optimization\\n3. Static Phase Definitions: Chose flexible, inference-based approach\\n\\n**Recommended Next Steps**:\\n1. Review architecture proposal\\n2. Validate technical approach\\n3. Confirm design meets business requirements\\n4. Proceed with implementation"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016v24e2cx4YX85UggCZAf5T', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/smart_task_decomposition_milestones.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016v24e2cx4YX85UggCZAf5T', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Smart Task Decomposition Engine - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nImplement a comprehensive Task Decomposition Engine for Ensemble AI that analyzes complex user requests, generates dependency graphs, estimates resources, and presents execution plans for user approval.\\n\\n## Milestones\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Core Infrastructure & Decomposition Engine\\n**Objective**: Build the core decomposition engine with task analysis and dependency graph generation.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `src/runtime/agents/decomposition_engine.py` - Core engine with:\\n   - Pydantic data models (TaskAnalysis, SubTask, DecompositionPlan, ResourceEstimate, AllocationPlan, Schedule)\\n   - `TaskDecompositionEngine` class with all core methods\\n   - NetworkX-based DAG generation and validation\\n   - Resource estimation and allocation optimization\\n   - Execution schedule generation\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Can analyze task complexity and domain\\n- Generates valid DAGs (no cycles)\\n- Produces resource estimates with cost calculations\\n- Creates parallel execution waves\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Learning Module\\n**Objective**: Build the learning module for continuous improvement of estimates.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `src/runtime/agents/decomposition_learner.py` - Learning module with:\\n   - `DecompositionLearner` class\\n   - Execution recording and history storage\\n   - Estimate improvement based on historical data\\n   - Accuracy metrics tracking\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Records execution outcomes\\n- Improves estimates over time\\n- Provides accuracy metrics\\n- Suggests improvements based on patterns\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (uses DecompositionPlan models)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Executive Director Integration\\n**Objective**: Integrate decomposition engine into Executive Director workflow.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Updated `leadership/executive_director.md` with:\\n   - New decomposition workflow\\n   - Extended output format with `decomposition_plan` field\\n   - User approval flow for plans\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Executive Director uses decomposition before spawning agents\\n- Output includes decomposition plan\\n- Supports plan approval workflow\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1, 2\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 4: API Endpoints\\n**Objective**: Add backend API endpoints for decomposition functionality.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Updated `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py` with:\\n   - `POST /api/decompose` - Decompose user request\\n   - `POST /api/approve-plan` - Accept/reject/modify plans\\n   - `GET /api/decomposition-history` - Historical accuracy\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All endpoints functional\\n- Proper error handling\\n- Integration with decomposition engine\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1, 2\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 5: Frontend Visualization\\n**Objective**: Build React component for task decomposition visualization.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/TaskDecompositionViewer.jsx` with:\\n   - Mermaid diagram rendering\\n   - Resource estimates display\\n   - Execution wave visualization\\n   - Agent assignment table\\n   - Approve/Reject/Modify buttons\\n   - Plan modification interface\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Renders dependency graph with Mermaid\\n- Displays resource estimates\\n- Action buttons work correctly\\n- Responsive UI\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 4 (needs API endpoints)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 6: Test Suite\\n**Objective**: Comprehensive testing for all decomposition functionality.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `tests/test_decomposition.py` with:\\n   - Unit tests for each method\\n   - Integration tests for full flow\\n   - Graph validity tests\\n   - Benchmark tests (simple, medium, complex)\\n   - Learning accuracy tests\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All unit tests pass\\n- Integration tests cover full workflow\\n- DAG validity verified\\n- Performance benchmarks documented\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1, 2, 4\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 7: Documentation\\n**Objective**: Complete documentation for the decomposition engine.\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. `TASK_DECOMPOSITION.md` with:\\n   - Architecture overview\\n   - Usage examples\\n   - API reference\\n   - Configuration options\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Clear architecture explanation\\n- Working code examples\\n- Complete API documentation\\n- Configuration fully documented\\n\\n**Dependencies**: All previous milestones\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Execution Order\\n1. Milestone 1 (Core Engine) - Foundation\\n2. Milestone 2 (Learning Module) - Builds on engine\\n3. Milestones 3, 4 (Integration + API) - Can run in parallel\\n4. Milestone 5 (Frontend) - Needs API\\n5. Milestone 6 (Tests) - Needs all code\\n6. Milestone 7 (Documentation) - Final\\n\\n## Estimated Timeline\\n- Milestones 1-2: Core implementation\\n- Milestones 3-5: Integration and UI\\n- Milestones 6-7: Quality and documentation\\n\\n## Risk Assessment\\n- **Medium Risk**: NetworkX/PuLP integration complexity\\n- **Low Risk**: Standard patterns for API/UI\\n- **Mitigation**: Use existing project patterns, fallback to simpler algorithms if needed\\n"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Frontend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks frontend milestones into specific component, page, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify UI components, user flows, state management, and API integration needs. Coordinates frontend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break frontend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable UI/UX assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Frontend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**Framework**: React with hooks or Vue 3 with Composition API\n**Styling**: Tailwind CSS or CSS Modules\n**State**: Context API (simple) or Redux/Vuex (complex)\n**API Client**: fetch or axios with error handling\n**Forms**: Controlled components with validation\n**Routing**: React Router or Vue Router\n**Testing**: