{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 03:00:18", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-e8c7de22-c186-43f5-9a17-a01d888e4e57', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Implement CLI Provider Integration and Cost Estimation Foundation",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ai_provider_enhancement_requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01K8EP8vqecQSx9wVdm1wNCd', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01K8EP8vqecQSx9wVdm1wNCd', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Project View Dashboard - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n**Architectural Pattern**: Modular Single-Page Application (SPA) with Backend-Driven Views\\n**Core Goal**: Create a flexible, maintainable project tracking dashboard that provides comprehensive project insights and actionable next steps.\\n\\n## 2. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Language**: Python\\n- **Framework**: FastAPI\\n  - Rationale: Lightweight, high-performance, built-in OpenAPI support\\n  - Alternatives Considered: Flask (less opinionated), Django (too heavyweight)\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **Framework**: React\\n  - Rationale: Component-based architecture, existing codebase uses React\\n- **Styling**: Bootstrap + Custom Dark Theme\\n- **State Management**: Local React State (for simplicity)\\n  - Alternatives: Redux (over-engineered for current scope), Context API (potential future upgrade)\\n\\n### Persistence\\n- **Existing Project Tracking**: Leverage `project_tracker.py`\\n- **Data Source**: Project notes and tasks as primary data store\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### Backend Components\\n1. **ProjectDetailsEndpoint**\\n   - Responsibility: Retrieve comprehensive project information\\n   - Input: `project_id`\\n   - Output: Project state, SDLC phase, milestones, tasks\\n\\n2. **ProjectContinuationEndpoint**\\n   - Responsibility: Trigger next phase of project\\n   - Mechanism: Spawn Executive Director with project context\\n   - Handles: Phase transition, context preservation\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n1. **ProjectView.jsx** (Main Container)\\n   - Manages overall layout and page state\\n   - Fetches and displays project list\\n   - Renders detailed project view\\n\\n2. **ProjectStatusCard.jsx**\\n   - Displays high-level project metadata\\n   - Shows status, timestamps, basic info\\n\\n3. **SDLCIndicator.jsx**\\n   - Visualizes current SDLC phase\\n   - Supports multiple phase representations\\n\\n4. **MilestoneProgress.jsx**\\n   - Tracks and displays milestone completion\\n   - Provides visual and numerical progress\\n\\n5. **NextStepsPanel.jsx**\\n   - Displays actionable project continuation steps\\n   - Manages \\"Continue\\" button interaction\\n\\n## 4. File/Directory Structure\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 backend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 api/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 project_details.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 project_continuation.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 sdlc_tracker.py\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ProjectView.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ProjectStatusCard.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 SDLCIndicator.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 MilestoneProgress.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 NextStepsPanel.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 api.js\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Data Flow\\n1. User navigates to Projects view\\n2. Frontend requests `/api/projects` to fetch project list\\n3. User selects a project\\n4. Frontend calls `/api/projects/{project_id}/details`\\n5. Backend retrieves project info from project_tracker\\n6. Frontend renders detailed project view\\n7. User clicks \\"Continue\\"\\n8. Frontend calls `/api/projects/{project_id}/continue`\\n9. Backend spawns Executive Director\\n10. UI updates to reflect new project state\\n\\n## 6. API Design\\n### Endpoints\\n- `GET /api/projects` - List all projects\\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/details` - Get project details\\n- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/continue` - Advance project\\n\\n### Response Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"project_id\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"name\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"current_phase\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"milestones\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"name\\": \\"string\\",\\n      \\"status\\": \\"completed|in_progress|pending\\",\\n      \\"progress\\": 0.75\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\"next_steps\\": [\\"string\\"]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 7. Deployment Strategy\\n- Containerized with Docker\\n- Deployed alongside existing Ensemble UI\\n- Uses existing authentication mechanisms\\n\\n## 8. Testing Strategy\\n### Backend\\n- Unit tests for SDLC phase detection\\n- Integration tests for API endpoints\\n- Error handling and edge case coverage\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- Component rendering tests (Jest)\\n- Interaction tests (React Testing Library)\\n- API service mocking\\n- State management tests\\n\\n## 9. Risks and Mitigations\\n1. **Incomplete Project Data**\\n   - Mitigation: Graceful UI handling, default states\\n2. **SDLC Phase Detection Accuracy**\\n   - Mitigation: Flexible keyword-based detection, manual override capability\\n3. **Performance with Large Project Sets**\\n   - Mitigation: Implement pagination, lazy loading\\n\\n## 10. Open Questions\\n- How granular should milestone tracking be?\\n- Preferences for SDLC phase visual representation?\\n- Desired level of \\"Continue\\" action customization?\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n1. Microservices Architecture: Rejected due to unnecessary complexity\\n2. Redux for State Management: Premature optimization\\n3. Static Phase Definitions: Chose flexible, inference-based approach\\n\\n**Recommended Next Steps**:\\n1. Review architecture proposal\\n2. Validate technical approach\\n3. Confirm design meets business requirements\\n4. Proceed with implementation"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Backend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks backend milestones into specific API, database, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify backend components, endpoints, data models, and business logic. Coordinates backend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break backend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Backend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**API Style**: REST with JSON, OpenAPI docs\n**Framework**: FastAPI (Python) or Express (Node.js)\n**Database**: PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy/Prisma ORM\n**Auth**: JWT tokens, bcrypt password hashing\n**Validation**: Pydantic (Python) or Joi (Node.js)\n**Testing**: pytest or Jest with coverage\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all backend components:\n  * API endpoints (REST, GraphQL)\n  * Database models/schemas\n  * Business logic services\n  * Authentication/authorization\n  * Background jobs/workers\n  * External API integrations\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (how to know it\'s done)\nDependencies (what must be done first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by Priority**\nGroup related tasks together\nOrder by dependencies (foundational → features)\nIdentify critical path tasks\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Backend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Business logic is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "calculate shipping" without formula)\n- **Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., sync vs async processing)\n- **Data relationships are contradictory** (e.g., conflicting schema requirements)\n- **Security/compliance requirements are ambiguous** (e.g., PII handling rules)\n- **NOT for**: standard tech choices, common patterns, typical implementations\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All backend tasks identified and documented\n- Task dependencies mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 96.3%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.7\n- Common errors to avoid: RateLimitError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: RateLimitError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
