0\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502                  TaskDecompositionEngine                         \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  decomposition_engine.py                                         \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502                                                                   \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  Methods:                                                         \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  - analyze_task() \\u2192 TaskAnalysis                                  \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  - decompose_task() \\u2192 DecompositionPlan                          \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  - generate_dependency_graph() \\u2192 nx.DiGraph                      \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  - estimate_resources() \\u2192 ResourceEstimate                        \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  - optimize_allocation() \\u2192 AllocationPlan                         \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  - generate_execution_schedule() \\u2192 Schedule                       \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518    \\u2502\\n\\u2502                                    \\u2502                                     \\u2502\\n\\u2502                                    \\u25bc                                     \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502                   DecompositionLearner                           \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  decomposition_learner.py                                        \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502                                                                   \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  Methods:                                                         \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  - record_execution()                                             \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  - improve_estimates() \\u2192 CalibrationReport                        \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  - suggest_improvements()                                         \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  - get_historical_accuracy() \\u2192 AccuracyMetrics                    \\u2502    \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518    \\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518\\n                                    \\u2502\\n                                    \\u25bc\\n\\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510\\n\\u2502                    Existing Ensemble Infrastructure                      \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510  \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510  \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510       \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  AgentRuntime     \\u2502  \\u2502  AgentMetrics    \\u2502  \\u2502  ModelSelector   \\u2502       \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  runtime.py       \\u2502  \\u2502  metrics.py      \\u2502  \\u2502  model_selector  \\u2502       \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518  \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518  \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518       \\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518\\n```\\n\\n## Data Models (Pydantic)\\n\\n### Core Models\\n\\n```python\\n# Task Analysis\\nclass TaskAnalysis(BaseModel):\\n    complexity_score: int  # 1-10 scale\\n    domain: str  # e.g., \\"fullstack_web_app\\", \\"data_pipeline\\"\\n    estimated_human_hours: float\\n    key_requirements: List[str]\\n    risk_factors: List[str] = []\\n\\n# Sub-Task\\nclass SubTask(BaseModel):\\n    task_id: str\\n    description: str\\n    agent_type: str  # backend_lead, frontend_lead, etc.\\n    estimated_duration_minutes: int\\n    complexity: str  # simple, medium, complex\\n    dependencies: List[str] = []  # task_ids this depends on\\n    priority: int = 1  # 1 = highest\\n\\n# Decomposition Plan\\nclass DecompositionPlan(BaseModel):\\n    task_analysis: TaskAnalysis\\n    sub_tasks: List[SubTask]\\n    dependency_graph: Dict[str, List[str]]  # Serialized DAG\\n\\n# Resource Estimate\\nclass ResourceEstimate(BaseModel):\\n    agent_count: int\\n    peak_concurrent: int\\n    model_distribution: Dict[str, str]  # task_id -> model\\n    estimated_tokens: int\\n    estimated_cost: float\\n    critical_path_duration_minutes: int\\n    parallelization_factor: float\\n\\n# Allocation Plan\\nclass AllocationPlan(BaseModel):\\n    task_assignments: Dict[str, str]  # task_id -> agent_id\\n    model_selections: Dict[str, str]  # task_id -> model\\n    resource_utilization: float  # 0-1\\n\\n# Execution Wave\\nclass ExecutionWave(BaseModel):\\n    wave_number: int\\n    task_ids: List[str]\\n    estimated_duration_minutes: int\\n\\n# Schedule\\nclass Schedule(BaseModel):\\n    waves: List[ExecutionWave]\\n    total_duration_minutes: int\\n    estimated_start: datetime\\n    estimated_end: datetime\\n\\n# Full Execution Plan\\nclass ExecutionPlan(BaseModel):\\n    id: str\\n    user_request: str\\n    task_analysis: TaskAnalysis\\n    decomposition_plan: DecompositionPlan\\n    resource_estimate: ResourceEstimate\\n    allocation_plan: AllocationPlan\\n    schedule: Schedule\\n    created_at: datetime\\n    status: str  # pending_approval, approved, rejected, executing, completed\\n```\\n\\n## Algorithm Design\\n\\n### Task Analysis Algorithm\\n1. Use LLM to classify task domain and identify requirements\\n2. Calculate complexity based on:\\n   - Number of distinct components (frontend, backend, database, etc.)\\n   - Integration complexity (number of dependencies)\\n   - Technical risk factors\\n3. Estimate human hours based on similar historical tasks\\n\\n### Decomposition Algorithm\\n1. **Hierarchical Decomposition**:\\n   - Goals: High-level objectives\\n   - Tasks: Specific deliverables (30-40 minute chunks)\\n   - Actions: Atomic operations\\n2. **Domain-Specific Patterns**:\\n   - Web App: DB Schema \\u2192 API \\u2192 Frontend \\u2192 Integration \\u2192 Deploy\\n   - Data Pipeline: Source \\u2192 Transform \\u2192 Load \\u2192 Validate\\n3. **Dependency Inference**:\\n   - Use keyword matching and LLM assistance\\n   - Apply standard patterns (e.g., frontend depends on API)\\n\\n### DAG Generation\\n```python\\ndef generate_dependency_graph(sub_tasks: List[SubTask]) -> nx.DiGraph:\\n    G = nx.DiGraph()\\n    for task in sub_tasks:\\n        G.add_node(task.task_id, **task.dict())\\n        for dep in task.dependencies:\\n            G.add_edge(dep, task.task_id)\\n    \\n    # Validate DAG (no cycles)\\n    if not nx.is_directed_acyclic_graph(G):\\n        raise ValueError(\\"Dependency graph contains cycles\\")\\n    \\n    return G\\n```\\n\\n### Resource Estimation\\n- Agent count: Based on parallel paths in DAG\\n- Model selection: Based on task complexity\\n  - Simple tasks: Haiku ($0.25/1M tokens)\\n  - Complex tasks: Sonnet ($3/1M tokens)\\n- Token estimation: Based on task type and historical data\\n- Cost: Sum of (tokens * model_rate) for each task\\n\\n### Optimization (Linear Programming)\\nUsing PuLP to minimize:\\n- Objective: Minimize total cost subject to time constraints\\n- Constraints:\\n  - Maximum concurrent agents\\n  - Task dependencies respected\\n  - Budget limits\\n\\n### Execution Scheduling\\n1. Topological sort of DAG\\n2. Group tasks into waves (tasks that can run in parallel)\\n3. Calculate wave durations based on longest task\\n\\n## File Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 runtime/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 agents/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 decomposition_engine.py    # NEW: Core engine\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 decomposition_learner.py   # NEW: Learning module\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 runtime.py                 # Existing\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 metrics.py                 # Existing (extend)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 field/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ensemble_ui/\\n        \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 backend/\\n        \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 main.py                # Add new endpoints\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n                \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n                    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 TaskDecompositionViewer.jsx  # NEW\\n\\ntests/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 test_decomposition.py              # NEW: Test suite\\n\\nTASK_DECOMPOSITION.md                   # NEW: Documentation\\n```\\n\\n## Integration Points\\n\\n### With Existing Metrics (metrics.py)\\n- Use `AgentMetricsTracker` for historical performance data\\n- Store decomposition accuracy metrics in same SQLite DB\\n- Add new table: `decomposition_history`\\n\\n### With Model Selector (model_selector.py)\\n- Use for intelligent model assignment per task\\n- Respect budget tiers in optimization\\n\\n### With Agent Runtime (runtime.py)\\n- Execute scheduled tasks through runtime\\n- Track actual vs. estimated performance\\n\\n## API Contracts\\n\\n### POST /api/decompose\\n```json\\nRequest:\\n{\\n  \\"user_request\\": \\"Build a todo app with React frontend...\\"\\n}\\n\\nResponse:\\n{\\n  \\"plan_id\\": \\"uuid\\",\\n  \\"task_analysis\\": {...},\\n  \\"dependency_graph\\": {...},\\n  \\"execution_schedule\\": {...},\\n  \\"resource_estimate\\": {...},\\n  \\"mermaid_diagram\\": \\"graph TD; ...\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### POST /api/approve-plan\\n```json\\nRequest:\\n{\\n  \\"plan_id\\": \\"uuid\\",\\n  \\"action\\": \\"approve|reject|modify\\",\\n  \\"modifications\\": {...}  // Optional\\n}\\n\\nResponse:\\n{\\n  \\"status\\": \\"approved|rejected|modified\\",\\n  \\"execution_id\\": \\"uuid\\"  // If approved\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### GET /api/decomposition-history\\n```json\\nResponse:\\n{\\n  \\"total_plans\\": 50,\\n  \\"avg_accuracy\\": 0.85,\\n  \\"recent_plans\\": [...]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Performance Considerations\\n\\n1. **Decomposition Speed**: Target < 5 seconds\\n   - Use async LLM calls\\n   - Cache common patterns\\n   \\n2. **Graph Operations**: O(V + E) for most operations\\n   - NetworkX is suitable for < 100 tasks\\n   \\n3. **Optimization**: PuLP suitable for < 100 variables\\n   - Use timeout for complex problems\\n\\n## Error Handling\\n\\n1. **Cycle Detection**: Fail fast with clear error\\n2. **LLM Failures**: Fallback to simple sequential plan\\n3. **Resource Constraints**: Warn user, suggest alternatives\\n4. **Invalid Input**: Validate with Pydantic, return helpful errors\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01GuMZrQfXuPRGwKGQcR9UJU', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Test Strategy - Milestone 1: Core Decomposition Engine & Data Models\n\n## Test Overview\nThis milestone establishes the foundation testing strategy for the Smart Task Decomposition Engine. Our testing approach ensures robust data models, reliable algorithms, and comprehensive coverage of the core decomposition functionality.\n\n## Coverage Goals\n- **Unit Test Coverage**: 85% for business logic\n- **Integration Coverage**: 100% of engine methods and data model validation\n- **E2E Coverage**: Complete decomposition flow + error scenarios\n\n## Test Framework Selection\n- **Backend Testing**: pytest with pytest-asyncio for async operations\n- **Data Model Testing**: Pydantic model validation testing\n- **Graph Testing**: NetworkX graph validation and cycle detection\n- **API Testing**: FastAPI test client with pytest\n\n## Test Categories\n\n### 1. Unit Tests - Data Models (Pydantic)\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-001: TaskAnalysis Model Tests\n**Scope**: `TaskAnalysis` Pydantic model validation\n**Test Cases**:\n- Valid model creation with required fields\n- Complexity score validation (1-10 range)\n- Estimated hours validation (positive float)\n- Domain enum validation\n- Risk factors optional list handling\n- Field type validation (str, int, float, List)\n- Invalid data rejection with proper error messages\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-002: SubTask Model Tests  \n**Scope**: `SubTask` Pydantic model validation\n**Test Cases**:\n- Valid subtask creation with all fields\n- Task ID uniqueness validation\n- Agent type enum validation\n- Duration validation (positive integer)\n- Complexity enum validation (simple/medium/complex)\n- Dependencies list validation (empty list default)\n- Priority validation (positive integer, default 1)\n- Description length validation\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-003: DecompositionPlan Model Tests\n**Scope**: `DecompositionPlan` Pydantic model validation\n**Test Cases**:\n- Valid plan creation with analysis and subtasks\n- Nested model validation (TaskAnalysis within plan)\n- Dependency graph serialization validation\n- Empty subtasks list handling\n- Complex nested data structure validation\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-004: ResourceEstimate Model Tests\n**Scope**: `ResourceEstimate` Pydantic model validation\n**Test Cases**:\n- Valid resource estimate creation\n- Agent count validation (positive integer)\n- Model distribution dict validation\n- Token estimation validation (positive integer)\n- Cost validation (positive float)\n- Duration validation (positive integer)\n- Parallelization factor validation (0.0-1.0 range)\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-005: ExecutionPlan Model Tests\n**Scope**: `ExecutionPlan` comprehensive model validation\n**Test Cases**:\n- Complete execution plan creation\n- Nested model relationships validation\n- DateTime field validation\n- Status enum validation\n- ID uniqueness validation\n- Complex nested structure integrity\n\n### 2. Unit Tests - Core Engine Methods\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-006: TaskDecompositionEngine.analyze_task Tests\n**Scope**: `analyze_task()` method business logic\n**Test Cases**:\n- Simple task analysis (complexity score 1-3)\n- Medium task analysis (complexity score 4-6)\n- Complex task analysis (complexity score 7-10)\n- Domain classification accuracy\n- Human hours estimation logic\n- Risk factor identification\n- Requirement extraction validation\n- Edge cases (empty input, malformed input)\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-007: TaskDecompositionEngine.decompose_task Tests\n**Scope**: `decompose_task()` method core logic\n**Test Cases**:\n- Web app decomposition pattern validation\n- Data pipeline decomposition pattern validation\n- Subtask generation logic\n- Dependency inference accuracy\n- Task ID generation uniqueness\n- Agent type assignment logic\n- Duration estimation accuracy\n- Priority assignment validation\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-008: TaskDecompositionEngine.generate_dependency_graph Tests\n**Scope**: DAG generation and validation\n**Test Cases**:\n- Valid DAG creation from subtasks\n- Cycle detection and prevention\n- Graph topology validation\n- Node attribute preservation\n- Edge relationship accuracy\n- Empty graph handling\n- Single node graph handling\n- Complex dependency chain validation\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-009: TaskDecompositionEngine.estimate_resources Tests\n**Scope**: Resource estimation algorithms\n**Test Cases**:\n- Agent count calculation accuracy\n- Concurrent agent estimation\n- Model selection logic (Haiku vs Sonnet)\n- Token estimation algorithms\n- Cost calculation accuracy\n- Critical path duration calculation\n- Parallelization factor computation\n- Resource optimization validation\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-010: TaskDecompositionEngine.optimize_allocation Tests\n**Scope**: Resource allocation optimization\n**Test Cases**:\n- Task-to-agent assignment optimization\n- Model selection optimization\n- Resource utilization calculation\n- Budget constraint handling\n- Time constraint optimization\n- Conflict resolution logic\n- Optimization objective validation\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-011: TaskDecompositionEngine.generate_execution_schedule Tests\n**Scope**: Execution scheduling algorithm\n**Test Cases**:\n- Topological sort accuracy\n- Wave generation logic\n- Parallel task grouping\n- Wave duration calculation\n- Schedule timeline validation\n- Dependency respect verification\n- Critical path scheduling\n- Schedule optimization validation\n\n### 3. Integration Tests - Engine Workflows\n\n#### Test Task M1-IT-001: Complete Decomposition Flow Test\n**Scope**: End-to-end engine workflow integration\n**Test Cases**:\n- Full decomposition pipeline (analyze → decompose → graph → estimate → schedule)\n- Data flow between engine methods\n- State consistency across method calls\n- Error propagation through pipeline\n- Performance benchmarks (< 5 second target)\n\n#### Test Task M1-IT-002: DAG Operations Integration\n**Scope**: NetworkX graph operations with engine\n**Test Cases**:\n- Graph creation and manipulation\n- Cycle detection integration\n- Topological sort integration\n- Graph traversal algorithms\n- Graph serialization/deserialization\n- Large graph performance (100+ nodes)\n\n#### Test Task M1-IT-003: Model Validation Integration\n**Scope**: Pydantic models with engine operations\n**Test Cases**:\n- Model creation through engine methods\n- Model validation error handling\n- Nested model relationship integrity\n- Model serialization consistency\n- Model field constraint enforcement\n\n#### Test Task M1-IT-004: Algorithm Chain Integration\n**Scope**: Algorithm interdependency testing\n**Test Cases**:\n- Analysis → Decomposition data flow\n- Decomposition → DAG generation consistency\n- DAG → Resource estimation accuracy\n- Resource → Allocation optimization\n- Allocation → Scheduling consistency\n\n### 4. Unit Tests - Algorithm Components\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-012: Complexity Calculation Algorithm Tests\n**Scope**: Task complexity scoring algorithm\n**Test Cases**:\n- Component count scoring (frontend, backend, database)\n- Integration complexity calculation\n- Risk factor weighting\n- Complexity score normalization (1-10 scale)\n- Edge cases (minimal/maximal complexity)\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-013: Duration Estimation Algorithm Tests\n**Scope**: Task duration estimation logic\n**Test Cases**:\n- Historical data-based estimation\n- Task type duration patterns\n- Complexity-based duration adjustment\n- Agent skill factor consideration\n- Confidence interval calculation\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-014: Dependency Inference Algorithm Tests\n**Scope**: Automatic dependency detection\n**Test Cases**:\n- Keyword-based dependency detection\n- Domain pattern application\n- LLM-assisted dependency inference\n- Circular dependency prevention\n- Dependency strength scoring\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-015: Cost Calculation Algorithm Tests\n**Scope**: Resource cost estimation\n**Test Cases**:\n- Token-based cost calculation\n- Model rate application (Haiku vs Sonnet)\n- Parallel execution cost modeling\n- Budget constraint validation\n- Cost optimization algorithms\n\n### 5. Error Handling & Edge Cases\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-016: Error Handling Tests\n**Scope**: Comprehensive error scenario coverage\n**Test Cases**:\n- Invalid input data handling\n- Pydantic validation error propagation\n- NetworkX graph exception handling\n- Algorithm failure recovery\n- Resource constraint violations\n- Timeout handling for complex problems\n\n#### Test Task M1-UT-017: Edge Case Tests\n**Scope**: Boundary condition testing\n**Test Cases**:\n- Empty task input\n- Single task decomposition\n- Maximum complexity tasks\n- Zero dependency tasks\n- Circular dependency input\n- Resource constraint edge cases\n- Extreme parallelization scenarios\n\n### 6. Performance Tests\n\n#### Test Task M1-PT-001: Performance Benchmark Tests\n**Scope**: Algorithm performance validation\n**Test Cases**:\n- Decomposition speed benchmarks (< 5 second target)\n- Large graph operations (100+ nodes)\n- Memory usage profiling\n- CPU utilization monitoring\n- Concurrent request handling\n- Optimization algorithm performance\n\n### 7. Integration Tests - Learning Module\n\n#### Test Task M1-IT-005: DecompositionLearner Integration\n**Scope**: Learning module integration with engine\n**Test Cases**:\n- Execution result recording\n- Historical data retrieval\n- Estimate improvement algorithms\n- Accuracy metric calculation\n- Learning feedback loop validation\n\n## Test Data & Fixtures\n\n### Test Data M1-TD-001: Sample Task Inputs\n- Simple 