end\\n- **Language**: Python (existing system)\\n- **Frameworks**: \\n  - Existing activity_tracker.py \\n  - AgentRuntime framework\\n- **Libraries**:\\n  - `datetime` for timestamp handling\\n  - `json` for data serialization\\n  - Existing cost calculation libraries\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **Framework**: React (existing AgentSummaryPane)\\n- **State Management**: Existing state management \\n- **Formatting Libraries**: \\n  - `date-fns` for time formatting\\n  - `numeral.js` for currency formatting\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### Backend Components\\n1. **Activity Tracker Extension**\\n   - Responsibility: Capture and store agent execution metrics\\n   - Input: Agent execution details\\n   - Output: Enhanced agent state with cost and timing information\\n\\n2. **AgentRuntime Modifier**\\n   - Responsibility: Calculate execution metrics during agent runs\\n   - Tracks start time, token usage, model selection\\n   - Computes cost estimates\\n\\n3. **API Endpoint Updater**\\n   - Responsibility: Include new metric fields in agent state responses\\n   - Ensures backward compatibility\\n   - Provides standardized metric format\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n1. **AgentSummaryPane Renderer**\\n   - Responsibility: Display agent execution metrics\\n   - Render cost, duration, model information\\n   - Handle formatting and readability\\n\\n## 4. Data Flow Diagram\\n```\\nAgentRuntime \\n  \\u2193 (execution metrics)\\nActivity Tracker \\n  \\u2193 (store & compute)\\nAPI Endpoint \\n  \\u2193 (transmit)\\nAgentSummaryPane\\n  \\u2193 (render)\\nUser Interface\\n```\\n\\n## 5. File/Directory Structure\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 backend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 activity_tracker.py        # Extended tracking\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 agent_runtime.py           # Metric calculation\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 api/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 main.py                # Updated endpoints\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 AgentSummaryPane.jsx   # Updated renderer\\n```\\n\\n## 6. Data Model Extensions\\n```python\\nclass AgentExecutionMetrics:\\n    started_at: datetime\\n    completed_at: datetime\\n    duration_ms: int\\n    model_used: str\\n    cost_estimate: float\\n    token_usage: int\\n```\\n\\n## 7. API Design\\n### Endpoint: `/api/agent_state`\\n**Response Extension:**\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"agent_id\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"status\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"metrics\\": {\\n    \\"started_at\\": \\"ISO8601 timestamp\\",\\n    \\"completed_at\\": \\"ISO8601 timestamp\\",\\n    \\"duration_ms\\": 42000,\\n    \\"model_used\\": \\"claude-3-5-sonnet\\",\\n    \\"cost_estimate\\": 0.0042\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 8. Deployment Strategy\\n- No additional infrastructure required\\n- Can be deployed as part of regular frontend/backend update\\n- Feature flag recommended for gradual rollout\\n\\n## 9. Testing Strategy\\n### Backend Tests\\n- Unit tests for metric calculation\\n- Integration tests for API compatibility\\n- Verify cost estimation accuracy\\n\\n### Frontend Tests\\n- Component rendering tests\\n- Snapshot testing for AgentSummaryPane\\n- Formatting and display tests\\n\\n## 10. Risks and Mitigations\\n1. **Performance Overhead**\\n   - Mitigation: Lightweight metric tracking\\n   - Minimal additional computation\\n\\n2. **Incomplete Metric Tracking**\\n   - Mitigation: Graceful fallback\\n   - Display partial information if complete data unavailable\\n\\n## 11. Alternatives Considered\\n1. **Full Rewrite of Tracking System**\\n   - Rejected: Too invasive\\n   - Current approach more maintainable\\n\\n2. **External Metrics Service**\\n   - Rejected: Adds unnecessary complexity\\n   - Current approach more integrated\\n\\n## 12. Open Questions\\n- Precise token pricing for different models\\n- Exact method of cost estimation for edge cases\\n\\n## 13. Implementation Notes\\n- Use existing infrastructure\\n- Minimal changes to current system\\n- Easily extensible for future enhancements"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MWZbWMaL6jASYTNJE19Xjf', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/project-view/milestone_plan.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'Project View Dashboard'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MWZbWMaL6jASYTNJE19Xjf', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "message": "Comprehensive architecture proposal for Project View Dashboard created, focusing on modular SPA design with flexible backend-driven project tracking", "key_decisions": ["Use FastAPI for backend with lightweight, performant approach", "Implement React frontend with modular component structure", "Leverage existing project_tracker.py for data retrieval", "Inference-based SDLC phase detection", "Local React state management for simplicity"], "self_analysis": "The architecture proposal successfully captures the project requirements by providing a detailed, extensible design that balances technical depth with practical implementation strategies. The approach demonstrates careful consideration of existing system constraints while introducing clear, modular components that can evolve with future project needs."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016rm8KUXowcn8tFzgrqKwwK', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016rm8KUXowcn8tFzgrqKwwK', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Project View Dashboard - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n**Architectural Pattern**: Modular Single-Page Application (SPA) with Backend-Driven Views\\n**Core Goal**: Create a flexible, maintainable project tracking dashboard that provides comprehensive project insights and actionable next steps.\\n\\n## 2. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Language**: Python\\n- **Framework**: FastAPI\\n  - Rationale: Lightweight, high-performance, built-in OpenAPI support\\n  - Alternatives Considered: Flask (less opinionated), Django (too heavyweight)\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **Framework**: React\\n  - Rationale: Component-based architecture, existing codebase uses React\\n- **Styling**: Bootstrap + Custom Dark Theme\\n- **State Management**: Local React State (for simplicity)\\n  - Alternatives: Redux (over-engineered for current scope), Context API (potential future upgrade)\\n\\n### Persistence\\n- **Existing Project Tracking**: Leverage `project_tracker.py`\\n- **Data Source**: Project notes and tasks as primary data store\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### Backend Components\\n1. **ProjectDetailsEndpoint**\\n   - Responsibility: Retrieve comprehensive project information\\n   - Input: `project_id`\\n   - Output: Project state, SDLC phase, milestones, tasks\\n\\n2. **ProjectContinuationEndpoint**\\n   - Responsibility: Trigger next phase of project\\n   - Mechanism: Spawn Executive Director with project context\\n   - Handles: Phase transition, context preservation\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n1. **ProjectView.jsx** (Main Container)\\n   - Manages overall layout and page state\\n   - Fetches and displays project list\\n   - Renders detailed project view\\n\\n2. **ProjectStatusCard.jsx**\\n   - Displays high-level project metadata\\n   - Shows status, timestamps, basic info\\n\\n3. **SDLCIndicator.jsx**\\n   - Visualizes current SDLC phase\\n   - Supports multiple phase representations\\n\\n4. **MilestoneProgress.jsx**\\n   - Tracks and displays milestone completion\\n   - Provides visual and numerical progress\\n\\n5. **NextStepsPanel.jsx**\\n   - Displays actionable project continuation steps\\n   - Manages \\"Continue\\" button interaction\\n\\n## 4. File/Directory Structure\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 backend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 api/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 project_details.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 project_continuation.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 sdlc_tracker.py\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ProjectView.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ProjectStatusCard.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 SDLCIndicator.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 MilestoneProgress.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 NextStepsPanel.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 api.js\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Data Flow\\n1. User navigates to Projects view\\n2. Frontend requests `/api/projects` to fetch project list\\n3. User selects a project\\n4. Frontend calls `/api/projects/{project_id}/details`\\n5. Backend retrieves project info from project_tracker\\n6. Frontend renders detailed project view\\n7. User clicks \\"Continue\\"\\n8. Frontend calls `/api/projects/{project_id}/continue`\\n9. Backend spawns Executive Director\\n10. UI updates to reflect new project state\\n\\n## 6. API Design\\n### Endpoints\\n- `GET /api/projects` - List all projects\\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/details` - Get project details\\n- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/continue` - Advance project\\n\\n### Response Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"project_id\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"name\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"current_phase\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"milestones\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"name\\": \\"string\\",\\n      \\"status\\": \\"completed|in_progress|pending\\",\\n      \\"progress\\": 0.75\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\"next_steps\\": [\\"string\\"]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 7. Deployment Strategy\\n- Containerized with Docker\\n- Deployed alongside existing Ensemble UI\\n- Uses existing authentication mechanisms\\n\\n## 8. Testing Strategy\\n### Backend\\n- Unit tests for SDLC phase detection\\n- Integration tests for API endpoints\\n- Error handling and edge case coverage\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- Component rendering tests (Jest)\\n- Interaction tests (React Testing Library)\\n- API service mocking\\n- State management tests\\n\\n## 9. Risks and Mitigations\\n1. **Incomplete Project Data**\\n   - Mitigation: Graceful UI handling, default states\\n2. **SDLC Phase Detection Accuracy**\\n   - Mitigation: Flexible keyword-based detection, manual override capability\\n3. **Performance with Large Project Sets**\\n   - Mitigation: Implement pagination, lazy loading\\n\\n## 10. Open Questions\\n- How granular should milestone tracking be?\\n- Preferences for SDLC phase visual representation?\\n- Desired level of \\"Continue\\" action customization?\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n1. Microservices Architecture: Rejected due to unnecessary complexity\\n2. Redux for State Management: Premature optimization\\n3. Static Phase Definitions: Chose flexible, inference-based approach\\n\\n**Recommended Next Steps**:\\n1. Review architecture proposal\\n2. Validate technical approach\\n3. Confirm design meets business requirements\\n4. Proceed with implementation"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report 