{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 03:00:28", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-a22b430f-adf8-4923-84a0-4c7be6804ce5', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ensemble_system_analysis_requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "focus": "Design backend architecture for ensemble agent system improvements: 1) Real-time progress streaming with WebSocket events, 2) Error recovery with state persistence and retries, 3) Performance analytics with metrics tracking. Focus on backend Python systems, not UI components."\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0147xbPBktWtTkhcrD6a2EQX', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ensemble_system_analysis_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0147xbPBktWtTkhcrD6a2EQX', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble Agent System Analysis & Improvement Requirements\\n\\n## Executive Summary\\n\\nThis document analyzes the Ensemble multi-agent system architecture and identifies the top 3 improvements that would make agents more effective. The analysis is based on reviewing the codebase, agent definitions, and system architecture.\\n\\n## Project Vision\\n\\nAnalyze the ensemble agent system to identify and implement the three most impactful improvements that will enhance agent effectiveness, reduce coordination failures, and improve overall system reliability.\\n\\n## Current System Analysis\\n\\n### Architecture Overview\\n- **Agent Hierarchy**: 4 tiers (Leadership \\u2192 Coordinators \\u2192 Developers/Testers \\u2192 Writers)\\n- **Total Agents**: 16 agents (consolidated from 23, 30% reduction)\\n- **Core Technology**: Anthropic Claude API with hierarchical delegation\\n- **Key Features**: TDD workflow, permission system, state persistence\\n\\n### Identified Issues\\n\\nAfter analyzing the codebase and agent definitions, the following problems were identified:\\n\\n#### 1. **Lack of Real-Time Progress Feedback**\\n- **Problem**: Agents execute in background threads without granular progress updates\\n- **Impact**: Users don\'t know what agents are doing, causing uncertainty about system status\\n- **Evidence**: \\n  - `main.py` uses background threads for execution (line 79)\\n  - WebSocket broadcasts only top-level status changes\\n  - No intermediate progress reporting during long-running agent operations\\n  - No visibility into which sub-agents are currently active\\n\\n#### 2. **Inadequate Error Recovery & Context Preservation**\\n- **Problem**: When agents fail, there\'s no automatic retry logic or context preservation for resume\\n- **Impact**: Single failures cascade, wasting tokens and requiring manual intervention\\n- **Evidence**:\\n  - State persistence exists (`state.py`) but resume logic is incomplete (line 64 in `runtime.py`: \\"Full resume with conversation history would need message reconstruction\\")\\n  - No retry logic in `runtime.py` when tool execution fails\\n  - Failed spawns don\'t preserve parent agent context for debugging\\n  - Agent state checkpoints exist but aren\'t used for automatic recovery\\n\\n#### 3. **Missing Agent Performance Metrics & Feedback Loops**\\n- **Problem**: No tracking of agent effectiveness, token usage, or success rates\\n- **Impact**: Can\'t identify which agents need improvement or optimization\\n- **Evidence**:\\n  - No analytics collection in `AgentRuntime`\\n  - No metrics on spawn success/failure rates\\n  - No token usage tracking per agent type\\n  - No performance comparison between model tiers\\n  - README acknowledges this gap: \\"Phase 3: Self-Improvement\\" includes \\"Agent performance analytics\\"\\n\\n### Additional Observations\\n- \\u2705 **Strengths**: Strong permission system, clear hierarchy, rogue agent prevention working well\\n- \\u2705 **Strengths**: TDD workflow is well-designed\\n- \\u26a0\\ufe0f **Minor Issue**: Model selection is static (could be adaptive based on task success)\\n- \\u26a0\\ufe0f **Minor Issue**: Agent definitions in markdown could benefit from validation schema\\n\\n## Top 3 Improvements (Prioritized)\\n\\n### Improvement #1: Real-Time Agent Progress Streaming \\n**Priority**: HIGH  \\n**Complexity**: Medium  \\n**Impact**: High (dramatically improves user experience)\\n\\n**Description**: Implement granular progress tracking and streaming for agent execution, allowing users to see:\\n- Current agent activity (which agent is thinking/executing)\\n- Tool invocations in real-time\\n- Sub-agent spawn events\\n- Iteration progress (current/max)\\n- Streaming responses from Claude API\\n\\n**Requirements**:\\n1. Enhance `AgentRuntime` to emit progress events during execution\\n2. Add event bus or callback system for progress notifications\\n3. Update WebSocket handler to stream progress events to frontend\\n4. Add progress tracking to spawned agent execution\\n5. Include tool execution progress (start/complete/fail)\\n6. Show model selection decisions in progress feed\\n\\n**Success Criteria**:\\n- Users can see which agent is active at any moment\\n- Tool invocations appear in real-time\\n- Spawn events are visible with parent-child relationships\\n- WebSocket clients receive progress updates < 500ms after events\\n- No performance degradation (< 5% overhead)\\n\\n### Improvement #2: Automatic Error Recovery & Context Preservation\\n**Priority**: HIGH  \\n**Complexity**: High  \\n**Impact**: High (reduces wasted tokens, improves reliability)\\n\\n**Description**: Implement intelligent error recovery with automatic retries and full context preservation for resume after failures.\\n\\n**Requirements**:\\n1. Complete state manager resume functionality (message reconstruction)\\n2. Add retry logic with exponential backoff for transient failures\\n3. Implement context preservation for spawned agents (parent context + partial results)\\n4. Add automatic checkpoint validation and rollback\\n5. Create error classification system (retryable vs. fatal)\\n6. Preserve tool execution results across retries\\n\\n**Success Criteria**:\\n- Agents can resume from last checkpoint after crashes\\n- Transient API errors (rate limits, timeouts) trigger automatic retry\\n- Failed spawns preserve parent agent state for debugging\\n- Context includes: conversation history, tool results, spawned agent data\\n- Recovery success rate > 80% for retryable errors\\n- Zero token waste on successful recovery (resume from checkpoint)\\n\\n### Improvement #3: Agent Performance Analytics & Adaptive Optimization\\n**Priority**: MEDIUM  \\n**Complexity**: Medium  \\n**Impact**: Medium-High (enables continuous improvement)\\n\\n**Description**: Implement comprehensive analytics tracking for agent performance with adaptive model selection based on historical success rates.\\n\\n**Requirements**:\\n1. Track metrics per agent instance:\\n   - Token usage (input/output)\\n   - Execution time\\n   - Success/failure rates\\n   - Iteration count vs. max iterations\\n   - Tool invocation patterns\\n2. Aggregate metrics by agent type and model tier\\n3. Create analytics dashboard endpoint for reporting\\n4. Implement adaptive model selection:\\n   - Start with budget tier default\\n   - Upgrade model if agent fails repeatedly\\n   - Downgrade model if agent consistently succeeds quickly\\n5. Add performance comparison reports (model A vs. model B for same task)\\n6. Export metrics for analysis (JSON, CSV)\\n\\n**Success Criteria**:\\n- All agent executions tracked with complete metrics\\n- Analytics API returns per-agent and aggregate statistics\\n- Adaptive model selection improves success rate by 15%+\\n- Token usage optimization reduces costs by 10%+\\n- Reports identify underperforming agents for refinement\\n- Metrics persist across system restarts\\n\\n## Out of Scope (For This Phase)\\n\\nThe following are important but not in the top 3:\\n- Enhanced TDD workflow validation\\n- File exploration agents\\n- Multi-user support\\n- Agent definition schema validation\\n- Performance profiling tools\\n- Cost prediction before execution\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n1. **Must maintain backward compatibility** with existing agent definitions\\n2. **Must not break permission system** (can_write_code, can_write_tests enforcement)\\n3. **Must not increase API costs** by more than 10%\\n4. **Must support concurrent agent execution** (multi-user eventually)\\n5. **Must preserve existing state file format** (add extensions, don\'t replace)\\n\\n## Success Criteria (Overall)\\n\\n1. \\u2705 Real-time progress visible to users\\n2. \\u2705 Error recovery succeeds > 80% for retryable failures\\n3. \\u2705 Performance metrics tracked for all agents\\n4. \\u2705 All existing tests continue to pass\\n5. \\u2705 Documentation updated for new features\\n6. \\u2705 Zero breaking changes to agent definitions\\n\\n## Implementation Priority\\n\\n**Phase 1: Progress Streaming** (Implement First)\\n- High user impact\\n- Medium complexity\\n- Foundation for other improvements\\n\\n**Phase 2: Error Recovery** (Implement Second)\\n- High reliability impact\\n- High complexity (needs Phase 1 for monitoring)\\n- Builds on state persistence system\\n\\n**Phase 3: Performance Analytics** (Implement Third)\\n- Enables long-term improvement\\n- Medium complexity\\n- Leverages data from Phase 1 & 2\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. Updated `AgentRuntime` class with progress events\\n2. Enhanced `StateManager` with full resume capability\\n3. New `AgentAnalytics` module for metrics tracking\\n4. Updated WebSocket handlers for streaming\\n5. New API endpoints for analytics queries\\n6. Updated documentation (README, implementation guide)\\n7. Test suite covering new functionality\\n8. Performance benchmarks before/after\\n\\n## Timeline Estimate\\n\\n- **Improvement #1**: 2-3 days (progress streaming)\\n- **Improvement #2**: 3-4 days (error recovery)\\n- **Improvement #3**: 2-3 days (analytics)\\n- **Testing & Documentation**: 1-2 days\\n- **Total**: 8-12 days for complete implementation\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\nThis analysis prioritizes improvements that:\\n1. **Maximize user value** (progress feedback eliminates uncertainty)\\n2. **Improve system reliability** (error recovery reduces failures)\\n3. **Enable continuous improvement** (analytics identify what to optimize next)\\n\\nThe three improvements are complementary and build on each other, creating a more robust and observable agent system.\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0139m1iYJvwFAaT9Ej2smxE7', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Ensemble Agent Backend Architecture Proposal\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n\n### Core Design Philosophy\n- Modular, event-driven backend architecture\n- High observability and resilience\n- Minimal performance overhead\n- Seamless error recovery\n\n### High-Level Architecture Pattern\n- Event-Driven Microservices\n- CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) for metrics and state management\n- Pub/Sub for real-time progress streaming\n\n## 2. Technology Stack\n\n### Core Technologies\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+ (type hints, asyncio)\n- **Async Framework**: `asyncio` + `uvloop` for high-performance concurrency\n- **WebSocket**: `websockets` library\n- **Event Bus**: `aio-pika` (AMQP-based message queue)\n- **Metrics**: Prometheus + `prometheus_client`\n- **Persistence**: SQLAlchemy with PostgreSQL\n\n### Rationale\n- Python chosen for its strong async capabilities and rich AI/ML ecosystem\n- `asyncio` provides efficient concurrent execution without heavy threading\n- Prometheus offers robust metrics collection with minimal overhead\n- PostgreSQL ensures strong consistency for state persistence\n\n## 3. System Components\n\n### 1. AgentRuntime (Enhanced)\n- Responsible for agent lifecycle management\n- Emits granular progress events\n- Handles automatic error recovery\n- Coordinates state checkpointing\n\n### 2. StateManager\n- Manages agent state persistence\n- Implements checkpoint/resume functionality\n- Supports partial state reconstruction\n- Handles context preservation during retries\n\n### 3. ProgressEventBus\n- Centralized event streaming mechanism\n- Publishes real-time agent progress\n- Supports WebSocket broadcasting\n- Low-latency event routing\n\n### 4. AgentAnalytics\n- Collects performance metrics\n- Tracks token usage, success rates\n- Provides adaptive model selection logic\n- Generates performance reports\n\n### 5. ErrorRecoveryOrchestrator\n- Classifies errors (retriable vs fatal)\n- Manages retry strategies\n- Implements exponential backoff\n- Tracks error history for optimization\n\n## 4. Data Flow Diagram\n\n```\nAgent Spawn Request\n    ↓\n[AgentRuntime]\n    ├── Start Execution\n    ├── Emit Progress Events → [ProgressEventBus]\n    ├── Checkpoint State → [StateManager]\n    └── Track Metrics → [AgentAnalytics]\n        │\n        ├── On Error → [ErrorRecoveryOrchestrator]\n        │   ├── Retry Logic\n        │   └── State Resume\n        │\n        └── Performance Tracking\n            ├── Token Usage\n            ├── Success Rates\n            └── Model Performance\n```\n\n## 5. Key Implementation Details\n\n### Progress Streaming\n- Use WebSocket for real-time updates\n- Event types:\n  - `agent_spawn`\n  - `tool_invocation_start`\n  - `tool_invocation_complete`\n  - `agent_state_change`\n  - `error_occurred`\n\n### Error Recovery Strategy\n- Checkpoint every significant state transition\n- Store:\n  - Conversation history\n  - Tool execution results\n  - Spawned agent context\n- Retry mechanism:\n  1. Exponential backoff\n  2. Maximum retry limit\n  3. Fallback to manual intervention\n\n### Analytics Collection\n- Metrics per agent:\n  - Execution time\n  - Token consumption\n  - Success/failure rate\n  - Model tier performance\n- Aggregation levels:\n  - Per agent instance\n  - Per agent type\n  - Across system\n\n## 6. Deployment Considerations\n\n### Container Strategy\n- Docker containers for each component\n- Docker Compose for local development\n- Kubernetes for production scaling\n\n### Environment Configuration\n- Use `.env` files for configuration\n- Support multiple environments:\n  - Development\n  - Staging\n  - Production\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### Testing Approaches\n- Unit Tests: `pytest`\n- Integration Tests: `pytest-asyncio`\n- Performance Tests: `locust`\n- Coverage: `coverage.py`\n\n### Test Coverage Requirements\n- 90%+ unit test coverage\n- Integration tests for error recovery\n- Chaos testing for resilience verification\n\n## 8. Risks and Mitigations\n\n### Potential Risks\n1. Performance Overhead from Metrics\n   - **Mitigation**: Sampling, async metrics collection\n2. WebSocket Connection Instability\n   - **Mitigation**: Reconnection logic, connection pooling\n3. State Persistence Complexity\n   - **Mitigation**: Robust serialization, comprehensive testing\n\n## 9. Open Questions for User Review\n\n1. Preferred message queue technology (current proposal: AMQP)\n2. Specific performance budget for metrics collection\n3. Desired granularity of progress events\n\n## 10. Alternatives Considered\n\n### Alternative 1: Synchronous Execution\n- **Pros**: Simpler implementation\n- **Cons**: Poor concurrency, blocking operations\n- **Verdict**: Rejected in favor of async design\n\n### Alternative 2: Separate Metrics Service\n- **Pros**: Clearer separation of concerns\n- **Cons**: Additional complexity, network overhead\n- **Verdict**: Current design integrated for performance\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThis architecture provides a robust, performant backend for the ensemble agent system, focusing on real-time visibility, error resilience, and continuous improvement through comprehensive analytics.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0139m1iYJvwFAaT9Ej2smxE7', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_030028.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_030028.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.1%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.5\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- The architecture proposal successfully addresses the requirements by providing a lightweight, flexible approach to UI enhancements. The modular design allows for easy implementation of new features wi...\n- The architecture proposal effectively addresses the 404 error issue by providing a targeted, low-risk solution that preserves the existing system architecture. By analyzing root causes and proposing m...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
