y\\n7. All tests passing\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- \\u2705 UI dropdown/selector displays \\"1s\\", \\"1m\\", \\"5m\\" options only\\n- \\u2705 Selecting \\"1s\\" applies 1-second (1000ms) update interval\\n- \\u2705 Selecting \\"1m\\" applies 1-minute (60000ms) update interval\\n- \\u2705 Selecting \\"5m\\" applies 5-minute (300000ms) update interval\\n- \\u2705 UI updates at correct frequency for each selection\\n- \\u2705 No console errors or warnings\\n- \\u2705 All unit tests pass\\n- \\u2705 All integration tests pass\\n- \\u2705 Code follows existing project conventions\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- None (first milestone)\\n\\n### Estimated Scope\\n- **Development:** 2-3 hours\\n- **Testing:** 1-2 hours\\n- **Total:** 3-5 hours\\n\\n### Technical Notes\\n- Need to find React/Vue/Angular components (likely React based on typical patterns)\\n- Look for dropdown/select components with interval configuration\\n- Update both display values and internal millisecond mappings\\n- Handle potential legacy preference values gracefully\\n- Follow TDD approach: write tests first, then implementation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n- All interval options changed to 1s, 1m, 5m\\n- All three intervals function correctly\\n- Test coverage for interval logic and UI interaction\\n- No regression in existing functionality\\n- Clean commit history with descriptive messages\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Risk Management\\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |\\n|------|------------|--------|------------|\\n| Cannot locate source files | Low | High | Search output directory and common UI patterns |\\n| Breaking existing state management | Medium | Medium | Write tests first, validate before/after |\\n| Legacy saved preferences | Low | Low | Add default/fallback logic for invalid values |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Notes\\n- This is a single-milestone project due to its focused scope\\n- All work (discovery, implementation, testing) contained in one milestone\\n- Focus on TDD approach to ensure correctness\\n- Commit changes after all tests pass\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MNAHfZDQ2cnzYJpuoUtT5S', 'name': 'run_command', 'input': {'command': 'find /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui -name "*.md" | grep -E "(requirements|req)" | head -5'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MNAHfZDQ2cnzYJpuoUtT5S', 'content': '{"success": true, "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/requirements.md\\n/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/node_modules/require-from-string/readme.md\\n/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend_integration_requirements.md\\n/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/ui_files_404_fix_requirements.md\\n/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/ui_enhancements_requirements.md\\n", "stderr": ""}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FWP1j8tyzAQb3sLEVz39NA', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FWP1j8tyzAQb3sLEVz39NA', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble UI Requirements\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nComplete a web application for submitting problems and monitoring agent execution in real-time, with full backend-frontend integration.\\n\\n## Core Objectives\\n1. Enable problem submission via UI\\n2. Spawn Executive Director agent from backend\\n3. Provide real-time agent execution visibility\\n4. Display agent hierarchy and status\\n5. Show comprehensive results and handle errors gracefully\\n\\n## Key Requirements\\n- Backend Integration with Agent Runtime\\n- Real-time Agent Status Display\\n- Agent Hierarchy Visualization\\n- Comprehensive Error Handling\\n- Responsive, Professional UI\\n\\n## Technical Stack\\n- Backend: Python 3.11+, FastAPI\\n- Frontend: React 18, Tailwind CSS\\n- WebSocket for real-time updates\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. User can submit problem description\\n2. Backend spawns Executive Director agent\\n3. Agent execution tracked in real-time\\n4. Agent hierarchy displays dynamically\\n5. Results displayed clearly\\n6. Errors handled professionally\\n7. All tests pass\\n8. Responsive, intuitive UI\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Use existing Ensemble agent runtime\\n- Follow Test-Driven Development\\n- Handle long-running tasks asynchronously\\n- Maintain clean, modular architecture"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016ufctdYUs8VpAF8trehpTv', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/requirements.md', 'milestone_file': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestones.md', 'project_name': 'Ensemble UI Requirements Implementation', 'specific_task': 'Update interval selector from high-frequency options (500ms, 1s, 2s) to production intervals (1s, 1m, 5m)', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016ufctdYUs8VpAF8trehpTv', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": null}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Ju6x2NhFk7o2HEHQ6c9p6B', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Ju6x2NhFk7o2HEHQ6c9p6B', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Whimsical Names Integration: Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Architectural Pattern: Decorator/Generator Integration\\n- **Core Approach:** Lightweight, non-invasive modification to existing agent runtime\\n- **Pattern:** Decorator pattern for name generation\\n- **Goal:** Minimal changes to existing system while adding significant UX improvement\\n\\n## 2. Tech Stack\\n- **Language:** Python 3.9+\\n- **Runtime:** Existing agent framework\\n- **Dependencies:** Standard library only (threading, random)\\n- **No external package dependencies**\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### 3.1 Name Data Source\\n- **Module:** `name_data.py`\\n- **Responsibility:** Provide list of whimsical names\\n- **Location:** `src/runtime/agents/name_data.py`\\n\\n### 3.2 Name Generator\\n- **Class:** `AgentNameGenerator`\\n- **Responsibilities:**\\n  - Generate unique whimsical names\\n  - Handle name collisions\\n  - Ensure thread-safety\\n- **Location:** `src/runtime/agents/name_generator.py`\\n\\n### 3.3 Runtime Integration\\n- **Target:** `AgentRuntime.__init__` method\\n- **Modification:** Replace timestamp-based ID generation\\n- **Preservation:** Backward compatibility with explicit `agent_id`\\n\\n## 4. Data Flow\\n```\\n[Name Data Source] -> [Name Generator] -> [AgentRuntime] -> [Activity Tracker]\\n       \\u2191                   |                   |\\n       |                   |                   |\\n  1000 Whimsical    Thread-Safe Name     Unique Agent ID\\n     Names          Generation           Assigned\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Key Design Decisions\\n\\n### 5.1 Name Generation Strategy\\n- **Randomization:** Shuffle name pool on initialization\\n- **Uniqueness:** \\n  - Use thread-safe set to track used names\\n  - Add numeric suffix for collisions\\n- **Performance:** O(1) name generation\\n\\n### 5.2 Concurrency Handling\\n- **Mechanism:** Explicit threading lock\\n- **Approach:** Prevent race conditions during name generation\\n- **Performance Impact:** Minimal overhead, < 1ms per name generation\\n\\n## 6. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk: Name Collision\\n- **Mitigation:** \\n  - Numeric suffix system\\n  - Large initial name pool (1000 names)\\n  - Explicit collision resolution mechanism\\n\\n### Risk: Performance Degradation\\n- **Mitigation:**\\n  - Lightweight name generation algorithm\\n  - Minimal synchronization overhead\\n  - Constant-time name selection\\n\\n## 7. Testing Approach\\n\\n### Unit Testing\\n- Name uniqueness verification\\n- Collision handling\\n- Thread-safety validation\\n- Edge case handling (large number of agents)\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n- Agent runtime integration\\n- Activity tracker compatibility\\n- UI rendering of new names\\n\\n## 8. Deployment Considerations\\n- **No database migrations**\\n- **No runtime environment changes**\\n- **Backward compatible**\\n- **Zero downtime deployment possible**\\n\\n## 9. Future Extensibility\\n- Easy to add more names\\n- Potential for theming or categorization\\n- Simple to modify name generation logic\\n\\n## 10. Alternative Approaches Considered\\n1. **UUID-based Names**: \\n   - Pros: Guaranteed uniqueness\\n   - Cons: Not human-readable\\n2. **Incremental Numbering**: \\n   - Pros: Simple\\n   - Cons: Less memorable\\n3. **External Name Service**: \\n   - Pros: Scalable\\n   - Cons: Added complexity\\n\\n**Chosen Approach:** Current implementation - lightweight, performant, human-friendly\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01D8T6Zrcm4pbq2Rj45U5fRZ', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Ensemble UI Interval Options Update: Architecture\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n\n### Architectural Pattern: Component-Level Update\n- **Core Approach:** Modify existing interval selector UI component\n- **Pattern:** Direct component modification with backwards compatibility\n- **Goal:** Change interval options from high-frequency (500ms, 1s, 2s) to production-suitable (1s, 1m, 5m)\n\n## 2. Tech Stack\n- **Frontend:** React 18+ with TypeScript\n- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS\n- **State Management:** React hooks (useState/useEffect)\n- **Testing:** Jest + React Testing Library\n\n## 3. System Components\n\n### 3.1 Interval Selector Component\n- **Location:** `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/`\n- **Responsibility:** Display interval dropdown/selector\n- **Modification Required:** Update options array and conversion logic\n\n### 3.2 Interval Conversion Logic\n- **Location:** Within interval selector or utility module\n- **Responsibility:** Convert user-friendly labels to milliseconds\n- **Current:** 500ms, 1s, 2s → 500, 1000, 2000ms\n- **Target:** 1s, 1m, 5m → 1000, 60000, 300000ms\n\n### 3.3 Real-time Update Handler\n- **Location:** WebSocket or polling mechanism\n- **Responsibility:** Use selected interval for status updates\n- **Modification Required:** Accept new interval values\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n```\n[User Selects Interval] → [Convert to Milliseconds] → [Update Mechanism] → [Backend Polling/WebSocket]\n        ↓                          ↓                        ↓\n   "1s", "1m", "5m"         1000, 60000, 300000      Timer/Interval Update\n```\n\n## 5. Key Design Decisions\n\n### 5.1 Interval Options\n- **Previous:** 500ms, 1s, 2s (too frequent for production)\n- **New:** 1s, 1m, 5m (practical for monitoring)\n- **Default:** 1s (maintains reasonable responsiveness)\n\n### 5.2 Conversion Strategy\n```typescript\nconst INTERVAL_OPTIONS = [\n  { label: "1s", value: 1000 },\n  { label: "1m", value: 60000 }, \n  { label: "5m", value: 300000 }\n];\n```\n\n### 5.3 Backwards Compatibility\n- Handle any saved preferences gracefully\n- Default to 1s if invalid value encountered\n- No breaking changes to API contracts\n\n## 6. Component Architecture\n\n### File Structure\n```\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/\n├── components/\n│   ├── IntervalSelector.tsx          (main component to modify)\n│   └── __tests__/\n│       └── IntervalSelector.test.tsx (test file to update)\n└── utils/\n    └── intervalUtils.ts              (conversion utilities)\n```\n\n## 7. Implementation Plan\n\n### Phase 1: Locate Components\n- Find interval selector UI component\n- Identify current options array\n- Locate conversion logic\n\n### Phase 2: Update Logic\n- Replace interval options\n- Update conversion mappings\n- Handle edge cases\n\n### Phase 3: Testing\n- Unit tests for conversion logic\n- Integration tests for UI behavior\n- Verify real-time updates work correctly\n\n## 8. Testing Strategy\n\n### Unit Tests\n- Interval conversion accuracy\n- Option rendering\n- Default selection behavior\n- Invalid value handling\n\n### Integration Tests  \n- Full UI workflow\n- Real-time update frequency\n- WebSocket/polling integration\n- Error handling\n\n## 9. Risk Mitigation\n\n### Risk: Breaking Existing Functionality\n- **Mitigation:** Write tests first, comprehensive regression testing\n\n### Risk: Invalid Saved Preferences\n- **Mitigation:** Add fallback logic for invalid interval values\n\n### Risk: Performance Impact\n- **Mitigation:** New intervals are less frequent, should improve performance\n\n## 10. Success Criteria\n- UI shows only "1s", "1m", "5m" options\n- Each option applies correct millisecond interval\n- Real-time updates work at correct frequency\n- All tests pass\n- No console errors or warnings\n- Clean, maintainable code\n\n## 11. Deployment\n- No backend changes required\n- Frontend-only modification\n- Can be deployed independently\n- Backwards compatible with existing backend'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01D8T6Zrcm4pbq2Rj45U5fRZ', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_025931.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260116_025931.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_017oKmaua9PKNgNhDXA8sd5D', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/frontend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Locate and Update UI Components - Update interval selector from high-frequency options (500ms, 1s, 2s) to production intervals (1s, 1m, 5m)', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_017oKmaua9PKNgNhDXA8sd5D', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "tasks_identified": 5, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md", "dependencies": ["task1", "task2", "task3", "task4", "task5"], "message": "Completed task breakdown for interval selector update with 5 detailed frontend tasks mapped to production requirements."}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 81.5%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.3\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively executed the complete planning and implementation workflow for Milestone 1. Successfully coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all three Coordinators for com...\n- Successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Effectively managed the sequential process: milestone planning, architec...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'o