{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 03:00:29", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-2f8f7aaf-0e22-465d-98c8-d219223ecd12', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Implement CLI Provider Integration and Cost Estimation Foundation",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ai_provider_enhancement_requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01K8EP8vqecQSx9wVdm1wNCd', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01K8EP8vqecQSx9wVdm1wNCd', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Project View Dashboard - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n**Architectural Pattern**: Modular Single-Page Application (SPA) with Backend-Driven Views\\n**Core Goal**: Create a flexible, maintainable project tracking dashboard that provides comprehensive project insights and actionable next steps.\\n\\n## 2. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Language**: Python\\n- **Framework**: FastAPI\\n  - Rationale: Lightweight, high-performance, built-in OpenAPI support\\n  - Alternatives Considered: Flask (less opinionated), Django (too heavyweight)\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **Framework**: React\\n  - Rationale: Component-based architecture, existing codebase uses React\\n- **Styling**: Bootstrap + Custom Dark Theme\\n- **State Management**: Local React State (for simplicity)\\n  - Alternatives: Redux (over-engineered for current scope), Context API (potential future upgrade)\\n\\n### Persistence\\n- **Existing Project Tracking**: Leverage `project_tracker.py`\\n- **Data Source**: Project notes and tasks as primary data store\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### Backend Components\\n1. **ProjectDetailsEndpoint**\\n   - Responsibility: Retrieve comprehensive project information\\n   - Input: `project_id`\\n   - Output: Project state, SDLC phase, milestones, tasks\\n\\n2. **ProjectContinuationEndpoint**\\n   - Responsibility: Trigger next phase of project\\n   - Mechanism: Spawn Executive Director with project context\\n   - Handles: Phase transition, context preservation\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n1. **ProjectView.jsx** (Main Container)\\n   - Manages overall layout and page state\\n   - Fetches and displays project list\\n   - Renders detailed project view\\n\\n2. **ProjectStatusCard.jsx**\\n   - Displays high-level project metadata\\n   - Shows status, timestamps, basic info\\n\\n3. **SDLCIndicator.jsx**\\n   - Visualizes current SDLC phase\\n   - Supports multiple phase representations\\n\\n4. **MilestoneProgress.jsx**\\n   - Tracks and displays milestone completion\\n   - Provides visual and numerical progress\\n\\n5. **NextStepsPanel.jsx**\\n   - Displays actionable project continuation steps\\n   - Manages \\"Continue\\" button interaction\\n\\n## 4. File/Directory Structure\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 backend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 api/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 project_details.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 project_continuation.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 sdlc_tracker.py\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ProjectView.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ProjectStatusCard.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 SDLCIndicator.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 MilestoneProgress.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 NextStepsPanel.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 api.js\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Data Flow\\n1. User navigates to Projects view\\n2. Frontend requests `/api/projects` to fetch project list\\n3. User selects a project\\n4. Frontend calls `/api/projects/{project_id}/details`\\n5. Backend retrieves project info from project_tracker\\n6. Frontend renders detailed project view\\n7. User clicks \\"Continue\\"\\n8. Frontend calls `/api/projects/{project_id}/continue`\\n9. Backend spawns Executive Director\\n10. UI updates to reflect new project state\\n\\n## 6. API Design\\n### Endpoints\\n- `GET /api/projects` - List all projects\\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/details` - Get project details\\n- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/continue` - Advance project\\n\\n### Response Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"project_id\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"name\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"current_phase\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"milestones\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"name\\": \\"string\\",\\n      \\"status\\": \\"completed|in_progress|pending\\",\\n      \\"progress\\": 0.75\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\"next_steps\\": [\\"string\\"]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 7. Deployment Strategy\\n- Containerized with Docker\\n- Deployed alongside existing Ensemble UI\\n- Uses existing authentication mechanisms\\n\\n## 8. Testing Strategy\\n### Backend\\n- Unit tests for SDLC phase detection\\n- Integration tests for API endpoints\\n- Error handling and edge case coverage\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- Component rendering tests (Jest)\\n- Interaction tests (React Testing Library)\\n- API service mocking\\n- State management tests\\n\\n## 9. Risks and Mitigations\\n1. **Incomplete Project Data**\\n   - Mitigation: Graceful UI handling, default states\\n2. **SDLC Phase Detection Accuracy**\\n   - Mitigation: Flexible keyword-based detection, manual override capability\\n3. **Performance with Large Project Sets**\\n   - Mitigation: Implement pagination, lazy loading\\n\\n## 10. Open Questions\\n- How granular should milestone tracking be?\\n- Preferences for SDLC phase visual representation?\\n- Desired level of \\"Continue\\" action customization?\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n1. Microservices Architecture: Rejected due to unnecessary complexity\\n2. Redux for State Management: Premature optimization\\n3. Static Phase Definitions: Chose flexible, inference-based approach\\n\\n**Recommended Next Steps**:\\n1. Review architecture proposal\\n2. Validate technical approach\\n3. Confirm design meets business requirements\\n4. Proceed with implementation"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MZ8Wnk8sYuF4y3YwQiz4W1', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ai_provider_enhancement_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MZ8Wnk8sYuF4y3YwQiz4W1', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Requirements: Ensemble AI Provider Enhancement System\\n\\n## Vision\\nEnhance the ensemble system to support local CLI-based AI providers (Claude CLI, ChatGPT CLI) as preferred alternatives to direct API calls, implement comprehensive cost estimation and tracking, enable intelligent agent-task routing based on performance metrics, and resume previously paused work across 10 stalled projects.\\n\\n## Executive Summary\\nThis project addresses four key user needs:\\n1. **Local CLI Providers**: Use locally installed Claude/ChatGPT CLI tools as API substitutes, with preference for local tools when available and functional\\n2. **Cost Estimation**: Comprehensive pre-execution cost estimation and post-execution tracking\\n3. **Smart Agent Routing**: Data-driven routing to match agents with suitable work based on historical performance\\n4. **Work Resume**: Restart 10 previously stalled projects that were paused due to API credit issues\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n### O1: Local CLI Provider Integration\\n- Detect locally installed Claude CLI (`/opt/homebrew/bin/claude` - confirmed present)\\n- Detect locally installed ChatGPT CLI (if available)\\n- Create adapter layer to use CLI tools as API substitutes\\n- Prefer CLI tools over API when available and functional\\n- Track success/failure statistics for CLI providers on metrics dashboard\\n\\n### O2: Cost Estimation Enhancement\\n- Pre-execution cost estimates based on task complexity and model selection\\n- Real-time cost tracking during execution\\n- Post-execution cost reporting\\n- Cost aggregation by project, agent type, and time period\\n- Cost visibility in metrics dashboard\\n\\n### O3: Intelligent Agent Routing\\n- Analyze historical agent performance data from metrics.db\\n- Route tasks to agents with best success rates for similar work\\n- Consider agent specialization (e.g., code_writer for code, tester for tests)\\n- Factor in cost efficiency when making routing decisions\\n- Provide routing recommendations with explanations\\n\\n### O4: Resume Paused Work\\n- Restart 10 stalled projects identified in task_recovery_analysis.md\\n- Sequential processing with independent error boundaries\\n- Generate recovery report documenting success/failure per project\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n#### Feature 1: CLI Provider Adapter System\\n- Auto-detect installed CLI tools on system startup\\n- Abstract provider interface supporting both API and CLI execution\\n- CLI provider for Claude (using `claude --print` or equivalent flags)\\n- CLI provider for ChatGPT (if available)\\n- Fallback chain: CLI \\u2192 API \\u2192 Error\\n- Provider health checks and availability testing\\n- Success/failure metrics per provider in dashboard\\n\\n#### Feature 2: Cost Estimation Module\\n- Pre-execution cost estimator based on:\\n  - Selected model (from model_selector.py)\\n  - Estimated input tokens (from prompt size)\\n  - Estimated output tokens (from task type heuristics)\\n- Cost tracking integration with existing cost_calculator.py\\n- Cost aggregation and reporting APIs\\n- Dashboard widgets for cost visualization\\n- Project-level cost attribution\\n\\n#### Feature 3: Smart Agent Router\\n- Performance analytics from metrics.db\\n- Agent-task matching algorithm considering:\\n  - Historical success rate per agent type\\n  - Task complexity vs agent capability\\n  - Cost efficiency per agent\\n  - Recent error patterns\\n- Routing recommendation API\\n- Override capability for manual agent selection\\n\\n#### Feature 4: Project Recovery Orchestration\\n- Parse task_recovery_analysis.md for 10 stalled projects\\n- Categorize by priority:\\n  - Priority 1: 3 in_progress tasks (likely stalled)\\n  - Priority 2: 5 todo tasks (not started)\\n  - Priority 3: 2 projects with no tasks\\n- Execute recovery sequentially\\n- Generate comprehensive recovery report\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Custom CLI tool development (use existing tools)\\n- Real-time API cost limits/caps (future enhancement)\\n- Parallel recovery execution (sequential for V1)\\n- CLI tool installation automation\\n\\n## Technical Design Overview\\n\\n### F1: CLI Provider Adapter\\n\\n#### Architecture\\n```\\n\\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510\\n\\u2502              AgentRuntime.execute()             \\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u252c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518\\n                      \\u2502\\n                      \\u25bc\\n\\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510\\n\\u2502           AIProviderManager (New)               \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510   \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502 detect_providers()                       \\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502 get_best_provider(model, task)           \\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502 execute(provider, prompt, model)         \\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518   \\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u252c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518\\n          \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u250