{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 03:00:37", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-b18094ce-06de-4c6e-98bb-af24c7b243d7', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ensemble_system_analysis_requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Ensemble Agent System Improvements",\n  "project_id": "6d864741",\n  "task_id": "1ca26aa2"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01LBWA95Ag7SA8J6SdzywKjx', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ensemble_system_analysis_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01LBWA95Ag7SA8J6SdzywKjx', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble Agent System Analysis & Improvement Requirements\\n\\n## Executive Summary\\n\\nThis document analyzes the Ensemble multi-agent system architecture and identifies the top 3 improvements that would make agents more effective. The analysis is based on reviewing the codebase, agent definitions, and system architecture.\\n\\n## Project Vision\\n\\nAnalyze the ensemble agent system to identify and implement the three most impactful improvements that will enhance agent effectiveness, reduce coordination failures, and improve overall system reliability.\\n\\n## Current System Analysis\\n\\n### Architecture Overview\\n- **Agent Hierarchy**: 4 tiers (Leadership \\u2192 Coordinators \\u2192 Developers/Testers \\u2192 Writers)\\n- **Total Agents**: 16 agents (consolidated from 23, 30% reduction)\\n- **Core Technology**: Anthropic Claude API with hierarchical delegation\\n- **Key Features**: TDD workflow, permission system, state persistence\\n\\n### Identified Issues\\n\\nAfter analyzing the codebase and agent definitions, the following problems were identified:\\n\\n#### 1. **Lack of Real-Time Progress Feedback**\\n- **Problem**: Agents execute in background threads without granular progress updates\\n- **Impact**: Users don\'t know what agents are doing, causing uncertainty about system status\\n- **Evidence**: \\n  - `main.py` uses background threads for execution (line 79)\\n  - WebSocket broadcasts only top-level status changes\\n  - No intermediate progress reporting during long-running agent operations\\n  - No visibility into which sub-agents are currently active\\n\\n#### 2. **Inadequate Error Recovery & Context Preservation**\\n- **Problem**: When agents fail, there\'s no automatic retry logic or context preservation for resume\\n- **Impact**: Single failures cascade, wasting tokens and requiring manual intervention\\n- **Evidence**:\\n  - State persistence exists (`state.py`) but resume logic is incomplete (line 64 in `runtime.py`: \\"Full resume with conversation history would need message reconstruction\\")\\n  - No retry logic in `runtime.py` when tool execution fails\\n  - Failed spawns don\'t preserve parent agent context for debugging\\n  - Agent state checkpoints exist but aren\'t used for automatic recovery\\n\\n#### 3. **Missing Agent Performance Metrics & Feedback Loops**\\n- **Problem**: No tracking of agent effectiveness, token usage, or success rates\\n- **Impact**: Can\'t identify which agents need improvement or optimization\\n- **Evidence**:\\n  - No analytics collection in `AgentRuntime`\\n  - No metrics on spawn success/failure rates\\n  - No token usage tracking per agent type\\n  - No performance comparison between model tiers\\n  - README acknowledges this gap: \\"Phase 3: Self-Improvement\\" includes \\"Agent performance analytics\\"\\n\\n### Additional Observations\\n- \\u2705 **Strengths**: Strong permission system, clear hierarchy, rogue agent prevention working well\\n- \\u2705 **Strengths**: TDD workflow is well-designed\\n- \\u26a0\\ufe0f **Minor Issue**: Model selection is static (could be adaptive based on task success)\\n- \\u26a0\\ufe0f **Minor Issue**: Agent definitions in markdown could benefit from validation schema\\n\\n## Top 3 Improvements (Prioritized)\\n\\n### Improvement #1: Real-Time Agent Progress Streaming \\n**Priority**: HIGH  \\n**Complexity**: Medium  \\n**Impact**: High (dramatically improves user experience)\\n\\n**Description**: Implement granular progress tracking and streaming for agent execution, allowing users to see:\\n- Current agent activity (which agent is thinking/executing)\\n- Tool invocations in real-time\\n- Sub-agent spawn events\\n- Iteration progress (current/max)\\n- Streaming responses from Claude API\\n\\n**Requirements**:\\n1. Enhance `AgentRuntime` to emit progress events during execution\\n2. Add event bus or callback system for progress notifications\\n3. Update WebSocket handler to stream progress events to frontend\\n4. Add progress tracking to spawned agent execution\\n5. Include tool execution progress (start/complete/fail)\\n6. Show model selection decisions in progress feed\\n\\n**Success Criteria**:\\n- Users can see which agent is active at any moment\\n- Tool invocations appear in real-time\\n- Spawn events are visible with parent-child relationships\\n- WebSocket clients receive progress updates < 500ms after events\\n- No performance degradation (< 5% overhead)\\n\\n### Improvement #2: Automatic Error Recovery & Context Preservation\\n**Priority**: HIGH  \\n**Complexity**: High  \\n**Impact**: High (reduces wasted tokens, improves reliability)\\n\\n**Description**: Implement intelligent error recovery with automatic retries and full context preservation for resume after failures.\\n\\n**Requirements**:\\n1. Complete state manager resume functionality (message reconstruction)\\n2. Add retry logic with exponential backoff for transient failures\\n3. Implement context preservation for spawned agents (parent context + partial results)\\n4. Add automatic checkpoint validation and rollback\\n5. Create error classification system (retryable vs. fatal)\\n6. Preserve tool execution results across retries\\n\\n**Success Criteria**:\\n- Agents can resume from last checkpoint after crashes\\n- Transient API errors (rate limits, timeouts) trigger automatic retry\\n- Failed spawns preserve parent agent state for debugging\\n- Context includes: conversation history, tool results, spawned agent data\\n- Recovery success rate > 80% for retryable errors\\n- Zero token waste on successful recovery (resume from checkpoint)\\n\\n### Improvement #3: Agent Performance Analytics & Adaptive Optimization\\n**Priority**: MEDIUM  \\n**Complexity**: Medium  \\n**Impact**: Medium-High (enables continuous improvement)\\n\\n**Description**: Implement comprehensive analytics tracking for agent performance with adaptive model selection based on historical success rates.\\n\\n**Requirements**:\\n1. Track metrics per agent instance:\\n   - Token usage (input/output)\\n   - Execution time\\n   - Success/failure rates\\n   - Iteration count vs. max iterations\\n   - Tool invocation patterns\\n2. Aggregate metrics by agent type and model tier\\n3. Create analytics dashboard endpoint for reporting\\n4. Implement adaptive model selection:\\n   - Start with budget tier default\\n   - Upgrade model if agent fails repeatedly\\n   - Downgrade model if agent consistently succeeds quickly\\n5. Add performance comparison reports (model A vs. model B for same task)\\n6. Export metrics for analysis (JSON, CSV)\\n\\n**Success Criteria**:\\n- All agent executions tracked with complete metrics\\n- Analytics API returns per-agent and aggregate statistics\\n- Adaptive model selection improves success rate by 15%+\\n- Token usage optimization reduces costs by 10%+\\n- Reports identify underperforming agents for refinement\\n- Metrics persist across system restarts\\n\\n## Out of Scope (For This Phase)\\n\\nThe following are important but not in the top 3:\\n- Enhanced TDD workflow validation\\n- File exploration agents\\n- Multi-user support\\n- Agent definition schema validation\\n- Performance profiling tools\\n- Cost prediction before execution\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n1. **Must maintain backward compatibility** with existing agent definitions\\n2. **Must not break permission system** (can_write_code, can_write_tests enforcement)\\n3. **Must not increase API costs** by more than 10%\\n4. **Must support concurrent agent execution** (multi-user eventually)\\n5. **Must preserve existing state file format** (add extensions, don\'t replace)\\n\\n## Success Criteria (Overall)\\n\\n1. \\u2705 Real-time progress visible to users\\n2. \\u2705 Error recovery succeeds > 80% for retryable failures\\n3. \\u2705 Performance metrics tracked for all agents\\n4. \\u2705 All existing tests continue to pass\\n5. \\u2705 Documentation updated for new features\\n6. \\u2705 Zero breaking changes to agent definitions\\n\\n## Implementation Priority\\n\\n**Phase 1: Progress Streaming** (Implement First)\\n- High user impact\\n- Medium complexity\\n- Foundation for other improvements\\n\\n**Phase 2: Error Recovery** (Implement Second)\\n- High reliability impact\\n- High complexity (needs Phase 1 for monitoring)\\n- Builds on state persistence system\\n\\n**Phase 3: Performance Analytics** (Implement Third)\\n- Enables long-term improvement\\n- Medium complexity\\n- Leverages data from Phase 1 & 2\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. Updated `AgentRuntime` class with progress events\\n2. Enhanced `StateManager` with full resume capability\\n3. New `AgentAnalytics` module for metrics tracking\\n4. Updated WebSocket handlers for streaming\\n5. New API endpoints for analytics queries\\n6. Updated documentation (README, implementation guide)\\n7. Test suite covering new functionality\\n8. Performance benchmarks before/after\\n\\n## Timeline Estimate\\n\\n- **Improvement #1**: 2-3 days (progress streaming)\\n- **Improvement #2**: 3-4 days (error recovery)\\n- **Improvement #3**: 2-3 days (analytics)\\n- **Testing & Documentation**: 1-2 days\\n- **Total**: 8-12 days for complete implementation\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\nThis analysis prioritizes improvements that:\\n1. **Maximize user value** (progress feedback eliminates uncertainty)\\n2. **Improve system reliability** (error recovery reduces failures)\\n3. **Enable continuous improvement** (analytics identify what to optimize next)\\n\\nThe three improvements are complementary and build on each other, creating a more robust and observable agent system.\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015xzKCeGzRFmyYvybEnFLB7', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Ensemble Agent System Improvements', 'description': 'Implement top 3 improvements for ensemble agent system: real-time progress streaming, error recovery & context preservation, and performance analytics with adaptive optimization'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_015xzKCeGzRFmyYvybEnFLB7', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "afd87a9e", "message": "Created project: Ensemble Agent System Improvements", "summary": {"project_id": "afd87a9e", "project_name": "Ensemble Agent System Improvements", "description": "Implement top 3 improvements for ensemble agent system: real-time progress streaming, error recovery & context preservation, and performance analytics with adaptive optimization", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T02:58:09.656543", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T02:58:09.656543", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T02:58:09.656543", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Ensemble Agent System Improvements\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_012XmvY3pMZ2uq3HKQcEbDjN', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Ensemble Agent System Improvements - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\n**Project**: Ensemble Agent System Improvements  \n**Project ID**: afd87a9e  \n**Total Duration**: 8-12 days  \n**Goal**: Implement the top 3 improvements to enhance agent effectiveness, reduce coordination failures, and improve system reliability\n\n## Milestone 1: Real-Time Agent Progress Streaming\n**Duration**: 2-3 days  \n**Priority**: HIGH  \n**Phase**: Foundation\n\n### Objective\nImplement granular progress tracking and streaming for agent execution, giving users real-time visibility into agent activities.\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Enhanced `AgentRuntime` class with progress event emission\n2. Event bus/callback system for progress notifications  \n3. Updated WebSocket handler for streaming progress to frontend\n4. Progress tracking for spawned agent execution\n5. Tool execution progress monitoring (start/complete/fail)\n6. Model selection decision visibility in progress feed\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- ✅ Users can see which agent is active at any moment\n- ✅ Tool invocations appear in real-time\n- ✅ Spawn events visible with parent-child relationships  \n- ✅ WebSocket clients receive updates < 500ms after events\n- ✅ Performance overhead < 5%\n- ✅ All existing tests continue to pass\n\n### Dependencies\n- None (foundational milestone)\n\n### Technical Focus\n- Enhance `/src/ensemble/runtime.py` AgentRuntime class\n- Update WebSocket handlers in `/src/ensemble/main.py`\n- Add event emission points throughout agent execution lifecycle\n- Implement progress state management\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 2: Automatic Error Recovery & Context Preservation\n**Duration**: 3-4 days  \n**Priority**: HIGH  \n**Phase**: Reliability Enhancement\n\n### Objective\nImplement intelligent error recovery with automatic retries and full context preservation for resume after failures.\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Complete state manager resume functionality (message reconstruction)\n2. Retry logic with exponential backoff for transient failures\n3. Context preservation for spawned agents (parent context + partial results)\n4. Automatic checkpoint validation and rollback\n5. Error classification system (retryable vs. fatal)\n6. Tool execution result preservation across retries\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- ✅ Agents can resume from last checkpoint after crashes\n- ✅ Transient API errors trigger automatic retry\n- ✅ Failed spawns preserve parent agent state for debugging\n- ✅ Context includes: conversation history, tool results, spawned agent data\n- ✅ Recovery success rate > 80% for retryable errors\n- ✅ Zero token waste on successful recovery\n\n### Dependencies\n- Milestone 1 (progress monitoring for recovery status)\n\n### Technical Focus\n- Complete `/src/ensemble/state.py` StateManager resume functionality\n- Enhance `/src/ensemble/runtime.py` with retry logic\n- Add error classification and recovery strategies\n- Implement checkpoint validation system\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 3: Agent Performance Analytics & Adaptive Optimization\n**Duration**: 2-3 days  \n**Priority**: MEDIUM  \n**Phase**: Optimization & Intelligence\n\n### Objective\nImplement comprehensive analytics tracking with adaptive model selection based on historical success rates.\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Agent metrics tracking system (token usage, execution time, success rates)\n2. Aggregated metrics by agent type and model tier\n3. Analytics dashboard endpoint for reporting\n4. Adaptive model selection implementation\n5. Performance comparison reports (model A vs B)\n6. Metrics export functionality (JSON, CSV)\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- ✅ All agent executions tracked with complete metrics\n- ✅ Analytics API returns per-agent and aggregate statistics\n- ✅ Adaptive model selection improves success rate by 15%+\n- ✅ Token usage optimization reduces costs by 10%+\n- ✅ Reports identify underperforming agents for refinement\n- ✅ Metrics persist across system restarts\n\n### Dependencies\n- Milestone 1 (progress data for metrics)\n- Milestone 2 (recovery data for success rates)\n\n### Technical Focus\n- Create new `AgentAnalytics` module\n- Add metrics collection throughout agent lifecycle\n- Implement adaptive model selection logic\n- Build analytics API endpoints\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 4: Testing, Documentation & Integration\n**Duration**: 1-2 days  \n**Priority**: HIGH  \n**Phase**: Quality Assurance\n\n### Objective\nComplete comprehensive testing, update documentation, and ensure seamless integration of all improvements.\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Test suite covering all new functionality\n2. Performance benchmarks (before/after comparison)\n3. Updated documentation (README, implementation guide)\n4. Integration testing across all three improvements\n5. Final system validation and optimization\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- ✅ 100% test coverage for new functionality\n- ✅ All existing tests continue to pass\n- ✅ Performance benchmarks show improvement\n- ✅ Documentation accurately reflects new capabilities\n- ✅ System ready for production deployment\n\n### Dependencies\n- Milestones 1, 2, 3 (all improvements implemented)\n\n### Technical Focus\n- Comprehensive testing across all modules\n- Performance validation and optimization\n- Documentation updates and examples\n- Final integration testing\n\n---\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n\n### High Risk Items\n1. **API Rate Limits**: Implement proper backoff and retry logic\n2. **State Corruption**: Add validation and rollback mechanisms  \n3. **Performance Regression**: Continuous monitoring during development\n4. **Backward Compatibility**: Maintain existing agent definition format\n\n### Mitigation Strategies\n- Incremental implementation with rollback capability\n- Extensive testing at each milestone\n- Performance monitoring throughout development\n- Staged deployment approach\n\n---\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n### User Experience\n- Real-time progress visibility (Milestone 1)\n- Reduced failure rates through recovery (Milestone 2)\n- Improved system performance through optimization (Milestone 3)\n\n### Technical Metrics  \n- Error recovery success rate > 80%\n- Progress update latency < 500ms\n- Token usage optimization > 10% cost reduction\n- Agent success rate improvement > 15%\n\n### Quality Assurance\n- Zero breaking changes to existing functionality\n- 100% test coverage for new features\n- Performance overhead < 5%\n- Documentation completeness score > 95%\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Begin Milestone 1: Progress Streaming implementation\n2. Set up development environment and testing framework\n3. Start with AgentRuntime enhancement for event emission\n4. Implement WebSocket streaming for progress updates'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_012XmvY3pMZ2uq3HKQcEbDjN', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_025842.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_025842.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011BSJpgVDfxbwxE7gL3o18r', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Us