{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 03:00:52", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-94108f76-d95d-4ee2-afe0-4269b9dd60ca', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Milestone 1: CLI Provider Integration - Implement CLI provider adapter system that detects and uses locally installed Claude CLI and ChatGPT CLI tools as preferred API alternatives.",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ai_provider_enhancement_milestones.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0134R46ykKud3FDrVHigqLyW', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0134R46ykKud3FDrVHigqLyW', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Project View Dashboard - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## A. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Architectural Pattern: Modular Single Page Application (SPA)\\n- Frontend: React-based component-driven architecture\\n- Backend: Python Flask microservices\\n- State Management: Redux for complex UI state\\n- Communication: RESTful API with WebSocket support for real-time updates\\n\\n### Core Design Principles\\n- Modularity: Each component has a single, well-defined responsibility\\n- Scalability: Loosely coupled components that can be independently developed\\n- Performance: Minimal payload, efficient data fetching\\n- Extensibility: Easy to add new project tracking features\\n\\n## B. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **Framework**: React 18\\n- **State Management**: Redux Toolkit\\n- **UI Components**: React Bootstrap\\n- **Routing**: React Router\\n- **HTTP Client**: Axios\\n- **Testing**: Jest, React Testing Library\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\\n- **Web Framework**: Flask\\n- **API Design**: Flask-RESTful\\n- **Authentication**: JWT (Flask-JWT-Extended)\\n- **Database Access**: SQLAlchemy\\n- **WebSocket**: Flask-SocketIO\\n\\n### Infrastructure\\n- **Containerization**: Docker\\n- **Orchestration**: Docker Compose\\n- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions\\n- **Deployment**: Kubernetes (optional scaling)\\n\\n## C. System Components\\n\\n### Frontend Components\\n1. **ProjectViewContainer**\\n   - Manages overall project view layout\\n   - Handles project selection and data loading\\n   - Renders child components\\n\\n2. **ProjectListPanel**\\n   - Displays list of projects\\n   - Handles project selection\\n   - Filters and searches projects\\n\\n3. **ProjectStatusCard**\\n   - Shows project metadata\\n   - Displays status badges\\n   - Shows timestamps\\n\\n4. **SDLCIndicator**\\n   - Visualizes current SDLC phase\\n   - Provides phase progression tracking\\n\\n5. **MilestoneTracker**\\n   - Displays milestone progress\\n   - Shows completion percentages\\n   - Renders milestone details\\n\\n6. **NextStepsPanel**\\n   - Lists actionable next steps\\n   - Shows task assignments\\n   - Provides \\"Continue\\" functionality\\n\\n### Backend Services\\n1. **ProjectService**\\n   - Retrieves project details\\n   - Manages project lifecycle\\n   - Handles project continuation requests\\n\\n2. **MilestoneService**\\n   - Tracks milestone progress\\n   - Calculates milestone statistics\\n   - Updates milestone status\\n\\n3. **AgentActivityService**\\n   - Retrieves agent activities\\n   - Tracks running agents\\n   - Provides agent hierarchy information\\n\\n## D. File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nensemble_ui/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ProjectView/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ProjectListPanel.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ProjectStatusCard.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 SDLCIndicator.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 MilestoneTracker.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 NextStepsPanel.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 common/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 redux/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 projectSlice.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 milestoneSlice.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 apiService.js\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 App.jsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 package.json\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 backend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 project_service.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 milestone_service.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 agent_activity_service.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 models/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 project.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 milestone.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 routes/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 project_routes.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 app.py\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 docker-compose.yml\\n```\\n\\n## E. Data Model\\n\\n### Project Model\\n```python\\nclass Project:\\n    id: str\\n    name: str\\n    description: str\\n    status: ProjectStatus\\n    sdlc_phase: SDLCPhase\\n    created_at: datetime\\n    updated_at: datetime\\n    milestones: List[Milestone]\\n    tasks: List[Task]\\n```\\n\\n### Milestone Model\\n```python\\nclass Milestone:\\n    id: str\\n    name: str\\n    status: MilestoneStatus\\n    started_at: datetime\\n    completed_at: datetime\\n    tasks: List[Task]\\n```\\n\\n## F. API Design\\n\\n### Project Endpoints\\n- `GET /api/projects` - List projects\\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}` - Get project details\\n- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/continue` - Continue project\\n\\n### Response Examples\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"project_id\\": \\"proj_123\\",\\n  \\"name\\": \\"AI Research Platform\\",\\n  \\"status\\": \\"active\\",\\n  \\"sdlc_phase\\": \\"architecture\\",\\n  \\"milestones\\": [\\n    {\\"name\\": \\"Design\\", \\"status\\": \\"completed\\"},\\n    {\\"name\\": \\"Implementation\\", \\"status\\": \\"in_progress\\"}\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## G. Deployment Strategy\\n- Docker containers for frontend and backend\\n- Nginx as reverse proxy\\n- Optional Kubernetes for horizontal scaling\\n- Environment-specific configuration management\\n\\n## H. Testing Strategy\\n- Unit Tests: \\n  - Frontend: Jest for React components\\n  - Backend: pytest for Python services\\n- Integration Tests: \\n  - API endpoint testing\\n  - Database interaction validation\\n- E2E Tests: Cypress for critical user flows\\n\\n## I. Alternatives Considered\\n1. **GraphQL vs REST**\\n   - Chose REST for simplicity and existing infrastructure\\n   - GraphQL would provide more flexible querying\\n2. **Redux vs Context API**\\n   - Redux chosen for complex state management\\n   - Provides better debugging and middleware support\\n\\n## J. Risks and Mitigations\\n- **Risk**: Inconsistent project tracking\\n  - **Mitigation**: Robust data validation, default states\\n- **Risk**: Performance with large projects\\n  - **Mitigation**: Pagination, lazy loading, caching\\n\\n## K. Open Questions\\n- Precise mechanism for \\"Continue to Next Step\\"\\n- Handling edge cases in project progression\\n- Long-term data retention strategy\\n\\n## Conclusion\\nA modular, scalable architecture that meets the Project View Dashboard requirements while providing flexibility for future enhancements."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01H8B4nzVS1fkMPnX7iLz4vw', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/ai_provider_enhancement_milestones.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01H8B4nzVS1fkMPnX7iLz4vw', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# AI Provider Enhancement System - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Project ID**: 3cd35d78\\n**Created**: 2026-01-13\\n**Status**: Planning\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 1: CLI Provider Integration\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: Highest\\n\\n### Objective\\nImplement CLI provider adapter system that detects and uses locally installed Claude CLI and ChatGPT CLI tools as preferred API alternatives.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `provider_manager.py` - AI provider abstraction and detection system\\n2. `cli_provider.py` - CLI provider implementations for Claude and ChatGPT\\n3. Updated `runtime.py` - Integration with provider manager\\n4. Unit tests for provider detection and execution\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Claude CLI at `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude` is detected automatically\\n- [ ] CLI provider executes prompts using `claude --print` flag\\n- [ ] Graceful fallback to Anthropic API when CLI unavailable\\n- [ ] Provider success/failure metrics tracked in database\\n- [ ] No increase in execution latency >10%\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Existing runtime.py infrastructure\\n- Claude CLI installed at `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 2: Cost Estimation Module\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n### Objective\\nImplement comprehensive pre-execution cost estimation and post-execution cost tracking with dashboard integration.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `cost_estimator.py` - Pre-execution cost estimation based on task complexity\\n2. Enhanced `cost_calculator.py` - Extended with estimation capabilities\\n3. Updated `metrics.py` - Cost tracking fields and aggregation queries\\n4. Cost API endpoints for dashboard\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Pre-execution cost estimates available before spawning agents\\n- [ ] Estimates within 50% of actual costs\\n- [ ] Cost aggregation by project, agent type, and time period\\n- [ ] Cost fields added to agent_executions table\\n- [ ] API endpoints expose cost data to dashboard\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 1 (provider tracking needed for CLI vs API cost differentiation)\\n- Existing cost_calculator.py\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 3: Smart Agent Router\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: Medium-High\\n\\n### Objective\\nImplement intelligent agent-task routing based on historical performance metrics.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `agent_router.py` - Performance analysis and routing recommendations\\n2. Updated agent execution flow to use router recommendations\\n3. Routing analytics API endpoints\\n4. Dashboard widget for routing explanations\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Agent recommendations based on historical performance from metrics.db\\n- [ ] Routing considers success rate (50%), cost efficiency (30%), speed (20%)\\n- [ ] Agent specialization bonuses applied (e.g., code_writer +10% for code tasks)\\n- [ ] Override capability for manual agent selection\\n- [ ] 10% improvement in overall success rate (measurable after deployment)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 2 (cost data needed for cost efficiency calculations)\\n- Populated metrics.db with historical data\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 4: Project Recovery & Dashboard Integration\\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\\n**Priority**: Medium\\n\\n### Objective\\nRestart 10 stalled projects and integrate all new features into the dashboard.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. `recovery_orchestrator.py` - Project recovery logic\\n2. Recovery execution report\\n3. Dashboard integration for provider, cost, and routing features\\n4. Updated frontend components\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] All 10 stalled projects attempted for restart\\n- [ ] Recovery report generated with outcomes per project\\n- [ ] Independent error boundaries (one failure doesn\'t stop others)\\n- [ ] Dashboard shows provider usage, cost trends, routing info\\n- [ ] Provider success rates visible in dashboard\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestones 1-3 completed\\n- Access to project tracking system\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone Summary\\n\\n| Milestone | Objective | Duration | Dependencies |\\n|-----------|-----------|----------|--------------|\\n| 1 | CLI Provider Integration | 2-3 days | None |\\n| 2 | Cost Estimation Module | 2-3 days | Milestone 1 |\\n| 3 | Smart Agent Router | 2-3 days | Milestone 2 |\\n| 4 | Project Recovery & Dashboard | 2-3 days | Milestones 1-3 |\\n\\n**Total Estimated Duration**: 8-12 days\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Technical Decisions Made\\n\\n### TD1: Provider Selection Strategy\\n- **Decision**: CLI preferred over API when available\\n- **Rationale**: CLI tools use user\'s existing subscription, avoiding API costs\\n\\n### TD2: Cost Estimation Approach\\n- **Decision**: Use task complexity heuristics for output token estimation\\n- **Rationale**: More accurate than fixed estimates, calibrated to task types\\n\\n### TD3: Routing Algorithm Weights\\n- **Decision**: 50% success rate, 30% cost efficiency, 20% speed\\n- **Rationale**: Reliability most important, then cost, then speed\\n\\n### TD4: Recovery Sequence\\n- **Decision**: Sequential processing, not parallel\\n- **Rationale**: Easier debugging, independent error boundaries, API rate limits\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Files to Create\\n- `src/runtime/agents/provider_manager.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/cli_provider.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/cost_estimator.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/agent_router.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/recovery_orchestrator.py`\\n\\n## Files to Modify\\n- `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\\n- `src/runtime/agents/metrics.py`\\n- `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py`\\n- `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/App.jsx`\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Document Status**: Complete\\n**Next Step**: System Architecture\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01ExPKNc5QN15GgJQftmCXJE', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Test Strategy - Milestone 1: CLI Provider Integration\n\n## Overview\n**Milestone**: CLI Provider Integration - Implement CLI provider adapter system that detects and uses locally installed Claude CLI and ChatGPT CLI tools as preferred API alternatives.\n\n**Testing Philosophy**: Comprehensive test coverage for provider detection, CLI execution, fallback mechanisms, and performance characteristics.\n\n## Test Coverage Goals\n- **Unit Test Coverage**: 85%+ for business logic\n- **Integration Test Coverage**: 100% of provider workflows  \n- **E2E Test Coverage**: Critical provider selection and execution paths\n\n## Test Categories\n\n### 1. Unit Tests\n\n#### 1.1 Provider Manager Tests\n**File**: `tests/unit/test_provider_manager.py`\n**Target**: `provider_manager.py`\n**Coverage**: Provider detection, selection logic, configuration\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_detect_claude_cli_present()` - Claude CLI found at expected path\n- `test_detect_claude_cli_missing()` - Claude CLI not installed\n- `test_detect_chatgpt_cli_present()` - ChatGPT CLI found and executable\n- `test_detect_chatgpt_cli_missing()` - ChatGPT CLI not available\n- `test_provider_selection_preference()` - CLI preferred over API when available\n- `test_provider_fallback_logic()` - API fallback when CLI fails\n- `test_provider_config_validation()` - Configuration parameter validation\n- `test_provider_health_check()` - Provider availability verification\n\n#### 1.2 CLI Provider Tests\n**File**: `tests/unit/test_cli_provider.py`\n**Target**: `cli_provider.py`\n**Coverage**: CLI execution, error handling, response parsing\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_claude_cli_execution_success()` - Successful Claude CLI prompt execution\n- `test_claude_cli_execution_failure()` - CLI execution errors handled gracefully\n- `test_claude_cli_timeout_handling()` - Long-running CLI commands timeout properly\n- `test_chatgpt_cli_execution_success()` - ChatGPT CLI execution with correct flags\n- `test_cli_output_parsing()` - CLI response parsing and formatting\n- `test_cli_command_construction()` - Proper CLI command building\n- `test_cli_environment_setup()` - Environment variables and paths configured\n- `test_cli_security_validation()` - Input sanitization for CLI commands\n\n#### 1.3 Runtime Integration Tests\n**File**: `tests/unit/test_runtime_provider_integration.py`\n**Target**: Updated `runtime.py`\n**Coverage**: Provider manager integration with existing runtime\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_runtime_provider_initialization()` - Provider manager setup in runtime\n- `test_runtime_provider_selection()` - Provider chosen correctly for agent spawn\n- `test_runtime_fallback_behavior()` - Graceful fallback when provider fails\n- `test_runtime_metrics_tracking()` - Provider usage metrics recorded\n- `test_runtime_performance_impact()` - No significant latency increase\n\n### 2. Integration Tests\n\n#### 2.1 Provider Detection Integration\n**File**: `tests/integration/test_provider_detection.py`\n**Coverage**: End-to-end provider detection in real environment\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_full_provider_detection_cycle()` - Complete detection process\n- `test_provider_detection_with_filesystem()` - Real filesystem path checking\n- `test_provider_detection_with_permissions()` - Execute permission validation\n- `test_provider_detection_caching()` - Detection results cached appropriately\n\n#### 2.2 CLI Execution Integration\n**File**: `tests/integration/test_cli_execution.py`\n**Coverage**: Real CLI execution with mocked external dependencies\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_claude_cli_real_execution()` - Execute actual CLI commands (mocked responses)\n- `test_cli_execution_with_large_prompts()` - Handle large prompt inputs\n- `test_cli_execution_concurrent_requests()` - Multiple simultaneous CLI calls\n- `test_cli_execution_error_scenarios()` - Various CLI failure modes\n\n#### 2.3 Database Integration Tests\n**File**: `tests/integration/test_provider_metrics_db.py`\n**Coverage**: Provider metrics storage and retrieval\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_provider_success_metrics_stored()` - Success metrics saved to database\n- `test_provider_failure_metrics_stored()` - Failure metrics recorded properly\n- `test_provider_performance_metrics()` - Execution time tracking\n- `test_provider_metrics_aggregation()` - Metrics queried and aggregated correctly\n\n### 3. End-to-End Tests\n\n#### 3.1 Provider Selection E2E\n**File**: `tests/e2e/test_provider_selection_flow.py`\n**Coverage**: Complete user journey with provider selection\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_agent_spawn_with_cli_provider()` - Agent spawned using CLI provider\n- `test_agent_spawn_with_api_fallback()` - Fallback to API when CLI unavailable\n- `test_provider_preference_respected()` - CLI used when both CLI and API available\n\n#### 3.2 Performance E2E Tests\n**File**: `tests/e2e/test_provider_performance.py`\n**Coverage**: Performance characteristics under realistic load\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_cli_provider_latency_acceptable()` - CLI execution within latency limits\n- `test_provider_switching_performance()` - Fast switching between providers\n- `test_high_load_provider_stability()` - Stable under concurrent requests\n\n## Test Infrastructure\n\n### 3.1 Test Fixtures\n**File**: `tests/fixtures/provider_fixtures.py`\n\n**Mock CLI Executables**:\n- Mock Claude CLI that returns predefined responses\n- Mock ChatGPT CLI with configurable behavior\n- Filesystem fixtures with various CLI installation states\n\n**Database Fixtures**:\n- Clean metrics database for each test\n- Pre-populated provider usage data\n- Test-specific database configurations\n\n### 3.2 Test Utilities\n**File**: `tests/utils/provider_test_utils.py`\n\n**Helper Functions**:\n- `mock_cli_environment()` - Set up controlled CLI environment\n- `assert_provider_metrics()` - Validate metrics recording\n- `create_test_agent_spawn()` - Generate test agent spawn requests\n- `measure_provider_performance()` - Performance measurement utilities\n\n## Test Data Requirements\n\n### 3.1 Mock CLI Responses\n```python\nCLAUDE_CLI_SUCCESS_RESPONSE = """\nHere is the response to your prompt:\n[Generated content here]\n"""\n\nCLAUDE_CLI_ERROR_RESPONSE = """\nError: Authentication failed\nPlease check your API key configuration\n"""\n```\n\n### 3.2 Test Scenarios\n- CLI available and functional\n- CLI available but returns errors\n- CLI not installed/not found\n- CLI installed but not executable\n- CLI times out during execution\n- Mixed provider environments\n\n## Performance Testing\n\n### 3.1 Performance Benchmarks\n**Target Metrics**:\n- Provider detection: <100ms\n- CLI execution overhead: <10% vs direct API\n- Provider switching: <50ms\n- Concurrent CLI calls: Support 5+ simultaneous\n\n**Performance Tests**:\n- `test_provider_detection_speed()` - Detection performance benchmark\n- `test_cli_execution_overhead()` - Compare CLI vs API execution time\n- `test_concurrent_cli_performance()` - Multiple simultaneous CLI calls\n- `test_memory_usage_impact()` - Memory footprint of provider system\n\n## Security Testing\n\n### 3.1 Security Test Cases\n**File**: `tests/security/test_provider_security.py`\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_cli_command_injection_prevention()` - Prevent command injection\n- `test_cli_path_traversal_prevention()` - Secure path handling\n- `test_cli_input_sanitization()` - Proper input validation\n- `test_cli_output_sanitization()` - Safe output handling\n\n## Test Automation\n\n### 3.1 CI/CD Integration\n**GitHub Actions Workflow**: `.github/workflows/milestone1_tests.yml`\n\n**Test Stages**:\n1. **Unit Tests**: Fast, isolated tests with mocks\n2. **Integration Tests**: Tests with controlled external dependencies\n3. **E2E Tests**: Full system tests with provider detection\n4. **Performance Tests**: Benchmark critical performance metrics\n\n**Test Environment**:\n- Mock CLI installations for consistent testing\n- Controlled filesystem permissions\n- Database test containers\n- Performance measurement infrastructure\n\n### 3.2 Test Coverage Requirements\n**Minimum Coverage Thresholds**:\n- `provider_manager.py`: 90%\n- `cli_provider.py`: 85%\n- Runtime integration code: 80%\n- Error handling paths: 100%\n\n## Risk Mitigation Testing\n\n### 3.1 Error Scenario Coverage\n- **CLI Process Crashes**: Ensure graceful handling and fallback\n- **CLI Not Responding**: Timeout mechanisms tested\n- **Permission Denied**: File system permission errors handled\n- **Network Issues**: API fallback when CLI has network problems\n- **Resource Exhaustion**: CLI memory/CPU limits respected\n\n### 3.2 Backward Compatibility\n- **Existing Runtime**: Ensure no regression in existing functionality\n- **API Provider**: Existing API provider continues to work unchanged\n- **Configuration**: Existing configurations remain valid\n\n## Test Execution Plan\n\n### Phase 1: Unit Tests (Day 1)\n1. Implement provider manager unit tests\n2. Implement CLI provider unit tests  \n3. Implement runtime integration unit tests\n4. Achieve 85%+ unit test coverage\n\n### Phase 2: Integration Tests (Day 2)\n1. Implement provider detection integration tests\n2. Implement CLI execution integration tests\n3. Implement database integration tests\n4. Test provider metrics recording\n\n### Phase 3: E2E & Performance Tests (Day 3)\n1. Implement end-to-end provider selection tests\n2. Implement performance benchmark tests\n3. Run security validation tests\n4. Validate all acceptance criteria through testing\n\n## Test Task Breakdown\n\n### Task 1: Unit Test Implementation\n**Assignee**: TDD Coordinator\n**Files**: \n- `tests/unit/test_provider_manager.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_cli_provider.py` \n- `tests/unit/test_runtime_provider_integration.py`\n**Acceptance**: 85%+ coverage, all unit tests pass\n\n### Task 2: Integration Test Implementation\n**Assignee**: TDD Coordinator  \n**Files**:\n- `tests/integration/test_provider_detection.py`\n- `tests/integration/test_cli_execution.py`\n- `tests/integration/test_provider_metrics_db.py`\n**Acceptance**: All provider workflows covered\n\n### Task 3: E2E Test Implementation\n**Assignee**: TDD Coordinator\n**Files**:\n- `tests/e2e/test_provider_selection_flow.py`\n- `tests/e2e/test_provider_performance.py`\n**Acceptance**: Critical paths tested end-to-end\n\n### Task 4: Test Infrastructure Setup\n**Assignee**: TDD Coordinator\n**Files**:\n- `tests/fixtures/provider_fixtures.py`\n- `tests/utils/provider_test_utils.py`\n- `.github/workflows/milestone1_tests.yml`\n**Acceptance**: Complete test infrastructure ready\n\n### Task 5: Performance & Security Testing\n**Assignee**: TDD Coordinator\n**Files**:\n- Performance benchmarks implemented\n- Security test cases covered\n- CI/CD pipeline integration complete\n**Acceptance**: All performance and security requirements validated\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n### Test Completion Criteria\n- [ ] All unit tests implemented with 85%+ coverage\n- [ ] All integration workflows tested\n- [ ] Critical E2E paths validated\n- [ ] Performance benchmarks meet targets\n- [ ] Security tests pass\n- [ ] CI/CD pipeline successfully runs all tests\n- [ ] Test documentation complete\n\n### Quality Gates\n- No test failures in CI/CD pipeline\n- Performance degradation <10%\n- All acceptance criteria validated through testing\n- Test execution time <5 mi