src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/`\\n- **Output Directory**: `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/`\\n\\n## Technical Investigation Required\\n\\n### 1. Backend Status\\n- Verify backend server is running on expected port (8001)\\n- Check if endpoint registration is correct\\n- Validate endpoint handler function exists and is accessible\\n\\n### 2. Frontend API Calls\\n- Review `getGeneratedFiles()` function in `frontend/src/services/api.js`\\n- Verify correct URL construction and parameters\\n- Check polling interval and frequency (currently set to 1000ms in App.jsx)\\n\\n### 3. Potential Root Causes\\n- Backend server not running or crashed\\n- Endpoint URL mismatch between frontend and backend\\n- CORS configuration issues\\n- Activity tracker database connectivity problems\\n- Missing dependencies or import errors in backend\\n\\n## Files to Examine\\n\\n### Backend Files\\n1. `backend/main.py` - Main FastAPI application\\n   - Line 717: `@app.get(\\"/api/activity/files\\")` endpoint definition\\n   - Activity tracker integration\\n   - Error handling\\n\\n2. Backend runtime dependencies:\\n   - `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` - Activity tracking system\\n   - `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py` - AgentRuntime class\\n\\n### Frontend Files\\n1. `frontend/src/services/api.js` - API service layer\\n   - `getGeneratedFiles()` function\\n   - API_BASE_URL configuration\\n\\n2. `frontend/src/App.jsx` - Main application component\\n   - Polling logic for file updates\\n   - Error handling display\\n\\n3. `frontend/src/components/GeneratedFiles.jsx` - Files display component\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n1. Frontend polls `/api/activity/files` endpoint at configured interval\\n2. Backend returns JSON response with generated files:\\n   ```json\\n   {\\n     \\"files\\": [...],\\n     \\"count\\": 0\\n   }\\n   ```\\n3. UI displays files in the \\"Generated Files\\" section without errors\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **No 404 errors** when frontend polls files endpoint\\n2. **Correct response format** - JSON without BOM characters\\n3. **Files displayed** in UI when agents generate outputs\\n4. **Error handling** - Graceful degradation if backend temporarily unavailable\\n5. **Logging** - Clear error messages in both frontend console and backend logs\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n- **No breaking changes** to existing API contract\\n- **Maintain backwards compatibility** with current frontend implementation\\n- **Minimal code changes** - focus on fixing the specific 404 issue\\n- **Preserve existing functionality** - don\'t break other endpoints\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n- Adding new features to file display\\n- Redesigning the UI layout\\n- Changing polling architecture to WebSockets\\n- Performance optimization beyond fixing the bug\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n- Backend is intended to run on port 8001\\n- Frontend is configured to connect to localhost:8001\\n- Activity tracker database exists and is accessible at `~/.ensemble/metrics.db`\\n- All required Python dependencies are installed\\n\\n## Acceptance Tests\\n\\n1. **Backend health check**: `curl http://localhost:8001/api/status` returns 200 OK\\n2. **Files endpoint test**: `curl http://localhost:8001/api/activity/files` returns JSON (not 404)\\n3. **Frontend test**: Open UI in browser, verify no 404 errors in console for `/api/activity/files`\\n4. **Integration test**: Generate a file via agent execution, verify it appears in UI without errors\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. **Root cause analysis** - Document why 404 was occurring\\n2. **Code fixes** - Implement solution in backend/frontend as needed\\n3. **Verification** - Test all affected endpoints work correctly\\n4. **Documentation** - Update any relevant docs about endpoint usage\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01PqVfhFj2iQRfxcUh2Edhxx', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# UI Files 404 Error Fix - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\n**Objective**: Fix 404 "Not Found" errors when frontend polls `/api/activity/files` endpoint\n**Duration**: 1-2 development cycles\n**Priority**: High (blocking user functionality)\n\n## Milestone 1: Root Cause Analysis & Backend Fix\n**Duration**: 1 development cycle\n**Objective**: Identify and fix the backend 404 issue\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. **Root cause analysis document**\n   - Backend server status verification\n   - Endpoint registration analysis\n   - Error reproduction and diagnosis\n\n2. **Backend fixes implemented**\n   - Fix endpoint registration if broken\n   - Ensure proper response formatting (no BOM)\n   - Add error handling and logging\n\n3. **Backend verification**\n   - Manual curl testing of endpoint\n   - Response format validation\n   - Error handling testing\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- [ ] `curl http://localhost:8001/api/activity/files` returns 200 OK with valid JSON\n- [ ] No BOM characters in response\n- [ ] Backend logs show proper request handling\n- [ ] Error handling gracefully returns appropriate status codes\n\n### Dependencies:\n- Backend server must be startable\n- Activity tracker database accessible\n- Python dependencies installed\n\n## Milestone 2: Frontend Integration & Testing\n**Duration**: 0.5 development cycles\n**Objective**: Verify frontend integration and complete end-to-end testing\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. **Frontend verification**\n   - Confirm API calls use correct URL\n   - Verify polling logic works correctly\n   - Test error handling in UI\n\n2. **Integration testing**\n   - End-to-end workflow testing\n   - File generation and display verification\n   - Cross-browser compatibility check\n\n3. **Documentation updates**\n   - API endpoint documentation\n   - Troubleshooting guide\n   - Known issues documentation\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- [ ] No 404 errors in browser console for `/api/activity/files`\n- [ ] Generated files appear correctly in UI\n- [ ] Graceful error handling when backend unavailable\n- [ ] All existing functionality preserved\n\n### Dependencies:\n- Milestone 1 completion\n- Frontend development environment\n- Test file generation capability\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n### High Risk:\n- Backend configuration issues preventing startup\n- Database connectivity problems\n\n### Medium Risk:\n- CORS configuration conflicts\n- Frontend polling logic issues\n\n### Low Risk:\n- Response format inconsistencies\n- Error message display problems\n\n## Rollback Plan\nIf issues arise:\n1. Revert backend changes to last working state\n2. Disable file polling temporarily in frontend\n3. Document known issues for future resolution\n\n## Success Metrics\n- Zero 404 errors on `/api/activity/files` endpoint\n- Files display correctly in UI within 2 seconds of generation\n- No regression in other API endpoints\n- Clean error logs without spam'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01PqVfhFj2iQRfxcUh2Edhxx', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_025845.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_025845.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01QjF8pM8mRWmL83B1uGQnPQ', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/ui_files_404_fix_requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'project_name': 'UI Files 404 Error Fix'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01QjF8pM8mRWmL83B1uGQnPQ', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01NoC2Be22GbWpVg5i1cW9JS', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/ui_files_404_fix_requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'UI Files 404 Error Fix'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01NoC2Be22GbWpVg5i1cW9JS', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "message": "Comprehensive architecture proposal created for resolving UI Files 404 Error, focusing on minimal changes to backend and frontend API handling", "key_decisions": ["Add explicit error handling in backend /api/activity/files endpoint", "Implement frontend API resilience with retry and error fallback", "Maintain existing tech stack and architecture", "Focus on fixing 404 issue without major refactoring"], "self_analysis": "The architecture proposal effectively addresses the 404 error issue by providing a targeted, low-risk solution that preserves the existing system architecture. By analyzing root causes and proposing minimal interventions, the design demonstrates a surgical approach to bug resolution."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FFMNcs7gXvdmDH5rYbdmi7', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FFMNcs7gXvdmDH5rYbdmi7', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble Agent System Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Core Design Philosophy\\n- **Observability First**: Enhance system transparency and reliability\\n- **Adaptive Intelligence**: Build self-improving mechanisms\\n- **Minimal Overhead**: Optimize performance while adding new capabilities\\n\\n### High-Level Architecture Pattern\\n- **Layered Microservices Architecture**\\n- **Event-Driven Communication**\\n- **Stateful Components with Checkpoint Recovery**\\n\\n## 2. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+\\n- **Framework**: FastAPI (async, high-performance)\\n- **Async Runtime**: asyncio\\n- **WebSocket**: Starlette WebSocket support\\n- **State Management**: Redis for distributed caching\\n- **Metrics**: Prometheus + Grafana\\n\\n### State & Messaging\\n- **Event Bus**: RabbitMQ (reliable, scalable messaging)\\n- **State Persistence**: Redis + Local Filesystem Checkpoints\\n- **Metrics Database**: InfluxDB (time-series performance tracking)\\n\\n### Frontend (Optional Monitoring Dashboard)\\n- **Framework**: Vue.js 3\\n- **State Management**: Vuex\\n- **Real-Time Updates**: Socket.IO\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### A. Progress Streaming Service\\n```\\n{\\n    \\"responsibility\\": \\"Real-time agent execution tracking\\",\\n    \\"features\\": [\\n        \\"Granular event emission\\",\\n        \\"WebSocket broadcast\\",\\n        \\"Low-latency updates (<500ms)\\"\\n    ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### B. Error Recovery Manager\\n```\\n{\\n    \\"responsibility\\": \\"Automatic failure detection and resume\\",\\n    \\"features\\": [\\n        \\"Exponential backoff retry\\",\\n        \\"Context preservation\\",\\n        \\"Error classification\\",\\n        \\"Checkpoint validation\\"\\n    ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### C. Agent Analytics Engine\\n```\\n{\\n    \\"responsibility\\": \\"Performance tracking and optimization\\",\\n    \\"features\\": [\\n        \\"Metrics collection\\",\\n        \\"Model performance comparison\\",\\n        \\"Adaptive model selection\\",\\n        \\"Cost optimization tracking\\"\\n    ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 4. Data Flow Diagram\\n\\n```\\nAgent Execution Flow:\\n[User Request] \\u2192 [Progress Streaming Service]\\n             \\u2193\\n    [Error Recovery Manager] \\u2190 [Checkpoint Store]\\n             \\u2193\\n    [Agent Analytics Engine] \\u2192 [Metrics Database]\\n             \\u2193\\n    [Final Result Delivery]\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Containerization\\n- **Docker Compose** for local development\\n- **Kubernetes** for production scaling\\n- **Helm Charts** for consistent deployment\\n\\n### CI/CD\\n- **GitHub Actions** for testing\\n- **Automated Deployment** to staging/production\\n- **Blue-Green Deployment** for zero-downtime updates\\n\\n## 6. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Testing\\n- **pytest** for backend\\n- **Coverage Target**: 95%\\n- **Mocking**: Extensive use of `unittest.mock`\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n- **Docker Compose** test environments\\n- **Chaos Testing**: Simulate failure scenarios\\n- **Performance Benchmarks**\\n\\n## 7. Security Considerations\\n- JWT Authentication\\n- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)\\n- Encrypted WebSocket connections\\n- Rate limiting on all endpoints\\n\\n## 8. Performance Optimization\\n\\n### Caching Strategies\\n- **L1 Cache**: In-memory (per-service)\\n- **L2 Cache**: Distributed Redis\\n- **Intelligent Eviction Policies**\\n\\n### Performance Targets\\n- **Latency**: <100ms for most operations\\n- **Throughput**: 100 concurrent agent executions\\n- **Resource Efficiency**: < 10% overhead from new features\\n\\n## 9. Scalability Plan\\n- Stateless service design\\n- Horizontal scaling via Kubernetes\\n- Dynamic resource allocation\\n- Circuit breaker patterns\\n\\n## 10. Open Questions & User Input Needed\\n1. Preferred monitoring dashboard design\\n2. Acceptable performance overhead threshold\\n3. Specific error recovery granularity\\n\\n## 11. Risks & Mitigations\\n\\n### Primary Risks\\n- **Increased Complexity**: Mitigated by clear component boundaries\\n- **Performance Overhead**: Extensive benchmarking\\n- **Token Cost Increase**: Adaptive model selection\\n\\n## 12. Migration Path\\n- **Phase 1**: Progress Streaming (Low Risk)\\n- **Phase 2**: Error Recovery (Medium Risk)\\n- **Phase 3**: Analytics Engine (Highest Risk)\\n\\n## Implementation Complexity\\n- **Estimated Development Time**: 8-12 days\\n- **Team Size Recommendation**: 2 senior engineers"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01BewSFB88Ey6hMk7PN7AEVV', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/backend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Root Cause Analysis & Backend Fix - Identify and fix the backend 404 issue for /api/activity/files endpoint', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/completed/ui_files_404_fix_requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01BewSFB88Ey6hMk7PN7AEVV', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "tasks_identified": 4, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md", "dependencies": ["Backend Health Check \\u2192 Debug Activity Tracker Endpoint", "Debug Activity Tracker Endpoint \\u2192 Frontend API Integration", "Backend Health Check \\u2192 CORS Configuration"], "message": "Completed task breakdown for resolving 404 errors in /api/activity/files endpoint, identifying 4 key tasks with clear dependencies and acceptance criteria"}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 81.5%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.3\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively executed the complete planning and implementation workflow for Milestone 1. Successfully coordinated with System Architect for architecture design, spawned all three Coordinators for com...\n- Successfully executed the complete Development Manager workflow from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Effectively managed the sequential process: milestone planning, architec...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
