{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 03:01:20", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-faa73833-707a-4d5f-a809-43e865115647', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Backend API Enhancement - Create and enhance backend endpoints to support project view functionality including detailed project endpoint, continue endpoint, SDLC phase determination logic, and integration with existing project_tracker.py module",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/project-view/milestone_plan.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_018v4RfoPHfPB9Kp952L64ma', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_018v4RfoPHfPB9Kp952L64ma', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Ensemble Agent Backend Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Core Design Philosophy\\n- Modular, event-driven backend architecture\\n- High observability and resilience\\n- Minimal performance overhead\\n- Seamless error recovery\\n\\n### High-Level Architecture Pattern\\n- Event-Driven Microservices\\n- CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) for metrics and state management\\n- Pub/Sub for real-time progress streaming\\n\\n## 2. Technology Stack\\n\\n### Core Technologies\\n- **Language**: Python 3.9+ (type hints, asyncio)\\n- **Async Framework**: `asyncio` + `uvloop` for high-performance concurrency\\n- **WebSocket**: `websockets` library\\n- **Event Bus**: `aio-pika` (AMQP-based message queue)\\n- **Metrics**: Prometheus + `prometheus_client`\\n- **Persistence**: SQLAlchemy with PostgreSQL\\n\\n### Rationale\\n- Python chosen for its strong async capabilities and rich AI/ML ecosystem\\n- `asyncio` provides efficient concurrent execution without heavy threading\\n- Prometheus offers robust metrics collection with minimal overhead\\n- PostgreSQL ensures strong consistency for state persistence\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### 1. AgentRuntime (Enhanced)\\n- Responsible for agent lifecycle management\\n- Emits granular progress events\\n- Handles automatic error recovery\\n- Coordinates state checkpointing\\n\\n### 2. StateManager\\n- Manages agent state persistence\\n- Implements checkpoint/resume functionality\\n- Supports partial state reconstruction\\n- Handles context preservation during retries\\n\\n### 3. ProgressEventBus\\n- Centralized event streaming mechanism\\n- Publishes real-time agent progress\\n- Supports WebSocket broadcasting\\n- Low-latency event routing\\n\\n### 4. AgentAnalytics\\n- Collects performance metrics\\n- Tracks token usage, success rates\\n- Provides adaptive model selection logic\\n- Generates performance reports\\n\\n### 5. ErrorRecoveryOrchestrator\\n- Classifies errors (retriable vs fatal)\\n- Manages retry strategies\\n- Implements exponential backoff\\n- Tracks error history for optimization\\n\\n## 4. Data Flow Diagram\\n\\n```\\nAgent Spawn Request\\n    \\u2193\\n[AgentRuntime]\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Start Execution\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Emit Progress Events \\u2192 [ProgressEventBus]\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Checkpoint State \\u2192 [StateManager]\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Track Metrics \\u2192 [AgentAnalytics]\\n        \\u2502\\n        \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 On Error \\u2192 [ErrorRecoveryOrchestrator]\\n        \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Retry Logic\\n        \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 State Resume\\n        \\u2502\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Performance Tracking\\n            \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Token Usage\\n            \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Success Rates\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Model Performance\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Key Implementation Details\\n\\n### Progress Streaming\\n- Use WebSocket for real-time updates\\n- Event types:\\n  - `agent_spawn`\\n  - `tool_invocation_start`\\n  - `tool_invocation_complete`\\n  - `agent_state_change`\\n  - `error_occurred`\\n\\n### Error Recovery Strategy\\n- Checkpoint every significant state transition\\n- Store:\\n  - Conversation history\\n  - Tool execution results\\n  - Spawned agent context\\n- Retry mechanism:\\n  1. Exponential backoff\\n  2. Maximum retry limit\\n  3. Fallback to manual intervention\\n\\n### Analytics Collection\\n- Metrics per agent:\\n  - Execution time\\n  - Token consumption\\n  - Success/failure rate\\n  - Model tier performance\\n- Aggregation levels:\\n  - Per agent instance\\n  - Per agent type\\n  - Across system\\n\\n## 6. Deployment Considerations\\n\\n### Container Strategy\\n- Docker containers for each component\\n- Docker Compose for local development\\n- Kubernetes for production scaling\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\n- Use `.env` files for configuration\\n- Support multiple environments:\\n  - Development\\n  - Staging\\n  - Production\\n\\n## 7. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Testing Approaches\\n- Unit Tests: `pytest`\\n- Integration Tests: `pytest-asyncio`\\n- Performance Tests: `locust`\\n- Coverage: `coverage.py`\\n\\n### Test Coverage Requirements\\n- 90%+ unit test coverage\\n- Integration tests for error recovery\\n- Chaos testing for resilience verification\\n\\n## 8. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Potential Risks\\n1. Performance Overhead from Metrics\\n   - **Mitigation**: Sampling, async metrics collection\\n2. WebSocket Connection Instability\\n   - **Mitigation**: Reconnection logic, connection pooling\\n3. State Persistence Complexity\\n   - **Mitigation**: Robust serialization, comprehensive testing\\n\\n## 9. Open Questions for User Review\\n\\n1. Preferred message queue technology (current proposal: AMQP)\\n2. Specific performance budget for metrics collection\\n3. Desired granularity of progress events\\n\\n## 10. Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Alternative 1: Synchronous Execution\\n- **Pros**: Simpler implementation\\n- **Cons**: Poor concurrency, blocking operations\\n- **Verdict**: Rejected in favor of async design\\n\\n### Alternative 2: Separate Metrics Service\\n- **Pros**: Clearer separation of concerns\\n- **Cons**: Additional complexity, network overhead\\n- **Verdict**: Current design integrated for performance\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a robust, performant backend for the ensemble agent system, focusing on real-time visibility, error resilience, and continuous improvement through comprehensive analytics."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01367smQK3XckpJe5kvkmWrx', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/output/project-view/milestone_plan.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01367smQK3XckpJe5kvkmWrx', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Project View Dashboard - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Project Name**: Project View Dashboard\\n**Description**: Add a dedicated Project View to the Ensemble UI that displays project status, SDLC position, milestone progress, next steps, and includes a \\"Continue to Next Step\\" button to advance implementation.\\n\\n## Milestones\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Backend API Enhancement\\n**Objective**: Create and enhance backend endpoints to support project view functionality\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Enhanced `/api/projects/{project_id}/details` endpoint for detailed project view\\n2. New `/api/projects/{project_id}/continue` endpoint to trigger project continuation\\n3. SDLC phase determination logic from project notes/status\\n4. Integration with existing project_tracker.py module\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- GET `/api/projects/{project_id}/details` returns complete project state including SDLC phase, milestones, tasks\\n- POST `/api/projects/{project_id}/continue` triggers a new Executive Director with appropriate context\\n- API handles missing/incomplete project data gracefully\\n- Endpoints respond within specified performance thresholds (<500ms for list, <1s for details)\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None (uses existing project_tracker.py)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Frontend Project View Components\\n**Objective**: Build React components for the Project View dashboard\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. ProjectView.jsx - Main container component with project list and details pane\\n2. ProjectStatusCard.jsx - Project header showing name, status, timestamps\\n3. SDLCIndicator.jsx - Visual SDLC phase progress indicator\\n4. MilestoneProgress.jsx - Milestone tracking with progress bar\\n5. NextStepsPanel.jsx - Actionable next steps display\\n6. Integration with App.jsx navigation (new \\"Projects\\" tab)\\n7. API service integration (api.js updates)\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Project list displays all projects with status badges\\n- Selected project shows detailed view with all required information\\n- SDLC indicator clearly shows current phase\\n- Milestone progress displays numerical counts and visual progress bar\\n- \\"Continue to Next Step\\" button triggers backend continuation endpoint\\n- UI follows existing dark theme and Bootstrap patterns\\n- Loading and error states handled appropriately\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (backend endpoints must be available)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Testing and Polish\\n**Objective**: Comprehensive testing and UI refinement\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n1. Backend unit tests for new endpoints\\n2. Frontend component tests (Jest/React Testing Library)\\n3. Integration testing for continue functionality\\n4. Error handling refinement\\n5. Loading state animations\\n6. Documentation\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- All new backend endpoints have unit test coverage\\n- Frontend components render correctly in tests\\n- Continue functionality works end-to-end\\n- Error states display user-friendly messages\\n- Documentation updated for new endpoints\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1 and 2\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Technical Decisions Made\\n\\n### Architecture Decisions\\n1. **SDLC Phase Tracking**: Will infer SDLC phase from project notes by scanning for phase-related keywords (requirements, architecture, planning, implementation, testing). This is pragmatic given current data.\\n\\n2. **Milestone Data Source**: Will use project tracker tasks and notes to infer milestones. Tasks tagged as milestones or notes with category \\"milestone\\" will be used.\\n\\n3. **Continue Functionality**: Will spawn a new Executive Director agent with the project context, instructing it to continue to the next phase/milestone.\\n\\n4. **Component Structure**: Single ProjectView.jsx as main container with sub-components for modularity, following existing patterns like SelfImprovementDashboard.\\n\\n### Technical Stack (Following Existing Patterns)\\n- Backend: FastAPI (Python) with existing project_tracker integration\\n- Frontend: React with Bootstrap components\\n- State: Local React state (following App.jsx pattern)\\n- Styling: Inline styles with existing dark theme colors\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n1. **SDLC Phase Detection**: If project notes don\'t contain phase information, default to \\"unknown\\" with graceful UI handling\\n2. **Milestone Data**: If no milestone data exists, show \\"No milestones defined\\" rather than empty state\\n3. **Continue Action**: Include confirmation dialog and proper error handling for failed continuation attempts\\n\\n## Estimated Scope\\n- **Milestone 1**: ~200-300 lines backend code\\n- **Milestone 2**: ~500-700 lines frontend code (5 components + api changes)\\n- **Milestone 3**: ~200-300 lines test code + documentation\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01AECoN95NXPyGaXj7R6daF4', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Backend Tasks - Backend API Enhancement (Milestone 1)\n\n## Overview\nThis milestone focuses on creating and enhancing backend endpoints to support project view functionality. The tasks will integrate with the existing project_tracker.py module and follow the event-driven architecture patterns outlined in the architecture document.\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Task 1: SDLC Phase Detection Service\n**Description**: Create a service to analyze project notes and determine SDLC phase\n**Priority**: High (Foundation for other tasks)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n**Implementation Details**:\n- Create `services/sdlc_analyzer.py` module\n- Implement keyword-based phase detection logic\n- Map project notes to SDLC phases: requirements, architecture, planning, implementation, testing\n- Handle edge cases (no notes, ambiguous phase, multiple phases)\n- Return structured phase information with confidence level\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Can determine SDLC phase from project notes with keyword matching\n- Returns phase enum (requirements|architecture|planning|implementation|testing|unknown)\n- Includes confidence score and reasoning\n- Handles missing or empty project notes gracefully\n- Unit tests covering all phase detection scenarios\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Files to Create/Modify**: \n- `services/sdlc_analyzer.py` (new)\n- `models/sdlc_models.py` (new)\n\n---\n\n### Task 2: Milestone Progress Calculator\n**Description**: Create service to calculate milestone progress from project tracker data\n**Priority**: High (Foundation for project details endpoint)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n**Implementation Details**:\n- Create `services/milestone_calculator.py` module\n- Extract milestone information from project tasks and notes\n- Calculate completion percentages based on task status\n- Identify next actionable steps from incomplete milestones\n- Handle cases where no milestone data exists\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Extracts milestones from project tracker tasks with milestone tags\n- Calculates accurate completion percentages\n- Identifies next steps from incomplete tasks\n- Returns structured milestone data with progress metrics\n- Handles projects without defined milestones\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Files to Create/Modify**:\n- `services/milestone_calculator.py` (new)\n- `models/milestone_models.py` (new)\n\n---\n\n### Task 3: Enhanced Project Details Endpoint\n**Description**: Enhance GET `/api/projects/{project_id}/details` endpoint with comprehensive project data\n**Priority**: High (Core functionality)\n**Complexity**: Complex\n\n**Implementation Details**:\n- Extend existing project details endpoint in FastAPI\n- Integrate SDLC phase detection service\n- Integrate milestone progress calculation\n- Include project metadata (name, description, timestamps)\n- Add task summary and next steps\n- Implement proper error handling and validation\n- Add OpenAPI documentation\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Returns complete project state including SDLC phase and confidence\n- Includes milestone progress with completion percentages\n- Shows task counts by status (todo, in_progress, completed)\n- Lists next actionable steps\n- Responds within 1 second for typical project sizes\n- Handles non-existent project IDs with 404\n- Returns proper HTTP status codes and error messages\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 2\n**Files to Create/Modify**:\n- `routers/projects.py` (modify existing)\n- `schemas/project_schemas.py` (extend existing)\n\n---\n\n### Task 4: Project Continuation Endpoint\n**Description**: Create POST `/api/projects/{project_id}/continue` endpoint to trigger project advancement\n**Priority**: High (Core functionality)\n**Complexity**: Complex\n\n**Implementation Details**:\n- Create new endpoint to handle project continuation requests\n- Determine appropriate next action based on current SDLC phase\n- Spawn Executive Director agent with project context\n- Include project history and current status in agent context\n- Implement async task creation and status tracking\n- Add proper authentication and authorization\n- Handle concurrent continuation attempts\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Successfully spawns Executive Director with project context\n- Includes current project state, SDLC phase, and next recommended actions\n- Returns task/agent ID for tracking continuation progress\n- Prevents multiple simultaneous continuations of same project\n- Validates project exists and is in continuable state\n- Responds within 500ms (async operation)\n- Proper error handling for agent spawn failures\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 3\n**Files to Create/Modify**:\n- `routers/projects.py` (modify existing)\n- `services/project_continuation.py` (new)\n- `schemas/continuation_schemas.py` (new)\n\n---\n\n### Task 5: Project Tracker Integration Enhancement\n**Description**: Enhance integration with existing project_tracker.py module for better data access\n**Priority**: Medium (Optimization)\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Implementation Details**:\n- Add helper methods to project_tracker.py for batch operations\n- Create data access layer for efficient project querying\n- Add caching for frequently accessed project data\n- Optimize database queries for project lists and details\n- Add filtering and sorting capabilities\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Batch loading of multiple projects for list views\n- Efficient single project loading with related data\n- Basic caching layer to reduce database hits\n- Support for filtering projects by status/phase\n- Maintains backward compatibility with existing code\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n**Files to Create/Modify**:\n- `project_tracker.py` (modify existing)\n- `services/project_data_layer.py` (new)\n\n---\n\n### Task 6: API Error Handling and Validation\n**Description**: Implement comprehensive error handling and input validation for new endpoints\n**Priority**: Medium (Quality)\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Implementation Details**:\n- Add Pydantic models for request/response validation\n- Implement custom exception classes for project-specific errors\n- Add error handling middleware for consistent error responses\n- Create error response schemas with detailed messages\n- Add request logging for debugging\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- All endpoints validate input using Pydantic models\n- Consistent error response format across all endpoints\n- Appropriate HTTP status codes for different error types\n- Clear error messages for client debugging\n- Request/response logging for monitoring\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 3, Task 4\n**Files to Create/Modify**:\n- `exceptions/project_exceptions.py` (new)\n- `middleware/error_handling.py` (modify existing)\n- `schemas/error_schemas.py` (new)\n\n---\n\n### Task 7: Performance Optimization and Monitoring\n**Description**: Add performance monitoring and optimization for project endpoints\n**Priority**: Low (Enhancement)\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Implementation Details**:\n- Add endpoint timing metrics with Prometheus\n- Implement query optimization for large projects\n- Add database connection pooling configuration\n- Create performance benchmarks for endpoint response times\n- Add health check endpoints\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Endpoint response times tracked in metrics\n- Database queries optimized for performance\n- Response times meet requirements (<500ms list, <1s details)\n- Health check endpoints return system status\n- Performance metrics exportable to monitoring systems\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 3, Task 4, Task 5\n**Files to Create/Modify**:\n- `monitoring/metrics.py` (modify existing)\n- `routers/health.py` (new)\n- `database/optimization.py` (new)\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n### Phase 1: Foundation (Parallel Development Possible)\n1. Task 1: SDLC Phase Detection Service\n2. Task 2: Milestone Progress Calculator\n5. Task 5: Project Tracker Integration Enhancement\n\n### Phase 2: Core Endpoints (Sequential)\n3. Task 3: Enhanced Project Details Endpoint\n4. Task 4: Project Continuation Endpoint\n\n### Phase 3: Quality and Performance (Parallel)\n6. Task 6: API Error Handling and Validation\n7. Task 7: Performance Optimization and Monitoring\n\n## Technical Specifications\n\n### Database Schema Updates\n- No new tables required (uses existing project_tracker schema)\n- May add indices for performance optimization\n\n### API Response Format\n```json\n{\n  "project_id": "string",\n  "name": "string", \n  "description": "string",\n  "created_at": "datetime",\n  "updated_at": "datetime",\n  "sdlc_phase": {\n    "current_phase": "requirements|architecture|planning|implementation|testing|unknown",\n    "confidence": 0.85,\n    "reasoning": "Found architecture document and design discussions"\n  },\n  "milestones": [\n    {\n      "name": "string",\n      "description": "string",\n      "completion_percentage": 75,\n      "tasks_completed": 3,\n      "tasks_total": 4,\n      "status": "in_progress|completed|todo"\n    }\n  ],\n  "task_summary": {\n    "todo": 5,\n    "in_progress": 2,\n    "completed": 12,\n    "blocked": 1\n  },\n  "next_steps": ["Complete API documentation", "Review security requirements"]\n}\n```\n\n### Technology Stack Alignment\n- **FastAPI**: REST API with automatic OpenAPI documentation\n- **SQLAlchemy**: ORM for database operations with existing project_tracker integration\n- **Pydantic**: Data validation and serialization\n- **Prometheus**: Metrics collection for monitoring\n- **pytest**: Unit and integration testing\n\n## Estimated Effort\n- **Total Backend Code**: ~250-350 lines\n- **Total Test Code**: ~400-500 lines\n- **Development Time**: 3-4 days for experienced FastAPI developer\n- **Testing Time**: 1-2 days\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n- **SDLC Phase Detection**: Graceful degradation with "unknown" phase if detection fails\n- **Missing Milestone Data**: Default to task-based progress if no milestones defined  \n- **Agent Spawn Failures**: Proper error handling and user feedback for continuation endpoint\n- **Performance**: Database query optimization and caching for large projects'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01AECoN95NXPyGaXj7R6daF4', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260116_030120.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260116_030120.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Backend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks backend milestones into specific API, database, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify backend components, endpoints, data models, and business logic. Coordinates backend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break backend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Backend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**API Style**: REST with JSON, OpenAPI docs\n**Framework**: FastAPI (Python) or Express (Node.js)\n**Database**: PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy/Prisma ORM\n**Auth**: JWT tokens, bcrypt password hashing\n**Validation**: Pydantic (Python) or Joi (Node.js)\n**Testing**: pytest or Jest with coverage\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all backend components:\n  * API endpoints (REST, GraphQL)\n  * Database models/schemas\n  * Business logic services\n  * Authentication/authorization\n  * Background jobs/workers\n  * External API integrations\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (how to know it\'s done)\nDependencies (what must be done first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by Priority**\nGroup related tasks together\nOrder by dependencies (foundational → features)\nIdentify critical path tasks\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Backend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Business logic is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "calculate shipping" without formula)\n- **Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., sync vs async processing)\n- **Data relationships are contradictory** (e.g., conflicting schema requirements)\n- **Security/compliance requirements are ambiguous** (e.g., PII handling rules)\n- **NOT for**: standard tech choices, common patterns, typical implementations\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All backend tasks identified and documented\n- Task dependencies mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
